export const QUESTION_PACK_ID = "core-v1"
export const QUESTION_PACK_JSON = "[{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A trapezoid has parallel sides of lengths 10 centimeters and 16 centimeters, and the perpendicular distance between those two sides is 6 centimeters. What is the area, in square centimeters, of the trapezoid?\",\"option_a\":\"60\",\"option_b\":\"78\",\"option_c\":\"96\",\"option_d\":\"156\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The area of a trapezoid is $A = \\\\frac{1}{2}(b_1 + b_2)h$. Here $A = \\\\frac{1}{2}(10 + 16)(6) = \\\\frac{1}{2}(26)(6) = 78$ square centimeters, so choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoice A (60) uses only the shorter base: $10 \\\\cdot 6$. Choice C (96) uses only the longer base: $16 \\\\cdot 6$. Choice D (156) is $(10 + 16)(6)$; it forgets to multiply by $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Trapetsiyaning yuzasi $A = \\\\frac{1}{2}(b_1 + b_2)h$ formula bilan topiladi. Bu yerda $A = \\\\frac{1}{2}(10 + 16)(6) = \\\\frac{1}{2}(26)(6) = 78$ kvadrat santimetr, demak to‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA (60) — faqat qisqa asos olingan: $10 \\\\cdot 6$. C (96) — faqat uzun asos olingan: $16 \\\\cdot 6$. D (156) — bu $(10 + 16)(6)$, ya’ni $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ ga ko‘paytirish unutilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A wooden cube has an edge length of 7 inches. What is the total surface area, in square inches, of the cube?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"294\"],\"explanation_en\":\"A cube has 6 congruent square faces. Each face has area $7^2 = 49$ square inches, so the total surface area is $6 \\\\cdot 49 = 294$ square inches.\\n\\nCommon mistakes: $7^3 = 343$ is the volume, not the surface area, and $4 \\\\cdot 49 = 196$ counts only 4 of the 6 faces.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kubning 6 ta bir xil kvadrat yog‘i bor. Har bir yoqning yuzasi $7^2 = 49$ kvadrat dyuym, shuning uchun to‘liq sirt yuzasi $6 \\\\cdot 49 = 294$ kvadrat dyuym.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xatolar: $7^3 = 343$ — bu sirt yuzasi emas, hajm; $4 \\\\cdot 49 = 196$ esa 6 ta yoqdan faqat 4 tasini hisobga oladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A right circular cylinder has a radius of 4 meters and a height of 10 meters. What is the volume, in cubic meters, of the cylinder?\",\"option_a\":\"$40\\\\pi$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{160}{3}\\\\pi$\",\"option_c\":\"$80\\\\pi$\",\"option_d\":\"$160\\\\pi$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The volume of a cylinder is $V = \\\\pi r^2 h = \\\\pi (4)^2 (10) = 160\\\\pi$ cubic meters, so choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($40\\\\pi$) is $\\\\pi r h$; the radius is not squared. Choice B ($\\\\frac{160}{3}\\\\pi$) uses the cone formula $\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi r^2 h$, but this solid is a cylinder. Choice C ($80\\\\pi$) is $2\\\\pi r h$, the lateral (side) surface area, not the volume.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Silindrning hajmi $V = \\\\pi r^2 h = \\\\pi (4)^2 (10) = 160\\\\pi$ kub metr, demak to‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA ($40\\\\pi$) — bu $\\\\pi r h$, radius kvadratga oshirilmagan. B ($\\\\frac{160}{3}\\\\pi$) — konus formulasi $\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi r^2 h$ ishlatilgan, lekin bu jism silindr. C ($80\\\\pi$) — bu $2\\\\pi r h$, ya’ni yon sirt yuzasi, hajm emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A rectangular swimming pool is 25 meters long and 10 meters wide. A concrete walkway of uniform width 2 meters surrounds the pool on all four sides. What is the area, in square meters, of the walkway alone?\",\"option_a\":\"74\",\"option_b\":\"140\",\"option_c\":\"156\",\"option_d\":\"406\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The pool and the walkway together form a rectangle that is $25 + 2 + 2 = 29$ meters long and $10 + 2 + 2 = 14$ meters wide, with area $29 \\\\cdot 14 = 406$ square meters. Subtracting the pool's area, $25 \\\\cdot 10 = 250$, leaves $406 - 250 = 156$ square meters for the walkway. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A (74) adds the walkway width on only one side in each direction: $27 \\\\cdot 12 - 250$. Choice B (140) multiplies the pool's perimeter, 70, by the width 2 and misses the four corner squares ($4 \\\\cdot 2^2 = 16$). Choice D (406) is the area of the pool and the walkway together.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Hovuz va yo‘lak birgalikda uzunligi $25 + 2 + 2 = 29$ metr, eni $10 + 2 + 2 = 14$ metr bo‘lgan to‘g‘ri to‘rtburchak hosil qiladi; uning yuzasi $29 \\\\cdot 14 = 406$ kvadrat metr. Hovuz yuzasini ($25 \\\\cdot 10 = 250$) ayirsak, yo‘lak uchun $406 - 250 = 156$ kvadrat metr qoladi. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA (74) — yo‘lak kengligi har bir yo‘nalishda faqat bir tomonga qo‘shilgan: $27 \\\\cdot 12 - 250$. B (140) — hovuz perimetri (70) yo‘lak kengligiga (2) ko‘paytirilgan, ammo burchaklardagi to‘rtta kvadrat ($4 \\\\cdot 2^2 = 16$) tushib qolgan. D (406) — hovuz va yo‘lakning umumiy yuzasi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A sphere has a volume of $288\\\\pi$ cubic centimeters. What is the diameter, in centimeters, of the sphere?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"12\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Use $V = \\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\pi r^3$: $\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\pi r^3 = 288\\\\pi$, so $r^3 = 288 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{3}{4} = 216$ and $r = 6$. The diameter is $2r = 12$ centimeters.\\n\\nWatch out: 6 is the radius, not the diameter, and 216 is the value of $r^3$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$V = \\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\pi r^3$ formulasidan foydalanamiz: $\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\pi r^3 = 288\\\\pi$, demak $r^3 = 288 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{3}{4} = 216$ va $r = 6$. Diametr $2r = 12$ santimetr.\\n\\nE’tibor bering: 6 — bu radius, diametr emas; 216 esa $r^3$ ning qiymati.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Rectangular prism $Q$ is a scaled copy of rectangular prism $P$: each edge of prism $Q$ is 3 times as long as the corresponding edge of prism $P$. The volume of prism $Q$ is 1,080 cubic centimeters. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of prism $P$?\",\"option_a\":\"40\",\"option_b\":\"120\",\"option_c\":\"360\",\"option_d\":\"3,240\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"When every length of a solid is multiplied by $k$, its volume is multiplied by $k^3$. Going from $P$ to $Q$, $k = 3$, so the volume of $Q$ is $3^3 = 27$ times the volume of $P$. The volume of $P$ is $\\\\frac{1{,}080}{27} = 40$ cubic centimeters, so choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B (120) divides by $3^2 = 9$, the factor for areas, not volumes. Choice C (360) divides by 3, the factor for lengths. Choice D (3,240) multiplies by 3 instead of dividing, but $P$ is the smaller prism.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Jismning barcha uzunliklari $k$ marta oshirilsa, hajmi $k^3$ marta oshadi. $P$ dan $Q$ ga o‘tishda $k = 3$, demak $Q$ ning hajmi $P$ nikidan $3^3 = 27$ marta katta. $P$ ning hajmi $\\\\frac{1{,}080}{27} = 40$ kub santimetr, to‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB (120) — $3^2 = 9$ ga bo‘lingan, bu hajm emas, yuza uchun koeffitsiyent. C (360) — 3 ga bo‘lingan, bu uzunliklar uchun koeffitsiyent. D (3,240) — bo‘lish o‘rniga 3 ga ko‘paytirilgan, holbuki $P$ kichikroq prizma.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A closed right circular cylinder has a height that is twice its radius. The volume of the cylinder is $128\\\\pi$ cubic centimeters. What is the total surface area, in square centimeters, of the cylinder?\",\"option_a\":\"$32\\\\pi$\",\"option_b\":\"$64\\\\pi$\",\"option_c\":\"$80\\\\pi$\",\"option_d\":\"$96\\\\pi$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let the radius be $r$, so the height is $2r$. Then $V = \\\\pi r^2 (2r) = 2\\\\pi r^3 = 128\\\\pi$, so $r^3 = 64$ and $r = 4$; the height is 8. A closed cylinder has two circular bases and a lateral surface: $SA = 2\\\\pi r^2 + 2\\\\pi r h = 2\\\\pi(16) + 2\\\\pi(4)(8) = 32\\\\pi + 64\\\\pi = 96\\\\pi$. Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($32\\\\pi$) counts only the two bases. Choice B ($64\\\\pi$) is only the lateral area. Choice C ($80\\\\pi$) includes just one base, as for an open cylinder, but this cylinder is closed.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Radiusni $r$ deb olamiz, u holda balandlik $2r$. $V = \\\\pi r^2 (2r) = 2\\\\pi r^3 = 128\\\\pi$, demak $r^3 = 64$ va $r = 4$; balandlik 8 ga teng. Yopiq silindrning ikkita doira asosi va yon sirti bor: $SA = 2\\\\pi r^2 + 2\\\\pi r h = 2\\\\pi(16) + 2\\\\pi(4)(8) = 32\\\\pi + 64\\\\pi = 96\\\\pi$. To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA ($32\\\\pi$) — faqat ikki asos hisoblangan. B ($64\\\\pi$) — faqat yon sirt yuzasi. C ($80\\\\pi$) — ochiq silindrdagidek bitta asos olingan, lekin silindr yopiq.\",\"estimated_seconds\":125,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A right circular cone with a radius of 6 centimeters and a height of 10 centimeters is completely filled with water. All of the water is poured into an empty right circular cylinder with a radius of 4 centimeters, and none spills. What is the height, in centimeters, of the water in the cylinder?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"7.5\",\"15/2\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The cone holds $\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi r^2 h = \\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi (6)^2 (10) = 120\\\\pi$ cubic centimeters of water. In the cylinder, the water forms a cylinder with radius 4 and unknown height $h$, so its volume is $\\\\pi (4)^2 h = 16\\\\pi h$. Setting $16\\\\pi h = 120\\\\pi$ gives $h = 7.5$ centimeters. Either 7.5 or 15/2 is accepted.\\n\\nIf you forget the $\\\\frac{1}{3}$ in the cone formula, you get $\\\\frac{360\\\\pi}{16\\\\pi} = 22.5$, which is incorrect.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Konusdagi suv hajmi $\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi r^2 h = \\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi (6)^2 (10) = 120\\\\pi$ kub santimetr. Silindrda suv radiusi 4 va balandligi $h$ bo‘lgan silindr shaklini oladi, uning hajmi $\\\\pi (4)^2 h = 16\\\\pi h$. $16\\\\pi h = 120\\\\pi$ tenglamasidan $h = 7.5$ santimetr chiqadi. 7.5 yoki 15/2 javoblari qabul qilinadi.\\n\\nKonus formulasidagi $\\\\frac{1}{3}$ unutilsa, $\\\\frac{360\\\\pi}{16\\\\pi} = 22.5$ chiqadi — bu xato javob.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In 1960 the Aral Sea covered more than 60,000 square ______ the early 2000s, its surface area had shrunk to a fraction of that size, leaving behind a vast plain of salty sand where fishing boats once sailed.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"kilometers, by\",\"option_b\":\"kilometers by\",\"option_c\":\"kilometers; by\",\"option_d\":\"kilometers by,\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text contains two independent clauses: “In 1960 the Aral Sea covered more than 60,000 square kilometers” and “by the early 2000s, its surface area had shrunk to a fraction of that size….” A semicolon can join two independent clauses, so choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A joins the two clauses with only a comma, which creates a comma splice. Choice B uses no punctuation at all, which creates a run-on sentence. Choice D puts the comma after “by,” which splits the phrase “by the early 2000s” and still leaves the two clauses fused together.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda ikkita mustaqil gap (independent clause) bor: “In 1960 the Aral Sea covered more than 60,000 square kilometers” va “by the early 2000s, its surface area had shrunk to a fraction of that size…”. Ikki mustaqil gapni nuqtali vergul (;) bilan bog‘lash mumkin, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA — ikki gap faqat vergul bilan ulangan, bu comma splice xatosi. B — hech qanday tinish belgisi yo‘q, gaplar bir-biriga qo‘shilib ketgan (run-on). D — vergul “by” so‘zidan keyin qo‘yilgan: u “by the early 2000s” iborasini bo‘lib yuboradi, ikki gap esa baribir ajratilmay qoladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The Registan, a public square in the center of ______ is framed by three grand madrasas that were built between the fifteenth and seventeenth centuries and decorated with glazed tiles in shades of blue, green, and gold.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"Samarkand,\",\"option_b\":\"Samarkand\",\"option_c\":\"Samarkand;\",\"option_d\":\"Samarkand—\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The phrase “a public square in the center of Samarkand” is a nonessential appositive: it describes the Registan but could be removed without breaking the sentence. It opens with a comma after “Registan,” so it must close with a matching comma before the verb “is.” Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B leaves the appositive unclosed, so the sentence seems to say that “Samarkand is framed” by the madrasas. Choice C uses a semicolon, which cannot separate a subject from its verb. Choice D closes with a dash, but an element that opens with a comma must close with a comma.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“a public square in the center of Samarkand” — bu qo‘shimcha izoh (nonessential appositive): u Registonni tasvirlaydi, lekin olib tashlansa ham gap buzilmaydi. Izoh “Registan” so‘zidan keyingi vergul bilan boshlangan, shuning uchun “is” kesimidan oldin xuddi shunday vergul bilan yopilishi kerak. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB — izoh yopilmagan, natijada gap “Samarkand is framed” degan ma’noni beradi. C — nuqtali vergul ega (subject) va kesimni (verb) ajrata olmaydi. D — izoh tire bilan yopilgan, lekin vergul bilan boshlangan izoh vergul bilan yopilishi shart.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The glazed tiles that cover the domes and minarets of many historic buildings in ______ their brilliant blue and turquoise colors from cobalt and copper compounds that artisans mix into the glaze before the tiles are fired in a kiln.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"Bukhara: get\",\"option_b\":\"Bukhara get\",\"option_c\":\"Bukhara, get\",\"option_d\":\"Bukhara; get\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The subject of this sentence is the long noun phrase “The glazed tiles that cover the domes and minarets of many historic buildings in Bukhara,” and its main verb is “get.” No punctuation should separate a subject from its verb, so choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoices A, C, and D each insert a punctuation mark (a colon, a comma, or a semicolon) between the subject and its verb, which incorrectly breaks up the main clause. The length of the subject does not change this rule.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bu gapning egasi — uzun ot birikmasi: “The glazed tiles that cover the domes and minarets of many historic buildings in Bukhara”, kesimi esa “get”. Ega va kesim orasiga hech qanday tinish belgisi qo‘yilmaydi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA, C va D variantlarda ega bilan kesim orasiga tinish belgisi (ikki nuqta, vergul yoki nuqtali vergul) qo‘yilgan, bu esa bosh gapni noto‘g‘ri bo‘lib yuboradi. Ega qanchalik uzun bo‘lmasin, bu qoida o‘zgarmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"To qualify for the final round of the regional robotics contest, each team's machine had to complete two ______ climbing a steep wooden ramp and lifting a small box onto a shelf without dropping it.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"tasks;\",\"option_b\":\"tasks.\",\"option_c\":\"tasks\",\"option_d\":\"tasks:\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The words before the blank, “each team's machine had to complete two tasks,” form a complete independent clause, and the words after it name those two tasks. A colon is used after an independent clause to introduce a list or an explanation, so choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A uses a semicolon, but a semicolon must be followed by another independent clause, and “climbing a steep wooden ramp and lifting a small box onto a shelf” is not one. Choice B leaves that same phrase as a sentence fragment. Choice C runs “tasks” directly into the list with no punctuation.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bo‘sh joydan oldingi qism — “each team’s machine had to complete two tasks” — to‘liq mustaqil gap, undan keyingi so‘zlar esa o‘sha ikki vazifani sanab beradi. Mustaqil gapdan keyin ro‘yxat yoki izohni kiritish uchun ikki nuqta (:) ishlatiladi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA — nuqtali verguldan keyin yana mustaqil gap kelishi kerak, “climbing a steep wooden ramp and lifting a small box onto a shelf” esa mustaqil gap emas. B — nuqta qo‘yilsa, o‘sha ibora to‘liq bo‘lmagan gap (fragment) bo‘lib qoladi. C — “tasks” so‘zi hech qanday belgisiz ro‘yxatga qo‘shilib ketgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Engineers expected the new rooftop solar panels to lose much of their efficiency during the city's dusty summer ______ the panels' special coating shed most of the dust, and their power output stayed nearly constant from June through August.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"months; however,\",\"option_b\":\"months, however,\",\"option_c\":\"months; however\",\"option_d\":\"months however,\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text contains two independent clauses, and “however” is a conjunctive adverb that begins the second one. The first clause must end with a semicolon (or a period), and “however” must be followed by a comma. Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B joins the two independent clauses with only a comma, which creates a comma splice. Choice C omits the comma after “however.” Choice D has no punctuation before “however,” so the two clauses are fused.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda ikkita mustaqil gap bor, “however” esa ikkinchi gapni boshlovchi bog‘lovchi ravish (conjunctive adverb). Birinchi gap nuqtali vergul (yoki nuqta) bilan tugashi, “however” dan keyin esa vergul qo‘yilishi kerak. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB — ikki mustaqil gap faqat vergul bilan ulangan (comma splice). C — “however” dan keyingi vergul tushib qolgan. D — “however” dan oldin hech qanday belgi yo‘q, natijada ikki gap qo‘shilib ketgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Because the meltwater flowing into the mountain lake carries tiny particles of finely ground ______ the water often looks like an opaque, milky turquoise rather than the clear blue that visitors expect.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"rock;\",\"option_b\":\"rock.\",\"option_c\":\"rock,\",\"option_d\":\"rock:\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"“Because the meltwater flowing into the mountain lake carries tiny particles of finely ground rock” is a dependent clause: it begins with the subordinating conjunction “because” and cannot stand alone. When a dependent clause comes before the main clause, a comma separates the two, so choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoices A (semicolon) and B (period) belong between independent clauses; here they would leave the “because” clause as a fragment. Choice D is also incorrect, because a colon must follow an independent clause, and the “because” clause is not one.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“Because the meltwater flowing into the mountain lake carries tiny particles of finely ground rock” — bu ergash gap (dependent clause): u “because” bog‘lovchisi bilan boshlanadi va mustaqil gap bo‘la olmaydi. Ergash gap bosh gapdan oldin kelsa, ular vergul bilan ajratiladi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA (nuqtali vergul) va B (nuqta) mustaqil gaplar orasida ishlatiladi; bu yerda ular “because” bilan boshlangan qismni to‘liq bo‘lmagan gapga (fragment) aylantiradi. D ham xato, chunki ikki nuqtadan oldin mustaqil gap turishi kerak, “because” bilan boshlangan qism esa mustaqil gap emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The carpet—knotted by hand from wool that had been colored with natural dyes made from pomegranate rind, walnut husks, and ______ took a family of weavers in the Fergana Valley nearly two years to finish.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"madder root,\",\"option_b\":\"madder root—\",\"option_c\":\"madder root;\",\"option_d\":\"madder root\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The words between “The carpet” and “took” form a nonessential element that describes the carpet. This element opens with a dash after “The carpet,” so it must close with a matching dash, which choice B provides. The main clause then reads smoothly without the interruption: “The carpet … took a family of weavers in the Fergana Valley nearly two years to finish.”\\n\\nChoice A closes the element with a comma; the commas inside the list make this tempting, but an element that opens with a dash must close with a dash. Choice C's semicolon would separate the subject “The carpet” from its verb “took.” Choice D leaves the element unclosed, so the list runs straight into the main verb.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“The carpet” va “took” orasidagi so‘zlar gilamni tasvirlovchi qo‘shimcha izoh (nonessential element). Bu izoh “The carpet” dan keyingi tire bilan boshlangan, demak u xuddi shunday tire bilan yopilishi kerak — buni B varianti beradi. Shunda bosh gap uzilmasdan o‘qiladi: “The carpet … took a family of weavers in the Fergana Valley nearly two years to finish.”\\n\\nA — izoh vergul bilan yopilgan; ro‘yxat ichidagi vergullar bu variantni jozibali qiladi, lekin tire bilan boshlangan izoh tire bilan yopilishi shart. C — nuqtali vergul “The carpet” egasini “took” kesimidan ajratib qo‘yadi. D — izoh yopilmagan, ro‘yxat to‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri kesimga qo‘shilib ketadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The field team that spent the summer studying glaciers in the Pamir Mountains included Dilnoza Karimova, a glaciologist from Tashkent; Javier Ruiz, a geochemist from ______ and Mei Lin, a photographer from Taipei.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"Seville,\",\"option_b\":\"Seville:\",\"option_c\":\"Seville\",\"option_d\":\"Seville;\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"This sentence lists three people, and each item already contains a comma (for example, “Dilnoza Karimova, a glaciologist from Tashkent”). When the items in a list contain internal commas, semicolons separate the items so that readers can tell where each one ends. The first two items are already separated by a semicolon, so a semicolon must also follow “Seville.” Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A uses a comma, which makes the list inconsistent and makes it unclear whether “Mei Lin” is a separate person or a description of Javier Ruiz. Choice B's colon would wrongly signal that what follows explains the previous item. Choice C omits the separator entirely.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bu gapda uch kishi sanab o‘tilgan va har bir bandning ichida allaqachon vergul bor (masalan, “Dilnoza Karimova, a glaciologist from Tashkent”). Ro‘yxat bandlari ichida vergul bo‘lsa, bandlar bir-biridan nuqtali vergul bilan ajratiladi — shunda o‘quvchi har bir band qayerda tugashini tushunadi. Birinchi ikki band nuqtali vergul bilan ajratilgan, demak “Seville” dan keyin ham nuqtali vergul kerak. To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA — vergul ro‘yxatni nomuvofiq qiladi va “Mei Lin” alohida shaxsmi yoki Javier Ruizning tavsifimi, tushunarsiz bo‘lib qoladi. B — ikki nuqta keyingi qism oldingi bandni izohlaydi degan noto‘g‘ri ishora beradi. C — ajratuvchi belgi umuman yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"For years, the small fishing town of Port Ellery struggled as catches declined and young people moved away to find work. In 2015, a group of residents turned an empty fish cannery into a workshop where local fishers teach visitors to mend nets, smoke fish and build wooden boats. The workshop now draws thousands of visitors each summer, and several young people who had left the town have returned to work there as instructors.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"A project built on Port Ellery's fishing traditions has helped revive the town.\",\"option_b\":\"Fish catches near Port Ellery increased after the workshop opened.\",\"option_c\":\"Most visitors to Port Ellery hope to become professional fishers.\",\"option_d\":\"Young people left Port Ellery mainly because the cannery closed.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text describes a struggling town, a workshop that teaches traditional fishing skills, and the results: thousands of visitors and young people returning. Choice A sums up this whole story. Choice B is unsupported: the text never says that catches increased. Choice C is unsupported: the text says visitors learn fishing skills, not that they want to become fishers. Choice D is wrong because the text says young people left to find work as catches declined; it does not say the cannery's closing was the main reason.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda qiyin ahvoldagi shaharcha, an’anaviy baliqchilik ko‘nikmalarini o‘rgatadigan ustaxona va natijalar — minglab mehmonlar hamda qaytib kelgan yoshlar tasvirlanadi. A javob butun voqeani umumlashtiradi. B asossiz: matnda baliq ovi ko‘paygani aytilmagan. C asossiz: matnda mehmonlar baliqchilik ko‘nikmalarini o‘rganishi aytiladi, ular professional baliqchi bo‘lishni xohlashi emas. D noto‘g‘ri: matnga ko‘ra yoshlar baliq ovi kamaygach ish qidirib ketgan; konserva zavodining yopilishi asosiy sabab ekani aytilmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Ceramicist Odina Rask makes her bowls from clay she digs herself from the riverbank behind her studio. Unlike commercial clay, which is cleaned and mixed so that it behaves the same way every time, her river clay changes from batch to batch: some loads crack in the kiln, while others turn unexpected shades of red or gray. Rask says that this unpredictability is exactly why she uses the river clay, since it keeps her from repeating the same designs.\",\"stem\":\"According to the text, why does Rask use clay from the riverbank behind her studio?\",\"option_a\":\"It costs less than commercial clay.\",\"option_b\":\"It never cracks when it is fired in the kiln.\",\"option_c\":\"Its unpredictable qualities keep her from repeating her designs.\",\"option_d\":\"It is cleaner and more uniform than commercial clay.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The last sentence states Rask's reason directly: the clay's “unpredictability is exactly why she uses” it, “since it keeps her from repeating the same designs.” That matches choice C. Choice A is never mentioned. Choice B contradicts the text, which says that “some loads crack in the kiln.” Choice D reverses the contrast: it is commercial clay that is cleaned and uniform, not her river clay.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Oxirgi jumlada Raskning sababi to‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri aytilgan: loyning oldindan bilib bo‘lmasligi (“unpredictability”) aynan u bu loyni ishlatishining sababi, chunki bu uni bir xil naqshlarni takrorlashdan saqlaydi. Bu C javobga mos. A haqida matnda hech narsa aytilmagan. B matnga zid: “some loads crack in the kiln” — ba’zi partiyalar xumdonda yorilib ketadi. D qarama-qarshilikni teskari qiladi: tozalangan va bir xil bo‘lgani — sotuvdagi loy, daryo loyi emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is adapted from a short story.\\n\\nBekzod had assumed that gardening meant simply putting seeds in the ground and waiting. But his grandmother tested the soil with her fingers before every watering, moved the tomato pots twice a day to follow the sun, and spoke about each plant as if it had moods of its own. By the end of the summer, Bekzod understood that her harvest, which the neighbors called luck, was really the result of countless small decisions.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Bekzod's grandmother is frustrated that her neighbors do not appreciate her garden.\",\"option_b\":\"Bekzod decides that he wants to become a professional gardener.\",\"option_c\":\"The grandmother's garden produces more tomatoes than any other garden nearby.\",\"option_d\":\"Bekzod comes to realize that his grandmother's success as a gardener results from careful, constant attention.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Bekzod begins with a simple idea of gardening, observes his grandmother's many careful habits, and finally understands that her harvest comes from “countless small decisions,” not luck. Choice D states this realization. Choice A is unsupported: the grandmother's feelings about her neighbors are never described. Choice B goes beyond the text, which says nothing about Bekzod's career plans. Choice C makes a comparison that the text never makes.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bekzod avval bog‘dorchilikni oddiy ish deb o‘ylaydi, keyin buvisining ko‘plab puxta odatlarini kuzatadi va oxirida uning hosili omad emas, “son-sanoqsiz kichik qarorlar” natijasi ekanini tushunadi. D javob aynan shu anglashni ifodalaydi. A asossiz: buvining qo‘shnilarga munosabati tasvirlanmagan. B matn doirasidan chiqib ketadi: Bekzodning kasb tanlashi haqida gap yo‘q. C esa matnda yo‘q taqqoslashni qiladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Large volcanic eruptions can release sulfur gases that form tiny droplets high in the atmosphere. These droplets reflect some sunlight back into space and can cool the planet for a year or two. Climate scientist Mehmet Arslan examined tree rings from high-mountain forests and found that unusually narrow rings, a sign of cold, short growing seasons, often appear in the years just after large eruptions recorded in polar ice. Arslan argues that tree rings can therefore help scientists estimate the climate effects of eruptions that happened before written records were kept.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Volcanic eruptions are the main cause of long-term changes in Earth's climate.\",\"option_b\":\"Because tree rings record cold years after eruptions, they may help scientists study the climate effects of eruptions that occurred long ago.\",\"option_c\":\"Polar ice provides more reliable evidence of past eruptions than tree rings do.\",\"option_d\":\"Trees in high-mountain forests grow more slowly than trees at lower elevations.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text explains how eruptions can cool the planet, describes Arslan's finding that narrow tree rings often follow large eruptions, and ends with his argument that tree rings can help estimate the climate effects of eruptions from before written records. Choice B captures this. Choice A is too extreme: the text says eruptions can cool the planet “for a year or two,” not that they drive long-term change. Choice C makes a comparison the text does not make; the ice records are used together with tree rings. Choice D is unsupported: the text does not compare trees at different elevations.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn vulqon otilishlari sayyorani qanday sovitishi mumkinligini tushuntiradi, so‘ng Arslanning topilmasini — yirik otilishlardan keyin daraxtlarda ko‘pincha ingichka yillik halqalar paydo bo‘lishini — tasvirlaydi va yozma manbalar paydo bo‘lishidan oldingi otilishlarning iqlimga ta’sirini daraxt halqalari yordamida baholash mumkin degan fikri bilan yakunlanadi. B javob shuni ifodalaydi. A haddan tashqari kuchli: matnda otilishlar sayyorani “bir-ikki yil” sovitishi mumkinligi aytilgan, iqlimning uzoq muddatli o‘zgarishlariga asosiy sabab ekani emas. C matnda yo‘q taqqoslash: muz ma’lumotlari daraxt halqalari bilan birga ishlatiladi. D asossiz: matnda turli balandlikdagi daraxtlar solishtirilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In the early 1900s, the city of Varnholt built a network of public bathhouses. City officials presented them as a way to improve public health, since few apartments had running water. Historian Clara Ostrova, however, has found that the bathhouses quickly became much more than places to wash: residents used them to exchange news, hold meetings of workers' unions and celebrate weddings. Ostrova argues that the bathhouses became some of the city's most important gathering places.\",\"stem\":\"According to the text, what has Ostrova found about the bathhouses in Varnholt?\",\"option_a\":\"Residents used them for a range of social activities beyond bathing.\",\"option_b\":\"They were built mainly to provide meeting places for workers' unions.\",\"option_c\":\"They did little to improve public health in the city.\",\"option_d\":\"They were rarely used because most apartments had running water.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Ostrova found that residents used the bathhouses “to exchange news, hold meetings of workers' unions and celebrate weddings,” which choice A summarizes. Choice B confuses one of these uses with the reason the bathhouses were built; officials presented them as a way to improve public health. Choice C is unsupported: Ostrova's findings concern social uses, not health results. Choice D contradicts the text, which says that “few apartments had running water.”\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ostrova aholining hammomlarda “yangiliklar almashgani, ishchilar kasaba uyushmalari yig‘ilishlarini o‘tkazgani va to‘ylar nishonlagani”ni aniqlagan — A javob shuni umumlashtiradi. B hammomlardan foydalanish usullaridan birini ularning qurilish sababi bilan aralashtiradi; rasmiylar ularni aholi salomatligini yaxshilash vositasi sifatida taqdim etgan. C asossiz: Ostrovaning topilmalari salomatlik natijalari haqida emas, ijtimoiy foydalanish haqida. D matnga zid: matnda “few apartments had running water” — oqar suvli xonadonlar kam bo‘lgani aytilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is from a poem. The speaker is addressing an old map.\\n\\nYou promised roads where only rivers ran,\\nAnd drew a city where the marsh still spreads;\\nYour mountains lean a little to the west,\\nYour coastlines wander. Still, I keep you near,\\nNot for the way you show me where things are,\\nBut for the way you show what someone hoped.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"The speaker intends to correct the errors on the old map.\",\"option_b\":\"The speaker is upset that the map caused travelers to become lost.\",\"option_c\":\"The speaker prefers modern maps because they are more accurate.\",\"option_d\":\"Although the map is inaccurate, the speaker values it as a record of its maker's hopes.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first lines list the map's errors (roads where there are only rivers, a city where there is marsh, misplaced mountains), but the speaker then says, “Still, I keep you near,” valuing the map not for its accuracy but for showing “what someone hoped.” Choice D captures this. Choice A is unsupported: the speaker never mentions correcting the map. Choice B is unsupported: no lost travelers are mentioned, and the speaker's tone is affectionate. Choice C is wrong because modern maps are never mentioned.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"She’rning birinchi satrlarida xaritaning xatolari sanab o‘tiladi (faqat daryolar oqadigan joyda yo‘llar, botqoq o‘rnida shahar, joyidan siljigan tog‘lar), lekin so‘ng so‘zlovchi “Still, I keep you near” deydi: u xaritani aniqligi uchun emas, “kimningdir umidlarini” ko‘rsatgani uchun qadrlaydi. D javob shuni ifodalaydi. A asossiz: so‘zlovchi xaritani tuzatish haqida gapirmaydi. B asossiz: adashgan sayohatchilar tilga olinmagan, so‘zlovchining ohangi esa iliq. C noto‘g‘ri: zamonaviy xaritalar haqida gap yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"City planners often assume that building a park in a neighborhood without green space will lead residents to exercise more. Public health researcher Hye-jin Seo tested this assumption by surveying residents of twelve neighborhoods before new parks opened in them and again two years later. Across the twelve neighborhoods, residents reported only small increases in exercise. In the three neighborhoods where the city also organized free fitness classes and walking groups in the new parks, however, exercise rose substantially.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Building new parks has no effect on how much residents exercise.\",\"option_b\":\"Free fitness classes improve residents' health more than parks do.\",\"option_c\":\"A new park may do little to increase residents' exercise unless it is paired with programs that encourage people to use it.\",\"option_d\":\"Residents of neighborhoods without green space exercise less than residents of other neighborhoods.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text describes an assumption (new parks lead to more exercise), a test of it, a weak overall result, and a much stronger result where the parks came with organized programs. Together these points suggest that a park alone may do little unless it is paired with programs, as choice C says. Choice A is too extreme: residents did report “small increases.” Choice B makes a comparison the study did not test, since the classes were held in the new parks rather than offered without them, and the study measured exercise, not overall health. Choice D is not stated; the study measured changes in exercise, not differences between neighborhoods with and without green space.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda taxmin (park qurilsa, odamlar ko‘proq jismoniy mashq qiladi), uning sinovi, umumiy natijaning kuchsizligi va parklar tashkil etilgan dasturlar bilan birga bo‘lgan joylardagi ancha kuchli natija tasvirlanadi. Bu fikrlar birgalikda park o‘zi yolg‘iz, dasturlarsiz kam natija berishi mumkinligini ko‘rsatadi — to‘g‘ri javob C. A haddan tashqari kuchli: aholi “kichik o‘sish” haqida xabar bergan. B tadqiqotda sinalmagan taqqoslashni qiladi: mashg‘ulotlar parklardan alohida emas, aynan yangi parklarda o‘tkazilgan, tadqiqot esa umumiy salomatlikni emas, jismoniy faollikni o‘lchagan. D matnda aytilmagan: tadqiqot yashil maydonli va yashil maydonsiz mahallalarni solishtirmagan, balki jismoniy faollikdagi o‘zgarishni o‘lchagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is adapted from a novel. Mira has returned to her hometown after ten years away.\\n\\nThe bakery on the corner had a new sign, and the bench outside the post office had been painted green. Mira noted each change with a small, unreasonable resentment, as though the town had been obliged to wait for her. Yet when she pushed open the bakery door and smelled the same cardamom bread her mother used to buy on Fridays, she was not comforted but unsettled: it was harder, somehow, to be met by what had stayed the same.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Mira is pleased to discover how much her hometown has improved while she was away.\",\"option_b\":\"Mira's return stirs complicated feelings, since both the changes in her hometown and the things that have stayed the same disturb her.\",\"option_c\":\"Mira regrets having left her hometown and decides to stay there permanently.\",\"option_d\":\"Mira is disappointed that the bakery no longer sells the bread her mother used to buy.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Mira feels “resentment” at the town's changes, yet the unchanged cardamom bread leaves her “not comforted but unsettled.” Both the new and the familiar trouble her, as choice B says. Choice A contradicts her resentment toward the changes. Choice C is unsupported: the text never mentions regret or a decision to stay. Choice D contradicts the text, which says the bakery still has “the same cardamom bread.”\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Mira shahardagi o‘zgarishlardan ranjiydi (“resentment”), ammo o‘zgarmagan kardamonli non hidi ham unga taskin bermaydi, aksincha, uni bezovta qiladi (“not comforted but unsettled”). Demak, uni ham yangi, ham tanish narsalar bezovta qiladi — to‘g‘ri javob B. A uning o‘zgarishlardan ranjishiga zid. C asossiz: matnda afsus yoki shaharda qolish qarori haqida gap yo‘q. D matnga zid: matnga ko‘ra novvoyxonada hali ham “the same cardamom bread” — o‘sha kardamonli non bor.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A circle has an area of $49\\\\pi$ square inches. What is the circumference, in inches, of the circle?\",\"option_a\":\"$14\\\\pi$\",\"option_b\":\"$28\\\\pi$\",\"option_c\":\"$49\\\\pi$\",\"option_d\":\"$98\\\\pi$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The area is $\\\\pi r^2 = 49\\\\pi$, so $r^2 = 49$ and $r = 7$ inches. The circumference is $2\\\\pi r = 2\\\\pi(7) = 14\\\\pi$ inches. Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B ($28\\\\pi$) uses the diameter, 14, in place of the radius. Choice C ($49\\\\pi$) assumes the circumference equals the area. Choice D ($98\\\\pi$) is $2\\\\pi r^2$, a mix of the area and circumference formulas.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Doira yuzasi $\\\\pi r^2 = 49\\\\pi$, demak $r^2 = 49$ va $r = 7$ dyuym. Aylana uzunligi $2\\\\pi r = 2\\\\pi(7) = 14\\\\pi$ dyuym. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB ($28\\\\pi$) — radius o‘rniga diametr (14) olingan. C ($49\\\\pi$) — aylana uzunligi yuzaga teng deb olingan. D ($98\\\\pi$) — bu $2\\\\pi r^2$, yuza va aylana uzunligi formulalari aralashtirib yuborilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A circle has a radius of 10 centimeters. A central angle of the circle measures $72^\\\\circ$. The length of the arc intercepted by this central angle is $k\\\\pi$ centimeters. What is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"4\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The arc is $\\\\frac{72}{360} = \\\\frac{1}{5}$ of the whole circle. The circumference is $2\\\\pi(10) = 20\\\\pi$ centimeters, so the arc length is $\\\\frac{1}{5} \\\\cdot 20\\\\pi = 4\\\\pi$ centimeters, and $k = 4$.\\n\\nIf you got 20, you found the area of the sector ($\\\\frac{1}{5} \\\\cdot 100\\\\pi = 20\\\\pi$) instead of the arc length.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Yoy butun aylananing $\\\\frac{72}{360} = \\\\frac{1}{5}$ qismini tashkil qiladi. Aylana uzunligi $2\\\\pi(10) = 20\\\\pi$ santimetr, demak yoy uzunligi $\\\\frac{1}{5} \\\\cdot 20\\\\pi = 4\\\\pi$ santimetr va $k = 4$.\\n\\nAgar 20 chiqqan bo‘lsa, siz yoy uzunligi o‘rniga sektor yuzasini ($\\\\frac{1}{5} \\\\cdot 100\\\\pi = 20\\\\pi$) topgansiz.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"An angle measures $\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{6}$ radians. What is the measure of the angle in degrees?\",\"option_a\":\"$30^\\\\circ$\",\"option_b\":\"$75^\\\\circ$\",\"option_c\":\"$150^\\\\circ$\",\"option_d\":\"$300^\\\\circ$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Because $\\\\pi$ radians equals $180^\\\\circ$, multiply by $\\\\frac{180^\\\\circ}{\\\\pi}$: $\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{6} \\\\cdot \\\\frac{180^\\\\circ}{\\\\pi} = 5 \\\\cdot 30^\\\\circ = 150^\\\\circ$. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($30^\\\\circ$) converts only $\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{6}$ and drops the factor 5. Choice B ($75^\\\\circ$) uses $\\\\pi = 90^\\\\circ$. Choice D ($300^\\\\circ$) uses $\\\\pi = 360^\\\\circ$; a full turn of $360^\\\\circ$ is $2\\\\pi$ radians, not $\\\\pi$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$\\\\pi$ radian $180^\\\\circ$ ga teng, shuning uchun $\\\\frac{180^\\\\circ}{\\\\pi}$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{6} \\\\cdot \\\\frac{180^\\\\circ}{\\\\pi} = 5 \\\\cdot 30^\\\\circ = 150^\\\\circ$. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA ($30^\\\\circ$) — faqat $\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{6}$ o‘girilgan, 5 ko‘paytuvchi tushib qolgan. B ($75^\\\\circ$) — $\\\\pi = 90^\\\\circ$ deb olingan. D ($300^\\\\circ$) — $\\\\pi = 360^\\\\circ$ deb olingan; aslida to‘liq aylanish $360^\\\\circ$ — bu $\\\\pi$ emas, $2\\\\pi$ radian.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The equation $x^2 + y^2 + 10x - 4y = -13$ defines a circle in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of the center of the circle and the length of its radius?\",\"option_a\":\"Center $(-5, 2)$, radius 4\",\"option_b\":\"Center $(5, -2)$, radius 4\",\"option_c\":\"Center $(-5, 2)$, radius 16\",\"option_d\":\"Center $(-10, 4)$, radius 4\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Complete the square in each variable. For $x^2 + 10x$, add $\\\\left(\\\\frac{10}{2}\\\\right)^2 = 25$; for $y^2 - 4y$, add $\\\\left(\\\\frac{-4}{2}\\\\right)^2 = 4$. Adding 25 and 4 to both sides gives $(x + 5)^2 + (y - 2)^2 = -13 + 25 + 4 = 16$. This matches $(x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2$ with $h = -5$, $k = 2$, and $r = \\\\sqrt{16} = 4$. Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B reverses the signs of the center's coordinates. Choice C gives $r^2 = 16$ as the radius. Choice D uses the coefficients 10 and $-4$ themselves instead of half of each.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir o‘zgaruvchi uchun to‘la kvadrat ajratamiz. $x^2 + 10x$ ga $\\\\left(\\\\frac{10}{2}\\\\right)^2 = 25$, $y^2 - 4y$ ga esa $\\\\left(\\\\frac{-4}{2}\\\\right)^2 = 4$ qo‘shiladi. 25 va 4 ni tenglamaning ikkala tomoniga qo‘shsak: $(x + 5)^2 + (y - 2)^2 = -13 + 25 + 4 = 16$. Bu $(x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2$ ko‘rinishiga mos: $h = -5$, $k = 2$, $r = \\\\sqrt{16} = 4$. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB — markaz koordinatalarining ishoralari teskari olingan. C — $r^2 = 16$ radius deb olingan. D — koeffitsiyentlarning yarmi o‘rniga 10 va $-4$ ning o‘zi ishlatilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In a circle with center $O$ and radius 12, the length of minor arc $AB$ is $5\\\\pi$. What is the measure, in degrees, of central angle $AOB$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"75\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The circumference is $2\\\\pi(12) = 24\\\\pi$. The arc is $\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{24\\\\pi} = \\\\frac{5}{24}$ of the circle, so the central angle is $\\\\frac{5}{24} \\\\cdot 360^\\\\circ = 75^\\\\circ$. In radians, $\\\\theta = \\\\frac{s}{r} = \\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{12}$, which also equals $75^\\\\circ$. Enter 75.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Aylana uzunligi $2\\\\pi(12) = 24\\\\pi$. Yoy aylananing $\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{24\\\\pi} = \\\\frac{5}{24}$ qismi, demak markaziy burchak $\\\\frac{5}{24} \\\\cdot 360^\\\\circ = 75^\\\\circ$. Radianda: $\\\\theta = \\\\frac{s}{r} = \\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{12}$, bu ham $75^\\\\circ$ ga teng. Javob katagiga 75 ni yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Line $\\\\ell$ is tangent at point $P$ to a circle with center $O$ and radius 9. Point $Q$ lies on line $\\\\ell$, and $PQ = 12$. What is the length of $\\\\overline{OQ}$?\",\"option_a\":\"3\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\sqrt{21}$\",\"option_c\":\"$3\\\\sqrt{7}$\",\"option_d\":\"15\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"A tangent line is perpendicular to the radius drawn to the point of tangency, so angle $OPQ$ is a right angle. In right triangle $OPQ$, $\\\\overline{OQ}$ is the hypotenuse: $OQ = \\\\sqrt{9^2 + 12^2} = \\\\sqrt{225} = 15$. Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A (3) simply subtracts $12 - 9$. Choice B ($\\\\sqrt{21}$) adds 9 and 12 without squaring them. Choice C ($3\\\\sqrt{7} = \\\\sqrt{144 - 81}$) treats $\\\\overline{PQ}$ as the hypotenuse, but the hypotenuse is the side opposite the right angle at $P$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Urinma urinish nuqtasiga o‘tkazilgan radiusga perpendikulyar, shuning uchun $OPQ$ burchak to‘g‘ri burchak. $OPQ$ to‘g‘ri burchakli uchburchakda $\\\\overline{OQ}$ — gipotenuza: $OQ = \\\\sqrt{9^2 + 12^2} = \\\\sqrt{225} = 15$. To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA (3) — shunchaki $12 - 9$ ayirilgan. B ($\\\\sqrt{21}$) — 9 va 12 kvadratga oshirilmasdan qo‘shilgan. C ($3\\\\sqrt{7} = \\\\sqrt{144 - 81}$) — $\\\\overline{PQ}$ gipotenuza deb olingan, holbuki gipotenuza $P$ dagi to‘g‘ri burchak qarshisidagi tomon.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, the graph of the equation $x^2 - 12x + y^2 + 2y + c = 0$ is a circle with radius 7, where $c$ is a constant. What is the value of $c$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-12$\",\"option_b\":\"12\",\"option_c\":\"30\",\"option_d\":\"86\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Complete the square: $(x^2 - 12x + 36) + (y^2 + 2y + 1) = -c + 36 + 1$, so $(x - 6)^2 + (y + 1)^2 = 37 - c$. The right side must equal $r^2 = 7^2 = 49$. Solving $37 - c = 49$ gives $c = -12$. Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B (12) has the wrong sign; it computes $49 - 37$. Choice C (30) sets $37 - c$ equal to 7 instead of $7^2$. Choice D (86) adds 37 and 49 instead of solving $37 - c = 49$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"To‘la kvadrat ajratamiz: $(x^2 - 12x + 36) + (y^2 + 2y + 1) = -c + 36 + 1$, ya’ni $(x - 6)^2 + (y + 1)^2 = 37 - c$. O‘ng tomon $r^2 = 7^2 = 49$ ga teng bo‘lishi kerak. $37 - c = 49$ tenglamadan $c = -12$. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB (12) — ishora xato: $49 - 37$ hisoblangan. C (30) — $37 - c$ ifoda $7^2$ ga emas, 7 ga tenglashtirilgan. D (86) — $37 - c = 49$ ni yechish o‘rniga 37 va 49 qo‘shilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"Points $A$, $B$, and $C$ lie on a circle with center $O$ and radius 20. The measure of inscribed angle $ACB$ is $\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{5}$ radians. The length of minor arc $AB$ is $k\\\\pi$, where $k$ is a constant. What is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"8\"],\"explanation_en\":\"An inscribed angle measures half of the central angle that intercepts the same arc. Because $\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{5}$ is less than $\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}$, angle $ACB$ intercepts minor arc $AB$, and central angle $AOB$ measures $2 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi}{5} = \\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{5}$ radians. With the angle in radians, arc length is $s = r\\\\theta = 20 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{5} = 8\\\\pi$, so $k = 8$.\\n\\nUsing the inscribed angle as if it were the central angle gives $20 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi}{5} = 4\\\\pi$, so 4 is a trap.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ichki chizilgan burchak xuddi shu yoyga tiralgan markaziy burchakning yarmiga teng. $\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{5}$ burchak $\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}$ dan kichik, shuning uchun $ACB$ burchak kichik $AB$ yoyga tiraladi va markaziy $AOB$ burchak $2 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi}{5} = \\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{5}$ radianga teng. Burchak radianda bo‘lganda yoy uzunligi $s = r\\\\theta = 20 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{5} = 8\\\\pi$, demak $k = 8$.\\n\\nIchki chizilgan burchakni markaziy burchak deb olsak, $20 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi}{5} = 4\\\\pi$ chiqadi — 4 javobi tuzoq.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Members of a school science club grew sunflowers in four types of soil and measured the plants' heights after eight weeks. Club president Aziza Karimova reported that the type of soil made a large difference: the tallest sunflowers, which were grown in ______, were more than twice as tall as the shortest ones.\\n\\n**Average sunflower height after eight weeks**\\n\\n| Soil type | Average height (cm) |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| Sandy | 48 |\\n| Clay | 61 |\\n| Compost-rich | 112 |\\n| Rocky | 39 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?\",\"option_a\":\"sandy soil, averaging 48 cm\",\"option_b\":\"clay soil, averaging 61 cm\",\"option_c\":\"compost-rich soil, averaging 112 cm\",\"option_d\":\"rocky soil, averaging 39 cm\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The statement describes the tallest sunflowers. According to the table, the plants grown in compost-rich soil had the greatest average height, 112 cm, which is more than twice the shortest average of 39 cm (rocky soil), so choice C is correct. Choices A and B name soils whose sunflowers were neither the tallest nor more than twice as tall as 39 cm (2 × 39 = 78). Choice D names the soil with the shortest sunflowers, not the tallest.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gapda eng baland kungaboqarlar haqida so‘z boradi. Jadvalga ko‘ra, eng katta o‘rtacha balandlik — 112 sm — kompostga boy tuproqda o‘stirilgan o‘simliklarda; bu eng past o‘rtacha balandlikdan (toshloq tuproq, 39 sm) ikki baravardan ko‘proq. Demak, to‘g‘ri javob — C. A va B dagi tuproqlarda o‘sgan kungaboqarlar eng baland ham emas, 39 sm dan ikki baravar baland ham emas (2 × 39 = 78). D esa eng baland emas, eng past kungaboqarlar o‘sgan tuproqni ko‘rsatadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Transportation planner Gulnora Sobirova surveyed residents of the city of Marlow about how they usually traveled to work in 2014 and in 2024. She claims that the share of residents who cycle to work grew substantially over that decade.\\n\\n**Usual way of traveling to work (percentage of Marlow residents)**\\n\\n| Way of traveling | 2014 | 2024 |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Car | 58% | 49% |\\n| Public transit | 27% | 28% |\\n| Bicycle | 4% | 13% |\\n| Walking | 11% | 10% |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support Sobirova's claim?\",\"option_a\":\"The percentage of residents who usually cycled to work rose from 4% in 2014 to 13% in 2024.\",\"option_b\":\"The percentage of residents who usually drove to work fell from 58% in 2014 to 49% in 2024.\",\"option_c\":\"In both 2014 and 2024, a greater percentage of residents usually took public transit to work than usually cycled.\",\"option_d\":\"In 2014, 11% of residents usually walked to work.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Sobirova's claim is about growth in cycling. Choice A shows that the share of residents who usually cycled to work more than tripled, from 4% to 13%. Choice B is accurate but describes driving, not cycling. Choice C is accurate but compares transit with cycling instead of showing that cycling grew. Choice D gives a single walking figure that is irrelevant to the claim.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Sobirovaning da’vosi velosipedda ishga boruvchilar ulushining o‘sishi haqida. A javob bu ulush 4% dan 13% gacha — uch baravardan ko‘proq oshganini ko‘rsatadi. B jadvalga mos, lekin velosiped haqida emas, avtomobil haqida. C ham jadvalga mos, ammo u velosipedning o‘sishini ko‘rsatmaydi, faqat jamoat transporti bilan taqqoslaydi. D da’voga aloqasi bo‘lmagan, piyoda yurish bo‘yicha bitta raqamni beradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Ornithologist Teodor Vance counted the visits that four bird species made to a feeding station during one week in winter. Vance noted that chickadees visited the station more often than any other species did, with ______\\n\\n**Visits to the feeding station in one week**\\n\\n| Bird species | Visits |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| Chickadee | 214 |\\n| Nuthatch | 87 |\\n| Blue jay | 142 |\\n| Cardinal | 63 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?\",\"option_a\":\"87 visits, compared with 214 visits by nuthatches.\",\"option_b\":\"142 visits, compared with 63 visits by cardinals.\",\"option_c\":\"214 visits, compared with 63 visits by blue jays.\",\"option_d\":\"214 visits, compared with 142 visits by blue jays, the species with the next-highest total.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The table shows 214 visits by chickadees, the highest total, and 142 by blue jays, the next-highest total. Choice D reports both figures correctly. Choice A reverses the chickadee and nuthatch figures. Choice B gives the blue jay total as the chickadee total. Choice C gives the correct chickadee total but pairs the cardinal figure (63) with blue jays, which actually made 142 visits.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Jadvalga ko‘ra, chickadee qushlari 214 marta kelgan — bu eng yuqori ko‘rsatkich; ikkinchi o‘rinda 142 ta tashrif bilan blue jay turadi. D javob ikkala raqamni ham to‘g‘ri beradi. A chickadee va nuthatch raqamlarini almashtirib yuboradi. B chickadee uchun blue jay raqamini beradi. C chickadee raqamini to‘g‘ri beradi, lekin blue jay uchun cardinal raqamini (63) ko‘rsatadi, holbuki blue jay 142 marta kelgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Agronomist Dilshod Rahimov compared three new wheat varieties with a standard variety at a test farm, once in a dry year and once in a wet year. He argues that variety K-7 is the best choice for farmers whose rainfall is unpredictable, because it produced far more than the standard variety in the dry year while yielding nearly as much as the standard variety in the wet year.\\n\\n**Wheat yield (tonnes per hectare)**\\n\\n| Variety | Dry year | Wet year |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Standard | 2.1 | 4.8 |\\n| K-7 | 3.4 | 4.6 |\\n| K-9 | 3.6 | 3.2 |\\n| L-2 | 2.0 | 5.1 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support Rahimov's argument?\",\"option_a\":\"In the dry year, K-9 yielded 3.6 tonnes per hectare, more than any other variety.\",\"option_b\":\"K-7 yielded 3.4 tonnes per hectare in the dry year, compared with 2.1 for the standard variety, and 4.6 tonnes per hectare in the wet year, compared with 4.8 for the standard variety.\",\"option_c\":\"In the wet year, L-2 yielded 5.1 tonnes per hectare, more than the standard variety's 4.8 tonnes per hectare.\",\"option_d\":\"K-7 yielded more in the wet year (4.6 tonnes per hectare) than in the dry year (3.4 tonnes per hectare).\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Rahimov's argument makes two comparisons between K-7 and the standard variety: K-7 produced far more in the dry year and nearly as much in the wet year. Choice B gives both comparisons: 3.4 versus 2.1 tonnes per hectare in the dry year and 4.6 versus 4.8 in the wet year. Choice A is accurate but concerns K-9, not K-7. Choice C is accurate but concerns L-2. Choice D is accurate but compares K-7 with itself across the two years instead of with the standard variety, so it does not address the argument.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Rahimovning dalili K-7 ni standart nav bilan ikki jihatdan solishtiradi: qurg‘oqchil yilda K-7 ancha ko‘p hosil bergan, nam yilda esa deyarli standart nav darajasida hosil bergan. B javob ikkala taqqoslashni ham beradi: qurg‘oqchil yilda gektariga 3.4 tonnaga qarshi 2.1 tonna, nam yilda 4.6 tonnaga qarshi 4.8 tonna. A jadvalga mos, lekin K-7 haqida emas, K-9 haqida. C ham to‘g‘ri, lekin L-2 haqida. D ham jadvalga mos, ammo K-7 ni standart nav bilan emas, o‘zi bilan turli yillarda solishtiradi, shuning uchun dalilni qo‘llab-quvvatlamaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Sea otters eat sea urchins, and sea urchins graze on kelp, a large seaweed. Ecologist Lana Petrovic predicted that after sea otters returned to Corran Bay in 2016, kelp forests there would expand. Her survey data are consistent with this prediction: from 2016 to 2020, ______\\n\\n**Corran Bay survey results**\\n\\n| Year | Sea otters | Urchins per square meter | Seafloor covered by kelp |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| 2014 | 0 | 41 | 12% |\\n| 2016 | 15 | 38 | 14% |\\n| 2018 | 60 | 19 | 27% |\\n| 2020 | 110 | 8 | 46% |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?\",\"option_a\":\"as the number of otters rose from 15 to 110, urchin density fell from 38 to 8 per square meter and kelp cover increased from 14% to 46% of the seafloor.\",\"option_b\":\"the number of otters rose from 0 to 15, while kelp cover increased from 12% to 14% of the seafloor.\",\"option_c\":\"urchin density fell from 41 to 8 per square meter, while kelp cover remained nearly unchanged.\",\"option_d\":\"kelp cover increased from 14% to 46% of the seafloor, while the number of otters remained about the same.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The statement concerns the period from 2016 to 2020. During that time, otters increased from 15 to 110, urchins decreased from 38 to 8 per square meter, and kelp cover grew from 14% to 46%, which is exactly the pattern Petrovic predicted, as choice A says. Choice B uses figures from 2014 to 2016, not from 2016 to 2020. Choice C uses the 2014 urchin figure (41) and wrongly says that kelp cover barely changed. Choice D wrongly says that the number of otters stayed about the same.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gap 2016–2020-yillar haqida. Bu davrda dengiz qunduzlari (otters) soni 15 tadan 110 taga oshgan, dengiz tipratikanlari (urchins) zichligi kvadrat metrga 38 tadan 8 taga kamaygan, kelp suvo‘tlari qoplami esa 14% dan 46% gacha kengaygan — bu Petrovic bashorat qilgan manzaraning aynan o‘zi. To‘g‘ri javob — A. B 2016–2020 emas, 2014–2016-yillar raqamlarini beradi. C 2014-yilgi tipratikanlar raqamini (41) ishlatadi va kelp qoplami deyarli o‘zgarmagan deb noto‘g‘ri aytadi. D qunduzlar soni deyarli o‘zgarmagan deb noto‘g‘ri aytadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Librarians in the city of Brenna compared how often different types of books were borrowed in 2018 and in 2023. Researcher Ilhom Nazarov claims that changes in borrowing were uneven across categories: loans of one type of book nearly doubled, while loans of another type fell.\\n\\n**Library loans (thousands)**\\n\\n| Category | 2018 | 2023 |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Graphic novels | 22 | 43 |\\n| Cookbooks | 15 | 17 |\\n| Travel guides | 19 | 11 |\\n| Biographies | 26 | 29 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support Nazarov's claim?\",\"option_a\":\"Biographies had more loans than any other category in 2018, with 26 thousand.\",\"option_b\":\"Loans of cookbooks rose from 15 thousand to 17 thousand, and loans of biographies rose from 26 thousand to 29 thousand.\",\"option_c\":\"Loans of graphic novels rose from 22 thousand in 2018 to 43 thousand in 2023, while loans of travel guides fell from 19 thousand to 11 thousand.\",\"option_d\":\"Loans of travel guides fell from 19 thousand in 2018 to 11 thousand in 2023.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Nazarov's claim has two parts: loans of one category nearly doubled, and loans of another fell. Choice C supports both: graphic novel loans went from 22 to 43 thousand (nearly double), while travel guide loans dropped from 19 to 11 thousand. Choice A gives a single 2018 figure and shows no change at all. Choice B describes two modest increases, neither of which is close to doubling or is a decline. Choice D is accurate but supports only the second part of the claim.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Nazarovning da’vosi ikki qismdan iborat: bir turdagi kitoblarni olish deyarli ikki baravar oshgan, boshqa turdagisini olish esa kamaygan. C javob ikkalasini ham qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi: graphic novels (komikslar) 22 mingdan 43 mingga — deyarli ikki baravar oshgan, sayohat qo‘llanmalari esa 19 mingdan 11 mingga kamaygan. A faqat 2018-yilga oid bitta raqamni beradi va hech qanday o‘zgarishni ko‘rsatmaydi. B ikkita kichik o‘sishni tasvirlaydi — ular na ikki baravar o‘sish, na kamayish. D jadvalga mos, lekin da’voning faqat ikkinchi qismini qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The cities of Aldmoor and Bexley both launched curbside food-waste collection programs in 2021. A local newspaper declared Aldmoor's program the more successful one because it collected more food waste in 2023. Analyst Saida Tursunova calls this comparison misleading: Aldmoor collected more in total only because more of its households took part, and each participating household in Bexley actually contributed more food waste than each participating household in Aldmoor did.\\n\\n**Food-waste collection programs, 2023**\\n\\n| City | Households | Participating households | Food waste collected (tonnes) |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| Aldmoor | 120,000 | 30,000 | 4,500 |\\n| Bexley | 40,000 | 20,000 | 3,600 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support Tursunova's argument?\",\"option_a\":\"Aldmoor collected 4,500 tonnes of food waste in 2023, while Bexley collected 3,600 tonnes.\",\"option_b\":\"Aldmoor had 30,000 participating households, while Bexley had 20,000.\",\"option_c\":\"Half of Bexley's 40,000 households took part in its program, while only one-quarter of Aldmoor's 120,000 households took part in Aldmoor's program.\",\"option_d\":\"Aldmoor's 30,000 participating households outnumbered Bexley's 20,000, but each participating household in Bexley contributed an average of 180 kilograms of food waste, compared with 150 kilograms in Aldmoor.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Tursunova makes two points: Aldmoor's larger total came from having more participating households, and Bexley's participating households each contributed more. Choice D supports both: Aldmoor had 30,000 participating households to Bexley's 20,000, but Bexley averaged 180 kilograms per participating household (3,600 tonnes ÷ 20,000) compared with Aldmoor's 150 kilograms (4,500 tonnes ÷ 30,000). Choice A gives the totals the newspaper relied on, which support the newspaper's view rather than Tursunova's. Choice B supports only her first point. Choice C compares participation rates, which show what share of households joined, not how much each participating household contributed.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tursunova ikki fikr bildiradi: Aldmoorning umumiy ko‘rsatkichi katta bo‘lishiga sabab — ishtirokchi xonadonlar ko‘pligi, Bexleyda esa har bir ishtirokchi xonadon ko‘proq chiqindi topshirgan. D javob ikkalasini ham qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi: Aldmoorda 30,000, Bexleyda 20,000 ishtirokchi xonadon bo‘lgan, lekin Bexleyda bir ishtirokchi xonadonga o‘rtacha 180 kilogramm (3,600 tonna ÷ 20,000) to‘g‘ri kelgan, Aldmoorda esa 150 kilogramm (4,500 tonna ÷ 30,000). A gazeta tayangan umumiy raqamlarni beradi — ular Tursunovani emas, gazetaning fikrini qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi. B faqat birinchi fikrni qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi. C ishtirok ulushini solishtiradi: bu xonadonlarning qancha qismi qatnashganini ko‘rsatadi, har bir ishtirokchi xonadon qancha chiqindi topshirganini emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In 2022, four museums in the city of Orvel began offering free admission on Sundays. Critics predicted that free Sundays would simply shift visits from other days to Sunday, leaving total attendance unchanged. Museum researcher Lina Haddad found, however, that at some museums free Sundays seem to have attracted visitors who would not otherwise have come: ______\\n\\n**Average weekly visitors**\\n\\n| Museum | Other days, 2021 | Other days, 2023 | Sundays, 2021 | Sundays, 2023 |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| Museum of Textiles | 3,200 | 3,150 | 600 | 1,900 |\\n| City History Museum | 2,800 | 2,750 | 500 | 1,400 |\\n| Natural History Museum | 5,100 | 4,000 | 900 | 2,000 |\\n| Glass Museum | 1,500 | 1,480 | 300 | 1,100 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?\",\"option_a\":\"at the Natural History Museum, attendance on other days fell from 5,100 to 4,000 while Sunday attendance rose from 900 to 2,000.\",\"option_b\":\"at the Museum of Textiles, Sunday attendance rose from 600 to 1,900 while attendance on other days stayed nearly the same, falling only from 3,200 to 3,150.\",\"option_c\":\"at the City History Museum, Sunday attendance in 2023 was 1,400, nearly three times its 2021 level.\",\"option_d\":\"at all four museums, attendance on days other than Sunday was lower in 2023 than in 2021.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"To show that free Sundays attracted new visitors rather than shifting existing ones, the data must show that Sunday attendance rose without a matching drop on other days. Choice B does this: at the Museum of Textiles, Sundays gained 1,300 visitors while other days lost only 50. Choice A shows the opposite pattern: the Natural History Museum's Sunday gain of 1,100 was matched by a loss of 1,100 on other days, just as the critics predicted. Choice C reports a Sunday increase but says nothing about other days, so it cannot rule out a shift in visits. Choice D describes declines on other days, which, if anything, supports the critics' view.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bepul yakshanbalar mavjud tashrif buyuruvchilarni boshqa kunlardan shunchaki ko‘chirmasdan, yangi mehmonlarni jalb qilganini ko‘rsatish uchun ma’lumotlar yakshanbadagi o‘sish boshqa kunlardagi shunga teng kamayish bilan qoplanmaganini ko‘rsatishi kerak. B javob aynan shunday: to‘qimachilik muzeyida (Museum of Textiles) yakshanba kunlari 1,300 ta mehmon qo‘shilgan, boshqa kunlarda esa atigi 50 taga kamaygan. A teskari manzarani ko‘rsatadi: tabiat tarixi muzeyida (Natural History Museum) yakshanbadagi 1,100 talik o‘sish boshqa kunlardagi 1,100 talik kamayish bilan teng — tanqidchilar aynan shuni bashorat qilgan. C yakshanbadagi o‘sishni ko‘rsatadi, ammo boshqa kunlar haqida hech narsa aytmaydi, shuning uchun tashriflar shunchaki ko‘chgan bo‘lishi ehtimolini istisno qila olmaydi. D boshqa kunlardagi kamayishni tasvirlaydi — bu, aksincha, tanqidchilar fikrini qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Each autumn, gray squirrels in Ardley Forest bury acorns in the ground and dig many of them up during the winter. Ecologist Samir Haddad hypothesizes that the squirrels adjust this behavior to the size of the acorn crop, burying more acorns in years when acorns are plentiful.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Haddad's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"Squirrels in Ardley Forest eat pine seeds as well as acorns.\",\"option_b\":\"The size of the acorn crop in Ardley Forest varies greatly from year to year.\",\"option_c\":\"Squirrels in a nearby forest bury acorns in the same spots each year.\",\"option_d\":\"Squirrels in Ardley Forest buried far more acorns in years with large acorn crops than in years with small ones.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Haddad's hypothesis links two things: the size of the acorn crop and the number of acorns the squirrels bury. Choice D shows exactly that link, with far more acorns buried in years with larger crops. Choice A concerns the squirrels' diet, not their burying. Choice B shows that crop size varies but says nothing about how the squirrels respond. Choice C concerns a different forest and where squirrels bury acorns, not how many they bury.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Haddad gipotezasi ikki narsani bog‘laydi: eman yong‘og‘i (acorn) hosilining hajmi va olmaxonlar ko‘madigan yong‘oqlar soni. D javob aynan shu bog‘liqlikni ko‘rsatadi: hosil katta bo‘lgan yillarda ancha ko‘p yong‘oq ko‘milgan. A olmaxonlarning ozuqasi haqida, ko‘mish haqida emas. B hosil hajmi o‘zgarib turishini ko‘rsatadi, lekin olmaxonlar bunga qanday javob berishini aytmaydi. C boshqa o‘rmon va yong‘oqlar qayerga ko‘milishi haqida, nechta ko‘milishi haqida emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"*The Ferryman's Son* is a 1958 novel by Arlo Penhallow. In the novel, the narrator recalls that his father rarely spoke about his feelings but showed his love through quiet acts of care.\",\"stem\":\"Which quotation from *The Ferryman's Son* most effectively illustrates the claim?\",\"option_a\":\"“My father knew every current in the river and could read the coming weather in the color of the water.”\",\"option_b\":\"“He never once told me he was proud of me, but every winter morning he rose before dawn to warm my boots by the stove.”\",\"option_c\":\"“The ferry carried farmers, merchants and, one summer, an entire traveling circus across the river.”\",\"option_d\":\"“When I was twelve, I made up my mind that I would never become a ferryman.”\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The claim has two parts: the father rarely spoke about his feelings, and he showed love through quiet acts of care. Choice B illustrates both: he “never once told” his son that he was proud of him, yet he rose before dawn to warm his son's boots. Choice A shows the father's skill, not his affection. Choice C describes the ferry's passengers. Choice D describes the narrator's own decision, not his father's behavior.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Da’vo ikki qismdan iborat: ota o‘z his-tuyg‘ulari haqida kam gapirgan va mehrini sokin g‘amxo‘rlik orqali ko‘rsatgan. B javob ikkalasini ham ko‘rsatadi: u o‘g‘liga u bilan faxrlanishini “hech qachon aytmagan”, lekin har qish tongida uning etigini isitish uchun saharda turgan. A otaning mahoratini ko‘rsatadi, mehrini emas. C parom yo‘lovchilarini tasvirlaydi. D otaning xatti-harakatini emas, hikoyachining o‘z qarorini tasvirlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Many students listen to music while they study. Psychologist Leila Moradi hypothesizes that songs with lyrics make it harder to memorize written information than instrumental music does, because the words in the songs compete for the same mental resources that reading requires.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Moradi's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"Students who studied a list of words while hearing songs with lyrics later recalled fewer words than students who studied while hearing instrumental versions of the same songs.\",\"option_b\":\"Students reported that they enjoyed songs with lyrics more than instrumental music.\",\"option_c\":\"Students who studied in silence recalled about as many words as students who heard instrumental music.\",\"option_d\":\"Students who heard songs with lyrics spent more time studying than students who heard instrumental music.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Moradi's hypothesis compares songs with lyrics and instrumental music in terms of how well people memorize written information. Choice A makes exactly that comparison, using the same songs with and without lyrics, and shows worse recall with lyrics. Choice B concerns enjoyment, not memory. Choice C compares silence with instrumental music and leaves out songs with lyrics. Choice D concerns study time, not how much students remembered.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Moradi gipotezasi yozma ma’lumotni yodlashda so‘zli qo‘shiqlarni cholg‘u musiqasi bilan solishtiradi. A javob aynan shu taqqoslashni — bir xil qo‘shiqlarning so‘zli va so‘zsiz variantlarini — qiladi va so‘zli qo‘shiq tinglaganlar kamroq so‘z eslab qolganini ko‘rsatadi. B yodlash haqida emas, yoqtirish haqida. C jimjitlikni cholg‘u musiqasi bilan solishtiradi, so‘zli qo‘shiqlar esa chetda qoladi. D qancha eslab qolish haqida emas, o‘qishga sarflangan vaqt haqida.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Many ancient sites in the Tarsen Valley contain large piles of seashells, even though the valley lies more than 100 kilometers from the coast. Archaeologist Petra Lund hypothesizes that valley residents obtained the shells by trading with coastal communities rather than by traveling to the coast to collect the shells themselves.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly weaken Lund's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"The shells in the valley belong to species found along the stretch of coast nearest to the valley.\",\"option_b\":\"Coastal sites from the same period contain stone tools made from a type of rock found only in the Tarsen Valley.\",\"option_c\":\"Chemical analysis of the teeth of people buried in the valley shows that many of them spent part of each year living on the coast.\",\"option_d\":\"Some of the shells found in the valley had been carved into beads and other ornaments.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Lund claims that valley residents obtained shells through trade rather than by traveling to the coast. Choice C weakens this claim by showing that many valley residents themselves spent time living on the coast, which makes it more likely that they collected the shells. Choice A fits both explanations, since traders or travelers could have brought shells from the nearest coast. Choice B actually supports Lund, since valley rock reaching the coast suggests trade between the two areas. Choice D describes what the shells were used for, not how they were obtained.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Lundning fikricha, vodiy aholisi chig‘anoqlarni sohilga borib emas, savdo orqali olgan. C javob bu gipotezani zaiflashtiradi: vodiy aholisining ko‘pchiligi har yili bir muddat sohilda yashagan bo‘lsa, ular chig‘anoqlarni o‘zlari terib kelgan bo‘lishi ehtimoli oshadi. A ikkala izohga ham mos: chig‘anoqlarni eng yaqin sohildan savdogarlar ham, sayohatchilar ham olib kelishi mumkin. B aslida Lundni qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi: faqat vodiyda uchraydigan toshning sohilga yetib borishi ikki hudud o‘rtasida savdo bo‘lganini ko‘rsatadi. D chig‘anoqlar nima uchun ishlatilganini ko‘rsatadi, qanday olinganini emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"“Night Train” is a 1934 poem by Wendell Ames. In the poem, the speaker, who is traveling alone by train at night, portrays the towns the train passes as places of warmth and family life that the speaker can observe but never share.\",\"stem\":\"Which quotation from “Night Train” most effectively illustrates the claim?\",\"option_a\":\"“The engine hums a low, unending note / that settles in the floorboards and the seats.”\",\"option_b\":\"“By dawn we'll reach the city by the bay, / where gulls wheel low above the fishing boats.”\",\"option_c\":\"“The conductor nods and punches every ticket / with the same small click he's made for twenty years.”\",\"option_d\":\"“Each lighted window in each passing town / holds out a supper I will never sit down to.”\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The claim is that the speaker sees the passing towns as places of warmth and family life that he or she can observe but not share. Choice D fits: the “lighted window” in each town suggests a warm home, and “a supper I will never sit down to” shows that the speaker can only look on from outside. Choice A describes the sound of the train. Choice B describes the journey's destination, not the towns the train passes along the way. Choice C describes the conductor's routine.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Da’voga ko‘ra, so‘zlovchi o‘tib ketayotgan shaharchalarni o‘zi kuzatishi mumkin, lekin hech qachon qatnasha olmaydigan iliq oilaviy hayot maskanlari sifatida tasvirlaydi. D javob bunga mos: har bir shaharchadagi “lighted window” (yoritilgan deraza) iliq xonadonni bildiradi, “a supper I will never sit down to” (hech qachon dasturxoniga o‘tirmaydigan kechki ovqat) esa so‘zlovchi faqat chetdan qarab turishini ko‘rsatadi. A poyezd ovozini tasvirlaydi. B yo‘l davomidagi shaharchalarni emas, safarning manzilini tasvirlaydi. C konduktorning odatiy ishini tasvirlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Sociologist Daniel Achebe hypothesizes that people who live in apartment buildings with shared courtyards get to know more of their neighbors than people who live in buildings without such spaces do, because courtyards create frequent chances for casual encounters.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Achebe's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"Residents of buildings with courtyards are, on average, older than residents of buildings without courtyards.\",\"option_b\":\"Residents of buildings with courtyards could name about twice as many neighbors as residents of similar buildings without courtyards could, and they most often said they had met those neighbors in the courtyard.\",\"option_c\":\"Most residents of buildings without courtyards said they would prefer to live in a building with one.\",\"option_d\":\"Buildings with courtyards cost more to maintain than buildings without courtyards do.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Achebe's hypothesis has two parts: residents of buildings with courtyards know more of their neighbors, and casual encounters in the courtyards are the reason. Choice B supports both parts: these residents could name about twice as many neighbors, and they usually met those neighbors in the courtyard. Choice A points to an age difference, which does not show that residents know more neighbors and could even suggest a different explanation. Choice C concerns residents' preferences, not how many neighbors they know. Choice D concerns maintenance costs, which are irrelevant to the hypothesis.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Achebe gipotezasi ikki qismdan iborat: hovlili binolar aholisi ko‘proq qo‘shnini taniydi va buning sababi — hovlidagi tasodifiy uchrashuvlar. B javob ikkala qismni ham qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi: bunday binolar aholisi taxminan ikki baravar ko‘p qo‘shnining ismini ayta olgan va ular bilan asosan hovlida tanishgan. A yosh farqini ko‘rsatadi — bu aholining ko‘proq qo‘shnini tanishini isbotlamaydi va hatto boshqa izohga ishora qilishi mumkin. C aholining xohishi haqida, nechta qo‘shnini tanishi haqida emas. D binoni saqlash xarajatlari haqida, bu gipotezaga aloqasiz.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"*The Glass Orchard* is a 1962 novel by Theodora Quill. In the novel, Edwin Marsh, a wealthy landowner, considers himself generous toward the workers on his estate, but the narrator suggests that Edwin's generosity is really a way of reminding the workers how much they depend on him.\",\"stem\":\"Which quotation from *The Glass Orchard* most effectively illustrates the narrator's suggestion?\",\"option_a\":\"“Each winter Edwin handed out the new coats himself, and he would not move on to the next worker until the last had thanked him and remarked, as was expected, how fortunate they all were to have such a master.”\",\"option_b\":\"“Edwin paid his workers more than any other landowner in the county, a fact he regarded as nothing more than sensible business.”\",\"option_c\":\"“The workers spoke of Edwin with genuine fondness, and more than one family had named a son after him.”\",\"option_d\":\"“Edwin had inherited the estate at twenty-three and had doubled its size within a decade.”\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The narrator suggests that Edwin's generosity serves to remind the workers of their dependence on him. In choice A, Edwin gives out coats but insists on being thanked and on hearing each worker say how “fortunate” they are to have “such a master,” turning his gift into a reminder of their dependence. Choice B shows generosity, but Edwin regards it as “sensible business,” not as a way to make the workers feel dependent. Choice C shows the workers' affection for Edwin, which does not illustrate the narrator's suggestion. Choice D concerns Edwin's wealth, not his generosity.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Hikoyachining fikricha, Edwinning saxovati ishchilarga ular unga qanchalik qaram ekanini eslatish vositasi. A javobda Edwin paltolarni o‘zi tarqatadi, lekin har bir ishchi unga rahmat aytishini va “shunday xo‘jayinga ega bo‘lganidan baxtli” (“fortunate”) ekanini aytishini kutadi — sovg‘a qaramlikni eslatishga aylanadi. B saxovatni ko‘rsatadi, ammo Edwin buni ishchilarni qaram his qildirish usuli emas, oddiy “sensible business” (oqilona ish yuritish) deb biladi. C ishchilarning Edwinga bo‘lgan mehrini ko‘rsatadi, bu hikoyachining fikrini tasvirlamaydi. D Edwinning boyligi haqida, saxovati haqida emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Fossils of *Velocia minor*, a small feathered dinosaur, show long feathers on its forelimbs. Some paleontologists think these feathers helped the animal glide between trees. Paleontologist Rhea Castillo disagrees, hypothesizing that the forelimb feathers evolved mainly for display, helping individuals attract mates.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Castillo's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"The forelimb feathers of *V. minor* were longer than the feathers on its tail.\",\"option_b\":\"Several dinosaurs closely related to *V. minor* also had feathered forelimbs.\",\"option_c\":\"The long forelimb feathers appear in fossils of adult *V. minor* but not in fossils of young individuals, and their shape would have produced too little lift for gliding.\",\"option_d\":\"Fossils of *V. minor* have been found only in rock layers that formed in dense forests with tall trees.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Castillo argues that the feathers evolved for attracting mates rather than for gliding. Choice C supports this in two ways: feathers that appear only in adults fit a role in mating, since young animals do not mate, and feathers that could not produce enough lift argue against the gliding explanation. Choice A compares feather lengths without connecting them to either display or gliding. Choice B shows that related species had similar feathers but not what the feathers were for. Choice D, if anything, supports the competing gliding explanation, since gliding between trees requires tall trees.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Castilloning fikricha, patlar havoda sirpanib uchish uchun emas, juft jalb qilish uchun paydo bo‘lgan. C javob buni ikki jihatdan qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi: patlarning faqat voyaga yetgan hayvonlarda uchrashi ularning juftlashishdagi roliga mos keladi, chunki yosh hayvonlar juftlashmaydi; patlarning yetarli ko‘tarish kuchi bermasligi esa sirpanib uchish haqidagi izohga qarshi dalil. A patlar uzunligini solishtiradi, lekin buni na ko‘z-ko‘z qilish (display), na sirpanib uchish bilan bog‘laydi. B qarindosh turlarda ham shunday patlar bo‘lganini ko‘rsatadi, ammo ular nima uchun kerak bo‘lganini emas. D aksincha, raqib izoh — sirpanib uchishni qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi, chunki daraxtlar orasida sirpanish uchun baland daraxtlar kerak.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nMany nutrition guides advise people to eat breakfast every day, warning that skipping it leads to weight gain. Dietitian Sara Holm argues that a morning meal reduces hunger later in the day and so helps people avoid overeating.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nResearcher Kenji Watanabe assigned adults either to eat breakfast every day or to skip it for sixteen weeks. At the end of the study, weight changes in the two groups were nearly identical. Watanabe concludes that, for weight control, the total amount people eat each day matters more than when they eat it.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Watanabe (Text 2) most likely respond to the warning described in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"He would agree with it, since the people in his study who skipped breakfast gained more weight.\",\"option_b\":\"He would question it, since his study found that skipping breakfast did not lead to more weight gain than eating breakfast did.\",\"option_c\":\"He would argue that it applies only to people who eat very large breakfasts.\",\"option_d\":\"He would claim that skipping breakfast causes people to eat less over the course of a day.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Text 1 describes the warning that skipping breakfast leads to weight gain. In Watanabe's study, people who skipped breakfast and people who ate it had “nearly identical” weight changes, so he would question the warning, as choice B says. Choice A contradicts his results. Choice C is unsupported: Text 2 says nothing about the size of breakfasts. Choice D goes beyond Text 2, which concludes only that total daily intake matters more than meal timing; it does not say that skipping breakfast reduces how much people eat.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Text 1 da nonushtani o‘tkazib yuborish vazn ortishiga olib keladi degan ogohlantirish keltiriladi. Watanabe tadqiqotida esa nonushta qilganlar va qilmaganlarning vazni deyarli bir xil (“nearly identical”) o‘zgargan. Demak, u bu ogohlantirishga shubha bildirardi — to‘g‘ri javob B. A uning natijalariga zid. C asossiz: Text 2 da nonushtaning hajmi haqida gap yo‘q. D Text 2 doirasidan chiqib ketadi: unda faqat kunlik umumiy ovqat miqdori ovqatlanish vaqtidan muhimroq ekani aytilgan, nonushtani o‘tkazib yuborish kamroq ovqatlanishga olib kelishi aytilmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nHistorian Lucia Ferro argues that the printing press transformed European science mainly by making books cheaper. Once scholars could afford their own copies of important works, she writes, they could study those works closely at home instead of traveling to distant libraries.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nHistorian Tomasz Wieland agrees that printing was crucial to the growth of European science but stresses a different effect. Copying by hand introduced errors into diagrams and tables, so no two manuscripts were exactly alike. Printing gave scholars in different cities identical copies, making it easier for them to compare and correct one another's work.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, Ferro (Text 1) and Wieland (Text 2) would most likely agree with which statement?\",\"option_a\":\"Printed books remained too expensive for most scholars to own.\",\"option_b\":\"The most important effect of printing was that it made libraries unnecessary.\",\"option_c\":\"Hand-copied manuscripts were generally as accurate as printed books.\",\"option_d\":\"The printing press played an important role in the development of European science.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Ferro says printing “transformed European science,” and Wieland “agrees that printing was crucial to the growth of European science,” though the two emphasize different reasons. Both would therefore accept choice D. Choice A contradicts Ferro, who argues that printing made books affordable. Choice B is wrong because neither author says libraries became unnecessary; Ferro says only that scholars no longer had to travel to them. Choice C contradicts Wieland, who says hand copying introduced errors.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ferro kitob bosish Yevropa ilmini “tubdan o‘zgartirgan”ini aytadi, Wieland esa kitob bosish ilm rivoji uchun “juda muhim” bo‘lganiga qo‘shiladi, garchi ular turli sabablarni ta’kidlasa ham. Demak, ikkalasi ham D fikriga rozi bo‘ladi. A Ferroning fikriga zid: u kitob bosish kitoblarni arzonlashtirganini ta’kidlaydi. B noto‘g‘ri: hech bir muallif kutubxonalar keraksiz bo‘lib qolganini aytmagan; Ferro faqat olimlar endi ularga uzoq yo‘l bosishi shart bo‘lmay qolganini aytadi. C Wielandning fikriga zid: uning so‘zlariga ko‘ra, qo‘lda ko‘chirish xatolarga olib kelgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nMany educators believe that people learn a second language best when they start as young children. Linguist Hamid Rahimov notes that children who move to a new country usually develop a more native-like accent than adults who make the same move.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nPsychologist Ruth Okafor compared adults and children taking the same twelve-week language course. The adults learned new vocabulary and grammar rules faster than the children did, likely because adults can use study strategies such as taking notes. Okafor argues that an early start is not the only path to success in a new language.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Okafor (Text 2) most likely respond to the educators' belief described in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"She would argue that the belief overlooks evidence that adults can learn some parts of a language faster than children can.\",\"option_b\":\"She would agree that children learn vocabulary and grammar faster than adults do.\",\"option_c\":\"She would argue that accent is the most important part of learning a language.\",\"option_d\":\"She would reject the idea that children ever develop more native-like accents than adults do.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The educators in Text 1 believe that young children learn languages best. Okafor found that adults in her course learned vocabulary and grammar faster than children, and she argues that starting early is “not the only path to success.” She would therefore say the belief overlooks adults' advantages in some areas, as choice A says. Choice B contradicts her findings. Choice C is unsupported: Okafor does not discuss accent at all. Choice D is too extreme: Text 2 never addresses accents, so there is no reason to think Okafor would reject Rahimov's observation.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Text 1 dagi pedagoglar tilni eng yaxshi yosh bolalar o‘rganadi deb hisoblaydi. Okafor esa o‘z kursida kattalar so‘z va grammatikani bolalardan tezroq o‘rganganini aniqlagan va erta boshlash muvaffaqiyatning “yagona yo‘li emas”ligini ta’kidlaydi. Demak, u bu qarash kattalarning ayrim sohalardagi ustunligini e’tiborga olmaydi, deb aytardi — to‘g‘ri javob A. B uning natijalariga zid. C asossiz: Okafor talaffuz haqida umuman gapirmaydi. D haddan tashqari kuchli: Text 2 da talaffuz muhokama qilinmaydi, shuning uchun Okafor Rahimovning kuzatuvini rad etadi deyishga asos yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nAt the ancient settlement of Tel Varo, archaeologists found hundreds of small bone pieces carved into cones, disks and spheres. Archaeologist Nadia Brenner argues that the pieces were used in a board game, noting that dozens of them were found beside a stone slab carved with rows of shallow hollows.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nArchaeologist Idris Kamal points out that most of the Tel Varo pieces were found not near the stone slab but in storerooms, and that the number of pieces of each shape in a room closely matches the number of jars of a particular good, such as oil or grain, stored there. Kamal argues that the pieces were most likely used to keep records of stored goods.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Kamal (Text 2) most likely respond to Brenner's argument in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"He would agree that the stone slab proves the pieces were used in a game.\",\"option_b\":\"He would argue that the pieces were made much later than Brenner assumes.\",\"option_c\":\"He would argue that Brenner's evidence does not account for the pattern found in the storerooms, which points to a different use for the pieces.\",\"option_d\":\"He would claim that the pieces were brought to Tel Varo from another settlement.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Brenner bases her game theory on pieces found beside a carved slab. Kamal notes that most pieces were actually found in storerooms, where their numbers match the stored jars, and concludes that they were used for record keeping. He would therefore say that Brenner's evidence ignores the storeroom pattern, as choice C says. Choice A contradicts Kamal's conclusion. Choices B and D are unsupported: neither text discusses when the pieces were made or where they came from.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Brenner o‘yin haqidagi nazariyasini o‘yilgan tosh plita yonidan topilgan buyumlarga asoslaydi. Kamal esa buyumlarning ko‘pchiligi aslida omborxonalardan topilganini va ularning soni u yerdagi ko‘zalar soniga mos kelishini ta’kidlab, ular hisob yuritish uchun ishlatilgan degan xulosaga keladi. Demak, u Brennerning dalili omborxonalardagi qonuniyatni hisobga olmaydi, deb aytardi — to‘g‘ri javob C. A Kamalning xulosasiga zid. B va D asossiz: hech bir matnda buyumlar qachon yasalgani yoki qayerdan keltirilgani muhokama qilinmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nAfter lynx were reintroduced to the Merrow Highlands in 2005, the number of hares there fell sharply, and young birch trees, which hares eat, began to grow back. Ecologist Ana Vidal argues that the lynx caused this recovery: by hunting hares, they reduced the pressure on young trees.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nEcologist Pavel Orlov agrees that hare numbers fell after 2005 but notes that the region also had several unusually snowy winters during those years. Deep snow makes it hard for hares to reach food and can greatly increase their death rate. Orlov argues that until the effects of the lynx and the winters are separated, the cause of the birch recovery remains uncertain.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Orlov (Text 2) most likely respond to Vidal's argument in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"He would reject her claim that the number of hares declined after 2005.\",\"option_b\":\"He would argue that the birch trees recovered because lynx protect them from other animals.\",\"option_c\":\"He would agree that the lynx were clearly the only cause of the birch recovery.\",\"option_d\":\"He would caution that her conclusion may be premature because another factor could also explain the decline in hares.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Vidal credits the lynx with reducing the hare population and thus allowing birches to recover. Orlov accepts that hares declined but points to snowy winters as another possible cause and says the cause of the recovery “remains uncertain.” He would therefore see her conclusion as premature, as choice D says. Choice A is wrong because Orlov “agrees that hare numbers fell.” Choice B is unsupported: neither text says that lynx protect trees from other animals. Choice C contradicts Orlov's view that the cause is uncertain.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Vidal quyonlar kamayishi va qayinlar qayta o‘sishini silovsinlarga bog‘laydi. Orlov quyonlar kamayganiga qo‘shiladi, lekin boshqa mumkin bo‘lgan sabab — qor ko‘p yoqqan qishlarni ko‘rsatadi va qayinlar tiklanishining sababi “hali noaniq” deydi. Demak, u Vidalning xulosasini shoshilinch deb hisoblaydi — to‘g‘ri javob D. A noto‘g‘ri: Orlov quyonlar soni kamayganiga “qo‘shiladi”. B asossiz: hech bir matnda silovsinlar daraxtlarni boshqa hayvonlardan himoya qilishi aytilmagan. C Orlovning sabab noaniq degan fikriga zid.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nCritics often praise the novels of Elena Morvay for their detailed descriptions of village life. According to critic Jonas Petric, Morvay's careful attention to farming, cooking and local customs is valuable mainly as a historical record of a way of life that has since disappeared.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nCritic Amara Diallo argues that reading Morvay's novels as historical records misses their real achievement. The detailed descriptions, Diallo contends, are not there for their own sake: Morvay uses them to reveal her characters' inner lives, as when the way a woman kneads bread betrays her grief more clearly than any dialogue could.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Diallo (Text 2) most likely respond to Petric's view in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"She would argue that Petric undervalues the role that Morvay's descriptions play in revealing her characters' feelings.\",\"option_b\":\"She would agree that the descriptions are valuable mainly as a record of village life.\",\"option_c\":\"She would claim that Morvay's descriptions of village life are historically inaccurate.\",\"option_d\":\"She would argue that Morvay's novels should include more dialogue.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Petric values Morvay's descriptions “mainly as a historical record.” Diallo says that reading the novels this way “misses their real achievement,” because the descriptions reveal the characters' inner lives. She would therefore say that Petric overlooks this role, as choice A says. Choice B contradicts Diallo's position. Choice C is unsupported: Diallo never questions the descriptions' accuracy. Choice D misreads her example: she says a description can reveal grief more clearly than dialogue could, which praises the descriptions rather than calling for more dialogue.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Petric Morvayning tasvirlarini “asosan tarixiy hujjat sifatida” qadrlaydi. Diallo esa romanlarni bunday o‘qish ularning “asl yutug‘ini e’tibordan chetda qoldiradi”, chunki tasvirlar qahramonlarning ichki dunyosini ochib beradi, deydi. Demak, u Petric tasvirlarning bu vazifasini yetarlicha baholamaydi, deb aytardi — to‘g‘ri javob A. B Diallo pozitsiyasiga zid. C asossiz: Diallo tasvirlarning aniqligiga shubha bildirmaydi. D uning misolini noto‘g‘ri tushunadi: u tasvir qayg‘uni har qanday dialogdan aniqroq ko‘rsata olishini aytadi — bu tasvirlarga maqtov, ko‘proq dialog kerak degan talab emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nCities facing hotter summers are planting trees along streets to cool neighborhoods. In a study led by climate scientist Iris Lindqvist, streets with dense tree canopies were on average 3°C cooler at midday than nearby streets without trees. Lindqvist recommends that cities plant dense rows of street trees in their hottest districts.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nResearcher Bakhtiyor Ergashev agrees that street trees cool cities during the day. But in narrow streets lined with tall buildings, his measurements showed that dense canopies can trap heat near the ground at night, keeping those streets warmer after sunset than similar streets without trees. Because nighttime heat is especially harmful to health, he argues that trees in such streets should be spaced to leave gaps through which heat can escape.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Ergashev (Text 2) most likely respond to Lindqvist's recommendation in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"He would reject it, since his measurements show that street trees do not lower daytime temperatures.\",\"option_b\":\"He would accept it without reservation, since dense canopies keep streets cooler both during the day and at night.\",\"option_c\":\"He would support planting street trees but caution that, in some streets, dense rows of trees could make nights hotter.\",\"option_d\":\"He would argue that cities should stop planting street trees and focus only on reducing nighttime heat.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Lindqvist recommends planting “dense rows” of street trees. Ergashev agrees that trees cool streets during the day, but he found that dense canopies in narrow streets lined with tall buildings can trap heat at night, so he wants trees in such streets spaced with gaps. He would therefore support tree planting while warning that dense planting may raise nighttime temperatures in some streets, as choice C says. Choice A contradicts his agreement that trees cool cities during the day. Choice B contradicts his finding about nighttime heat. Choice D is too extreme: he recommends spacing trees differently, not ending tree planting.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Lindqvist ko‘chalarga “zich qatorlarda” daraxt ekishni tavsiya qiladi. Ergashev daraxtlar kunduzi ko‘chalarni salqinlatishiga qo‘shiladi, lekin baland binolar bilan o‘ralgan tor ko‘chalarda zich daraxt soyaboni kechasi issiqni ushlab qolishini aniqlagan; shuning uchun u bunday ko‘chalarda daraxtlarni oraliq qoldirib ekishni taklif qiladi. Demak, u daraxt ekishni qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi, ammo ba’zi ko‘chalarda zich ekish tunlarni issiqroq qilishi mumkinligidan ogohlantiradi — to‘g‘ri javob C. A uning daraxtlar kunduzi salqinlatadi degan fikriga zid. B uning tungi issiqlik haqidagi topilmasiga zid. D haddan tashqari kuchli: u daraxt ekishni to‘xtatishni emas, daraxtlarni boshqacha joylashtirishni taklif qiladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nMany accounts portray the astronomer Leonor Castell (1803–1871) as a solitary genius who made her discoveries working alone at her private observatory. This portrayal relies largely on Castell's published papers, each of which lists her as the only author.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nHistorian Farhod Yusupov studied the letters Castell exchanged with more than forty correspondents, including amateur astronomers, instrument makers and members of her household staff. The letters show that many of her observations were checked, and some were first made, by these helpers. Yusupov notes that in the 1800s, the list of authors on a scientific paper often left out the people whose work the paper depended on.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Yusupov (Text 2) most likely respond to the portrayal of Castell described in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"He would agree with it, since Castell's published papers name her as their only author.\",\"option_b\":\"He would argue that it relies on a kind of evidence that can hide the contributions others made to Castell's work.\",\"option_c\":\"He would claim that Castell's discoveries were in fact made entirely by her household staff.\",\"option_d\":\"He would argue that it accurately describes Castell's early work but not her later work.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Text 1 says the “solitary genius” portrayal rests mainly on Castell's papers listing her as the only author. Yusupov's letters show that others checked and sometimes made her observations, and he notes that author lists of that era often left out contributors. He would therefore argue that the portrayal depends on a type of evidence (author lists) that can conceal others' contributions, as choice B says. Choice A is wrong because Yusupov's point is precisely that such author lists can mislead. Choice C is too extreme: the letters show that some observations were first made by helpers, not that all of her discoveries were. Choice D is unsupported: neither text distinguishes between earlier and later periods of Castell's career.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Text 1 ga ko‘ra, Castellni “yolg‘iz daho” sifatida ko‘rsatish asosan uning maqolalarida yagona muallif sifatida ko‘rsatilganiga tayanadi. Yusupov o‘rgangan maktublar esa uning kuzatuvlarini boshqalar tekshirganini, ba’zilarini esa birinchi bo‘lib boshqalar qilganini ko‘rsatadi; u o‘sha davrda mualliflar ro‘yxati ko‘pincha hissa qo‘shgan odamlarni tushirib qoldirganini ham ta’kidlaydi. Demak, u bu tasvir boshqalarning hissasini yashirishi mumkin bo‘lgan dalil turiga — mualliflar ro‘yxatiga — tayanadi, deb aytardi. To‘g‘ri javob — B. A noto‘g‘ri: Yusupovning asosiy fikri aynan shunday mualliflar ro‘yxati chalg‘itishi mumkinligi. C haddan tashqari kuchli: maktublar ba’zi kuzatuvlarni yordamchilar birinchi qilganini ko‘rsatadi, barcha kashfiyotlarni emas. D asossiz: hech bir matnda Castell faoliyatining erta va keyingi davrlari ajratilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which expression is equivalent to $3(2x - 5) - 4(x - 1)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$2x - 19$\",\"option_b\":\"$2x - 11$\",\"option_c\":\"$2x - 1$\",\"option_d\":\"$10x - 11$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Distribute each factor: $3(2x - 5) = 6x - 15$ and $-4(x - 1) = -4x + 4$.\\n\\nCombine like terms: $6x - 15 - 4x + 4 = 2x - 11$.\\n\\nChoice A multiplies $-4$ by $-1$ and gets $-4$ instead of $+4$, giving $6x - 15 - 4x - 4 = 2x - 19$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir qavsni ochamiz: $3(2x - 5) = 6x - 15$ va $-4(x - 1) = -4x + 4$.\\n\\nO‘xshash hadlarni ixchamlaymiz: $6x - 15 - 4x + 4 = 2x - 11$.\\n\\nA variant — $-4$ ni $-1$ ga ko‘paytirib, $+4$ o‘rniga $-4$ olish natijasi: $6x - 15 - 4x - 4 = 2x - 19$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which expression is equivalent to $(3x - 4)(x + 2)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$3x^2 - 8$\",\"option_b\":\"$3x^2 - 2x - 8$\",\"option_c\":\"$3x^2 + 2x - 8$\",\"option_d\":\"$3x^2 + 10x - 8$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Multiply each term of the first binomial by each term of the second: $3x \\\\cdot x + 3x \\\\cdot 2 - 4 \\\\cdot x - 4 \\\\cdot 2 = 3x^2 + 6x - 4x - 8$.\\n\\nCombine the middle terms: $3x^2 + 2x - 8$.\\n\\nChoice A multiplies only the first terms and the last terms, leaving out the middle terms $6x$ and $-4x$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi ikkihadning har bir hadini ikkinchisining har bir hadiga ko‘paytiramiz: $3x \\\\cdot x + 3x \\\\cdot 2 - 4 \\\\cdot x - 4 \\\\cdot 2 = 3x^2 + 6x - 4x - 8$.\\n\\nO‘rta hadlarni birlashtiramiz: $3x^2 + 2x - 8$.\\n\\nA variantda faqat birinchi hadlar va oxirgi hadlar ko‘paytirilgan, o‘rta hadlar $6x$ va $-4x$ tushib qolgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"If $\\\\dfrac{x^a \\\\cdot x^5}{x^2} = x^{10}$ for all positive values of $x$, what is the value of $a$?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{12}{5}$\",\"option_b\":\"$3$\",\"option_c\":\"$4$\",\"option_d\":\"$7$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"When multiplying powers with the same base, add the exponents; when dividing, subtract them: $\\\\frac{x^a \\\\cdot x^5}{x^2} = x^{a + 5 - 2} = x^{a + 3}$.\\n\\nSo $a + 3 = 10$, and $a = 7$.\\n\\nChoice B adds the exponent of the denominator instead of subtracting it: $a + 5 + 2 = 10$ gives $a = 3$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Asoslari bir xil darajalarni ko‘paytirganda ko‘rsatkichlar qo‘shiladi, bo‘lganda esa ayiriladi: $\\\\frac{x^a \\\\cdot x^5}{x^2} = x^{a + 5 - 2} = x^{a + 3}$.\\n\\nDemak $a + 3 = 10$ va $a = 7$.\\n\\nB variant maxrajdagi ko‘rsatkichni ayirish o‘rniga qo‘shadi: $a + 5 + 2 = 10$, bundan $a = 3$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following is a factor of $6x^2 + x - 15$?\",\"option_a\":\"$2x - 3$\",\"option_b\":\"$2x + 3$\",\"option_c\":\"$3x - 5$\",\"option_d\":\"$6x - 5$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Factor by grouping. Find two numbers whose product is $6(-15) = -90$ and whose sum is $1$: they are $10$ and $-9$.\\n\\nSo $6x^2 + x - 15 = 6x^2 + 10x - 9x - 15 = 2x(3x + 5) - 3(3x + 5) = (2x - 3)(3x + 5)$. Therefore $2x - 3$ is a factor.\\n\\nCheck: $(2x - 3)(3x + 5) = 6x^2 + 10x - 9x - 15 = 6x^2 + x - 15$.\\n\\nChoices B and C are the factors of $6x^2 - x - 15 = (2x + 3)(3x - 5)$; they come from mixing up the signs, which flips the sign of the middle term.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Guruhlash usulidan foydalanamiz. Ko‘paytmasi $6(-15) = -90$, yig‘indisi $1$ bo‘lgan ikki son: $10$ va $-9$.\\n\\nDemak $6x^2 + x - 15 = 6x^2 + 10x - 9x - 15 = 2x(3x + 5) - 3(3x + 5) = (2x - 3)(3x + 5)$. Shunday qilib, $2x - 3$ — ko‘paytuvchi.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $(2x - 3)(3x + 5) = 6x^2 + 10x - 9x - 15 = 6x^2 + x - 15$.\\n\\nB va C variantlar $6x^2 - x - 15 = (2x + 3)(3x - 5)$ ifodaning ko‘paytuvchilari: ishoralar almashib ketganda o‘rta hadning ishorasi ham o‘zgaradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"For $x \\\\ne -5$, the expression $\\\\dfrac{x^2 - 2x - 35}{x + 5}$ is equivalent to $x + k$, where $k$ is a constant. What is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"-7\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Factor the numerator. Two numbers whose product is $-35$ and whose sum is $-2$ are $-7$ and $5$, so $x^2 - 2x - 35 = (x - 7)(x + 5)$.\\n\\nThen $\\\\frac{(x - 7)(x + 5)}{x + 5} = x - 7$ for $x \\\\ne -5$. Matching $x - 7$ with $x + k$ gives $k = -7$.\\n\\nEntering $7$ is a common sign error: the expression is $x - 7$, so $k$ is negative.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Suratni ko‘paytuvchilarga ajratamiz. Ko‘paytmasi $-35$, yig‘indisi $-2$ bo‘lgan ikki son: $-7$ va $5$. Demak $x^2 - 2x - 35 = (x - 7)(x + 5)$.\\n\\nU holda $x \\\\ne -5$ da $\\\\frac{(x - 7)(x + 5)}{x + 5} = x - 7$. $x - 7$ ni $x + k$ bilan solishtirib, $k = -7$ ni olamiz.\\n\\n$7$ ni kiritish — ko‘p uchraydigan ishora xatosi: ifoda $x - 7$, demak $k$ manfiy.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following is equivalent to $\\\\dfrac{3}{x + 2} + \\\\dfrac{x}{x - 1}$ for $x > 1$?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\dfrac{x + 3}{2x + 1}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\dfrac{x^2 + 2x + 3}{(x + 2)(x - 1)}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\dfrac{x^2 + 5x - 3}{(x + 2)(x - 1)}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\dfrac{x^2 + 5x + 3}{(x + 2)(x - 1)}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Use the common denominator $(x + 2)(x - 1)$: $\\\\frac{3(x - 1)}{(x + 2)(x - 1)} + \\\\frac{x(x + 2)}{(x + 2)(x - 1)}$.\\n\\nAdd the numerators: $3x - 3 + x^2 + 2x = x^2 + 5x - 3$. So the sum is $\\\\frac{x^2 + 5x - 3}{(x + 2)(x - 1)}$.\\n\\nChoice B forgets to multiply the numerator $3$ by $(x - 1)$ when rewriting the first fraction; choice A adds the numerators and the denominators directly, which is never valid.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Umumiy maxraj $(x + 2)(x - 1)$ ni olamiz: $\\\\frac{3(x - 1)}{(x + 2)(x - 1)} + \\\\frac{x(x + 2)}{(x + 2)(x - 1)}$.\\n\\nSuratlarni qo‘shamiz: $3x - 3 + x^2 + 2x = x^2 + 5x - 3$. Demak yig‘indi $\\\\frac{x^2 + 5x - 3}{(x + 2)(x - 1)}$.\\n\\nB variantda birinchi kasrni qayta yozishda surat $3$ ni $(x - 1)$ ga ko‘paytirish unutilgan; A variantda esa suratlar va maxrajlar to‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri qo‘shilgan — bu hech qachon to‘g‘ri emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following is equivalent to $\\\\dfrac{6x^2 + 7x - 1}{2x + 3}$ for $x \\\\ne -\\\\frac{3}{2}$?\",\"option_a\":\"$3x - 1 - \\\\dfrac{4}{2x + 3}$\",\"option_b\":\"$3x - 1$\",\"option_c\":\"$3x - 1 + \\\\dfrac{2}{2x + 3}$\",\"option_d\":\"$3x + 8 - \\\\dfrac{25}{2x + 3}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Rewrite the numerator using multiples of the denominator: $(2x + 3)(3x - 1) = 6x^2 - 2x + 9x - 3 = 6x^2 + 7x - 3$.\\n\\nSo $6x^2 + 7x - 1 = (2x + 3)(3x - 1) + 2$, and dividing by $2x + 3$ gives $3x - 1 + \\\\frac{2}{2x + 3}$.\\n\\nCheck with $x = 1$: the original expression is $\\\\frac{6 + 7 - 1}{5} = \\\\frac{12}{5}$, and $3(1) - 1 + \\\\frac{2}{5} = \\\\frac{12}{5}$.\\n\\nChoice A comes from a sign error in the last subtraction of the long division: $-1 - (-3) = 2$, not $-4$; choice B ignores the remainder, so it is not equivalent (at $x = 1$ it gives $2$, not $\\\\frac{12}{5}$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Suratni maxrajning karralilari orqali yozamiz: $(2x + 3)(3x - 1) = 6x^2 - 2x + 9x - 3 = 6x^2 + 7x - 3$.\\n\\nDemak $6x^2 + 7x - 1 = (2x + 3)(3x - 1) + 2$, va $2x + 3$ ga bo‘lsak, $3x - 1 + \\\\frac{2}{2x + 3}$ hosil bo‘ladi.\\n\\nTekshiruv, $x = 1$: dastlabki ifoda $\\\\frac{6 + 7 - 1}{5} = \\\\frac{12}{5}$, va $3(1) - 1 + \\\\frac{2}{5} = \\\\frac{12}{5}$.\\n\\nA variant — burchakli bo‘lishning oxirgi ayirish bosqichidagi ishora xatosi: $-1 - (-3) = 2$, $-4$ emas; B variant esa qoldiqni hisobga olmaydi, shuning uchun ekvivalent emas ($x = 1$ da $\\\\frac{12}{5}$ emas, $2$ chiqadi).\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} 2x - 3y &= 5 \\\\\\\\ 4x^2 - 9y^2 &= 35 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nIf $(x, y)$ satisfies both of the given equations, what is the value of $x$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Recognize a difference of squares: $4x^2 - 9y^2 = (2x - 3y)(2x + 3y)$.\\n\\nSubstitute $2x - 3y = 5$: $5(2x + 3y) = 35$, so $2x + 3y = 7$.\\n\\nNow add $2x - 3y = 5$ and $2x + 3y = 7$: $4x = 12$, so $x = 3$. (Then $y = \\\\frac{1}{3}$; check: $4(9) - 9\\\\left(\\\\frac{1}{9}\\\\right) = 36 - 1 = 35$.)\\n\\nA common error is entering $7$, which is the value of $2x + 3y$, not of $x$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kvadratlar ayirmasini ko‘ramiz: $4x^2 - 9y^2 = (2x - 3y)(2x + 3y)$.\\n\\n$2x - 3y = 5$ ni qo‘yamiz: $5(2x + 3y) = 35$, demak $2x + 3y = 7$.\\n\\nEndi $2x - 3y = 5$ va $2x + 3y = 7$ ni qo‘shamiz: $4x = 12$, demak $x = 3$. (U holda $y = \\\\frac{1}{3}$; tekshiruv: $4(9) - 9\\\\left(\\\\frac{1}{9}\\\\right) = 36 - 1 = 35$.)\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $7$ ni kiritish: bu $x$ ning emas, $2x + 3y$ ning qiymati.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A school wants to know how its students feel about a new lunch menu. On one Monday, a staff member surveys 100 students who are buying lunch in the school cafeteria. Which of the following is the best reason the results might not represent the opinions of all students at the school?\",\"option_a\":\"A sample of 100 students is too large to analyze accurately.\",\"option_b\":\"The survey was given on a Monday instead of on a Friday.\",\"option_c\":\"The staff member should have surveyed teachers instead of students.\",\"option_d\":\"Students who buy lunch at school may feel differently about the menu than students who do not buy lunch at school.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The sample includes only students who chose to buy the school lunch that day. Students who bring lunch from home, possibly because they dislike the menu, had no chance to be surveyed, so the sample may be biased toward students who like the menu. A random sample of all students would avoid this problem. Choice A is wrong because a larger sample is not a problem. Choice B names a difference that, by itself, gives no reason to expect biased opinions, and choice C changes the question: the school wants to know what students think, not teachers.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tanlanmaga faqat o‘sha kuni maktab tushligini sotib olgan o‘quvchilar kirgan. Tushlikni uydan olib keladigan o‘quvchilar (balki aynan menyuni yoqtirmagani uchun) so‘rovga tushish imkoniga ega bo‘lmagan, shuning uchun tanlanma menyuni yoqtiradiganlar tomonga og‘ishi mumkin. Barcha o‘quvchilar orasidan tasodifiy tanlanma olish bu muammoni bartaraf etardi. A javob noto‘g‘ri, chunki tanlanmaning kattaligi muammo emas. B javobdagi kun farqining o‘zi fikrlar noxolis bo‘lishiga asos bermaydi, C javob esa savolni o‘zgartirib yuboradi: maktab o‘qituvchilarning emas, o‘quvchilarning fikrini bilmoqchi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Researchers surveyed a random sample of 500 adults in a city. The adults who reported walking at least 30 minutes a day reported lower stress levels, on average, than the adults who reported walking less. Which of the following is the best reason the researchers cannot conclude that walking at least 30 minutes a day reduces stress for adults in the city?\",\"option_a\":\"The adults were not randomly assigned to walk at least 30 minutes a day or to walk less.\",\"option_b\":\"The sample was not selected at random.\",\"option_c\":\"A sample of 500 adults is too small to support any conclusion.\",\"option_d\":\"The study included only adults and no children.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"To conclude that walking **causes** lower stress, the researchers would need an experiment in which participants are randomly assigned to walk or not. Here the adults chose their own walking habits, so other differences between the groups (such as free time, health or type of job) could explain the lower stress. Choice B is false: the sample was random, which allows the association to be generalized to adults in the city, but random sampling alone does not establish cause and effect. Choice C is wrong because 500 randomly selected adults are enough to support conclusions about an association, and choice D is irrelevant to a claim about adults.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Yurish stressni **kamaytiradi** degan xulosa uchun ishtirokchilar yurish yoki yurmaslikka tasodifiy taqsimlangan tajriba kerak. Bu yerda kattalar yurish odatini o‘zlari tanlagan, shuning uchun guruhlar orasidagi boshqa farqlar (bo‘sh vaqt, sog‘liq, ish turi va hokazo) stress darajasining pastligini tushuntirishi mumkin. B javob noto‘g‘ri: tanlanma tasodifiy bo‘lgan — bu bog‘liqlikni shahardagi kattalarga umumlashtirishga imkon beradi, lekin tasodifiy tanlashning o‘zi sabab-oqibat munosabatini isbotlamaydi. C javob ham xato, chunki tasodifiy tanlangan 500 kishi bog‘liqlik haqida xulosa chiqarish uchun yetarli; D javob esa kattalar haqidagi da’voga aloqador emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A health researcher selected a random sample of 150 nurses from all nurses working at hospitals in one city. The nurses in the sample worked an average of 41 hours per week. To which of the following groups can the results of this study most appropriately be generalized?\",\"option_a\":\"Only the 150 nurses in the sample\",\"option_b\":\"All hospital employees in the city\",\"option_c\":\"All nurses working at hospitals in the country\",\"option_d\":\"All nurses working at hospitals in the city\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Because the sample was selected at random from the nurses working at hospitals in this city, the results can be generalized to that population: all nurses working at hospitals in the city. Choice C goes too far, since nurses in other cities had no chance of being selected. Choice B includes other hospital employees who were not sampled. Choice A is too cautious: random sampling is exactly what allows a generalization beyond the sample.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tanlanma shu shahardagi kasalxonalarda ishlaydigan hamshiralar orasidan tasodifiy olingan, shuning uchun natijalarni aynan shu bosh to‘plamga — shahardagi kasalxonalarda ishlaydigan barcha hamshiralarga umumlashtirish mumkin. C javob haddan oshadi: boshqa shaharlardagi hamshiralar tanlanmaga tushish imkoniga ega bo‘lmagan. B javob tanlanmaga kirmagan boshqa kasalxona xodimlarini ham qo‘shib yuboradi. A javob esa ortiqcha ehtiyotkor: aynan tasodifiy tanlash natijani tanlanmadan tashqariga umumlashtirishga imkon beradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A council member collected data from 40 districts in a country and found that districts with more public libraries per 10,000 residents tend to have higher average household incomes. The council member claims that building more libraries in a district will raise household incomes in that district. Which of the following is the best evaluation of this claim?\",\"option_a\":\"The claim is not supported, because the data show only an association; for example, districts with higher incomes may be able to pay for more libraries.\",\"option_b\":\"The claim is supported, because the data show a positive association between the number of libraries and household income.\",\"option_c\":\"The claim is not supported, because data from 40 districts are too few to show any association.\",\"option_d\":\"The claim is supported for the 40 districts in the study but not for any other districts.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The data come from an observational study: no one randomly assigned numbers of libraries to districts. A positive association does not show that libraries cause higher incomes. The relationship could run the other way (districts with higher incomes can afford more libraries), or a third factor could affect both. Choice B is the trap: an association alone does not support a cause-and-effect claim. Choice C is wrong because the problem is the type of study, not the number of districts, and choice D still accepts the causal claim.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ma’lumotlar kuzatuv tadqiqotidan olingan: hech kim tumanlardagi kutubxonalar sonini tasodifiy belgilamagan. Musbat bog‘liqlik kutubxonalar daromadni oshirishini ko‘rsatmaydi. Munosabat teskari yo‘nalishda bo‘lishi ham mumkin (daromadi yuqori tumanlar ko‘proq kutubxona qura oladi) yoki ikkalasiga ham uchinchi omil ta’sir qilishi mumkin. B javob — tuzoq: bog‘liqlikning o‘zi sabab-oqibat haqidagi da’voni tasdiqlamaydi. C javob noto‘g‘ri, chunki muammo tumanlar sonida emas, tadqiqot turida; D javob esa baribir sabab-oqibat da’vosini qabul qiladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"Using the survey that gives the more reliable estimate for all of the city's residents, it is estimated that $p\\\\%$ of the city's residents support the plan. What is the value of $p$?\",\"passage\":\"A city government wanted to estimate the percentage of its residents who support a plan to extend a tram line. It collected data in two ways.\\n\\n- Survey 1: A poll was posted on the city's website, and 1,250 visitors chose to respond. Of these, 900 said they support the plan.\\n- Survey 2: A random sample of 400 residents was selected from a list of all city residents and contacted by phone. Of these, 136 said they support the plan.\",\"spr_answers\":[\"34\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Survey 1 is a voluntary-response sample: people decided for themselves whether to respond, so people with strong opinions (and people who visit the city's website) may be overrepresented. Its large size does not fix that bias. Survey 2 used a random sample of residents, so it gives the more reliable estimate: $\\\\frac{136}{400} = 0.34$, so $p = 34$. Entering 72, from $\\\\frac{900}{1{,}250}$, uses the biased online poll.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"1-so‘rovnoma — ixtiyoriy javob berilgan so‘rovnoma: odamlar javob berish-bermaslikni o‘zlari hal qilgan, shuning uchun kuchli fikrga ega bo‘lganlar (va shahar saytiga kiradiganlar) ortiqcha ulushda bo‘lishi mumkin. Katta hajm bu noxolislikni tuzatmaydi. 2-so‘rovnomada aholi orasidan tasodifiy tanlanma olingan, shuning uchun u ishonchliroq baho beradi: $\\\\frac{136}{400} = 0.34$, demak $p = 34$. 72 ($\\\\frac{900}{1{,}250}$) deb yozish noxolis onlayn so‘rovnomadan foydalanishni bildiradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A researcher wants to determine whether taking a certain supplement improves sleep quality for adults in a town. Which of the following study designs would best allow the researcher to reach a cause-and-effect conclusion that applies to all adults in the town?\",\"option_a\":\"Ask adults in the town who already take the supplement to rate their sleep quality, and compare their ratings with those of adults in the town who do not take it.\",\"option_b\":\"Recruit adult volunteers from a sleep clinic in the town, and randomly assign half of them to take the supplement and the other half to take a placebo.\",\"option_c\":\"Select a random sample of adults from the town, and let each selected adult choose whether to take the supplement.\",\"option_d\":\"Select a random sample of adults from the town, and randomly assign half of them to take the supplement and the other half to take a placebo.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Two features are needed. Random **assignment** to the supplement or a placebo makes the groups alike except for the supplement, which allows a cause-and-effect conclusion. Random **selection** from all adults in the town allows that conclusion to be generalized to the town. Only choice D has both. Choice B has random assignment, but sleep-clinic volunteers may differ from typical adults in the town, so the conclusion would apply only to people like them. In choices A and C, people choose their own treatment, so no cause-and-effect conclusion is possible.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikki xususiyat kerak. Qo‘shimcha yoki platseboga tasodifiy **taqsimlash** guruhlarni qo‘shimchadan boshqa barcha jihatdan o‘xshash qiladi — bu sabab-oqibat xulosasiga imkon beradi. Shaharchadagi barcha kattalar orasidan tasodifiy **tanlash** esa bu xulosani butun shaharchaga umumlashtirishga imkon beradi. Ikkalasi faqat D javobda bor. B javobda tasodifiy taqsimlash bor, lekin uyqu klinikasiga kelgan ko‘ngillilar shaharchaning odatiy kattalaridan farq qilishi mumkin, shuning uchun xulosa faqat ularga o‘xshash odamlarga taalluqli bo‘ladi. A va C javoblarda odamlar qo‘shimchani o‘zlari tanlaydi, shuning uchun sabab-oqibat xulosasini chiqarib bo‘lmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"An online store selected 400 of its customers at random. Each selected customer could choose whether to use a new one-click checkout feature for one month. At the end of the month, the customers who chose to use the feature had spent more, on average, than the customers who did not. Which of the following conclusions is best supported by this study?\",\"option_a\":\"Using the feature causes the store's customers to spend more.\",\"option_b\":\"Among the store's customers, using the feature is associated with spending more, but the study does not show that the feature causes customers to spend more.\",\"option_c\":\"Using the feature causes customers of all online stores to spend more.\",\"option_d\":\"No conclusion can be drawn about the store's customers, because only 400 customers were studied.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The customers were randomly **selected** from all of the store's customers, so the association can be generalized to the store's customers. But they were not randomly **assigned** to use the feature; they chose for themselves. Customers who already spend a lot might be the ones most likely to try a faster checkout, so the study cannot show cause and effect. Choice A is the trap: it claims causation from a study without random assignment. Choice C makes the same error and also overgeneralizes to other stores. Choice D is wrong because a random sample of 400 is enough to support conclusions about the population it was drawn from.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Mijozlar do‘konning barcha mijozlari orasidan tasodifiy **tanlangan**, shuning uchun bog‘liqlikni do‘kon mijozlariga umumlashtirish mumkin. Lekin ular yangi funksiyadan foydalanishga tasodifiy **taqsimlanmagan** — buni o‘zlari tanlashgan. Ko‘p xarid qiladigan mijozlar tezroq to‘lov usulini sinab ko‘rishga ko‘proq moyil bo‘lishi mumkin, shuning uchun tadqiqot sabab-oqibatni ko‘rsata olmaydi. A javob — tuzoq: u tasodifiy taqsimlanmagan tadqiqotdan sabab-oqibat xulosasini chiqaradi. C javob xuddi shu xatoga yo‘l qo‘yadi va natijani boshqa do‘konlarga ham yoyadi. D javob noto‘g‘ri, chunki 400 kishilik tasodifiy tanlanma u olingan bosh to‘plam haqida xulosa chiqarish uchun yetarli.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A city has three districts: North District has 12,000 adults, Central District has 20,000 adults, and South District has 8,000 adults. A researcher wants to survey a sample of the city's adults in which each district is represented in proportion to its number of adults. The researcher has already selected 90 adults at random from North District. To keep the sample proportional, how many adults in total should the complete sample from all three districts contain?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"300\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The numbers of adults are in the ratio $12{,}000 : 20{,}000 : 8{,}000 = 3 : 5 : 2$, so the sample must be split in the same ratio. North District's 90 adults correspond to 3 parts, so 1 part is 30 adults. Central District needs $5 \\\\times 30 = 150$ adults and South District needs $2 \\\\times 30 = 60$, so the complete sample has $90 + 150 + 60 = 300$ adults. Check: North District has $\\\\frac{12{,}000}{40{,}000} = 30\\\\%$ of the city's adults, and $\\\\frac{90}{300} = 30\\\\%$. Entering 150 or 60 gives only one district, and 270 (90 adults from each district) would overrepresent South District and underrepresent Central District.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kattalar soni $12{,}000 : 20{,}000 : 8{,}000 = 3 : 5 : 2$ nisbatda, demak tanlanma ham shu nisbatda bo‘linishi kerak. North District’dan olingan 90 kishi 3 qismga to‘g‘ri keladi, ya’ni 1 qism — 30 kishi. Central District’dan $5 \\\\times 30 = 150$, South District’dan $2 \\\\times 30 = 60$ kishi kerak, butun tanlanma esa $90 + 150 + 60 = 300$ kishi. Tekshiruv: North District shahar kattalarining $\\\\frac{12{,}000}{40{,}000} = 30\\\\%$ ini tashkil etadi va $\\\\frac{90}{300} = 30\\\\%$ ✓. 150 yoki 60 — faqat bitta tuman uchun son; 270 (har tumandan 90 kishidan) esa South District’ni ortiqcha, Central District’ni esa yetarlicha ifodalamaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":125,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The list of volunteers who signed up to help clean the riverbank last weekend ______ much longer than the organizers had expected, so the group was divided into four teams, each assigned to a different section of the shore.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"were\",\"option_b\":\"have been\",\"option_c\":\"are\",\"option_d\":\"was\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The subject of the sentence is the singular noun “list,” not “volunteers”; “volunteers” is part of the prepositional phrase “of volunteers who signed up….” A singular subject needs a singular verb, so choice D, “was,” is correct. It is also in the past tense, which matches “had expected.”\\n\\nChoices A (“were”), B (“have been”), and C (“are”) are plural verbs that agree with “volunteers” instead of the actual subject, “list.”\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gapning egasi — birlikdagi “list” so‘zi, “volunteers” emas; “volunteers” “of volunteers who signed up…” predlogli birikmasining bir qismi. Birlikdagi egaga birlikdagi kesim kerak, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob D — “was”. U o‘tgan zamonda ham bo‘lib, “had expected” bilan mos keladi.\\n\\nA (“were”), B (“have been”) va C (“are”) — ko‘plikdagi fe’llar; ular haqiqiy ega “list” bilan emas, “volunteers” bilan moslashtirilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Light slowly fades the ink on the museum's two oldest manuscripts. To protect these delicate pages, curators display ______ for only one week each year, during the city's annual book festival.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"it\",\"option_b\":\"them\",\"option_c\":\"itself\",\"option_d\":\"themselves\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The pronoun refers to “these delicate pages,” that is, the museum's two oldest manuscripts. That antecedent is plural, and the pronoun is the object of the verb “display,” so the plural object pronoun “them” is correct (choice B).\\n\\nChoice A, “it,” is singular and does not agree with the plural antecedent. Choices C and D are reflexive pronouns, which are used only when the object is the same as the subject; here the curators display the manuscripts, not themselves.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Olmosh “these delicate pages”, ya’ni muzeydagi eng qadimgi ikki qo‘lyozmaga ishora qiladi. Bu ot ko‘plikda, olmosh esa “display” fe’lining to‘ldiruvchisi, shuning uchun ko‘plikdagi obyekt olmoshi “them” to‘g‘ri (B).\\n\\nA — “it” birlikda, ko‘plikdagi otga mos kelmaydi. C va D — o‘zlik olmoshlari (reflexive); ular to‘ldiruvchi ega bilan bir xil bo‘lgandagina ishlatiladi. Bu yerda esa kuratorlar o‘zlarini emas, qo‘lyozmalarni namoyish qiladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Every spring, hundreds of cliff swallows return to the steep clay bank above the river. The ______ nests, which are built from small pellets of mud, cling to the bank in tight clusters that look like rows of tiny clay jars.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"swallow's\",\"option_b\":\"swallows\",\"option_c\":\"swallows'\",\"option_d\":\"swallows's\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The nests belong to many birds—the “hundreds of cliff swallows” mentioned in the first sentence. To form the possessive of a plural noun that ends in -s, add only an apostrophe: “swallows'.” Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A, “swallow's,” is the possessive of a single swallow. Choice B, “swallows,” is a plain plural and shows no possession. Choice D, “swallows's,” is not a standard possessive form.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Uyalar ko‘plab qushlarga — birinchi gapdagi “hundreds of cliff swallows” ga tegishli. -s bilan tugaydigan ko‘plikdagi otning egalik shaklini yasash uchun faqat apostrof qo‘shiladi: “swallows’”. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA — “swallow’s” bitta qaldirg‘ochga egalikni bildiradi. B — “swallows” oddiy ko‘plik shakli, egalikni bildirmaydi. D — “swallows’s” standart egalik shakli emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"By the time the new bridge across the river opened to traffic in 2019, engineers ______ more than a decade studying how the river's seasonal floods move sand and gravel along its bed.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"had spent\",\"option_b\":\"spend\",\"option_c\":\"will have spent\",\"option_d\":\"are spending\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The phrase “By the time the new bridge … opened to traffic in 2019” sets a point in the past, and the engineers' study took place before that point. The past perfect tense (“had” plus a past participle) describes an action completed before another past event, so choice A, “had spent,” is correct.\\n\\nChoice B (simple present), choice C (future perfect), and choice D (present progressive) do not fit an action that was finished before a past event in 2019.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“By the time the new bridge … opened to traffic in 2019” iborasi o‘tmishdagi bir nuqtani belgilaydi, muhandislarning tadqiqoti esa shu nuqtadan oldin bo‘lib o‘tgan. O‘tmishdagi boshqa voqeadan oldin tugagan harakat past perfect zamonida (“had” + past participle) ifodalanadi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob A — “had spent”.\\n\\nB (oddiy hozirgi zamon), C (future perfect) va D (present progressive) 2019-yildagi voqeadan oldin tugagan harakatga mos kelmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Visitors to the gallery often remark on how orderly the paintings in the new exhibition look. Trained as an architect before she turned to painting, ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"the canvases of Zulfiya Ahmedova are filled with precise geometric patterns and carefully measured lines.\",\"option_b\":\"precise geometric patterns and carefully measured lines fill the canvases of Zulfiya Ahmedova.\",\"option_c\":\"Zulfiya Ahmedova fills her canvases with precise geometric patterns and carefully measured lines.\",\"option_d\":\"Zulfiya Ahmedova's canvases are filled with precise geometric patterns and carefully measured lines.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The introductory phrase “Trained as an architect before she turned to painting” must describe the person who was trained, the painter. In Standard English, a modifying phrase like this one applies to the noun that comes right after the comma, so that noun must be “Zulfiya Ahmedova,” as in choice C.\\n\\nChoices A and D place “canvases” right after the phrase, so they say that the canvases were trained as an architect. Choice B says that the patterns and lines were trained as an architect. All three contain a dangling modifier.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kirish iborasi “Trained as an architect before she turned to painting” me’mor sifatida tahsil olgan shaxsni, ya’ni rassomni tasvirlashi kerak. Ingliz tilida bunday aniqlovchi ibora verguldan keyin darhol keladigan otga tegishli bo‘ladi, shuning uchun u ot “Zulfiya Ahmedova” bo‘lishi shart — C variantidagidek.\\n\\nA va D variantlarda iboradan keyin “canvases” keladi, ya’ni go‘yo kartinalar me’morlikni o‘rgangan bo‘lib chiqadi. B esa naqsh va chiziqlar me’morlikni o‘rgangan degan ma’noni beradi. Uchala variantda ham aniqlovchi noto‘g‘ri joylashgan (dangling modifier).\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Neither the lead researcher nor her two assistants ______ able to explain why the seedlings in the third greenhouse grew so much taller than the seedlings in the other two greenhouses during the eight-week trial.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"was\",\"option_b\":\"were\",\"option_c\":\"has been\",\"option_d\":\"is\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"When two subjects are joined by “neither … nor,” the verb agrees with the subject that is closer to it. Here the closer subject is “her two assistants,” which is plural, so the plural verb “were” (choice B) is correct. It is also in the past tense, which fits the rest of the sentence (“grew”).\\n\\nChoices A (“was”), C (“has been”), and D (“is”) are singular verbs. They would agree with “the lead researcher,” but that is the farther subject.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikki ega “neither … nor” bilan bog‘langanda, kesim o‘ziga yaqinroq turgan ega bilan moslashadi. Bu yerda yaqinroq ega — ko‘plikdagi “her two assistants”, shuning uchun ko‘plikdagi “were” (B) to‘g‘ri. U o‘tgan zamonda bo‘lib, gapning qolgan qismiga (“grew”) ham mos keladi.\\n\\nA (“was”), C (“has been”) va D (“is”) birlikdagi fe’llar. Ular “the lead researcher” bilan moslashardi, lekin bu ega kesimdan uzoqroqda turibdi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Archaeologists working at the site of an ancient trading settlement were surprised by what they found in a sealed storeroom. Among the objects recovered from the room ______ a set of polished bronze mirrors and a small ivory comb decorated with carved dancers.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"were\",\"option_b\":\"was\",\"option_c\":\"is\",\"option_d\":\"has been\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The second sentence is inverted: the prepositional phrase “Among the objects recovered from the room” comes first, and the subject follows the verb. The subject is “a set of polished bronze mirrors and a small ivory comb”—two things joined by “and”—so it takes a plural verb. Choice A, “were,” is plural and matches the past-tense narrative (“were surprised”).\\n\\nChoices B (“was”), C (“is”), and D (“has been”) are singular verbs. They may seem to fit because the noun just before the blank, “room,” and the first noun of the subject, “set,” are singular, but the full subject is a compound joined by “and.”\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkinchi gapda so‘z tartibi teskari: avval “Among the objects recovered from the room” predlogli birikmasi keladi, ega esa kesimdan keyin turadi. Ega — “a set of polished bronze mirrors and a small ivory comb”, ya’ni “and” bilan bog‘langan ikki narsa, shuning uchun kesim ko‘plikda bo‘lishi kerak. A — “were” ko‘plikda va hikoyadagi o‘tgan zamonga (“were surprised”) mos keladi.\\n\\nB (“was”), C (“is”) va D (“has been”) birlikdagi fe’llar. Bo‘sh joydan oldingi “room” va eganing birinchi oti “set” birlikda bo‘lgani uchun ular to‘g‘ridek ko‘rinishi mumkin, lekin to‘liq ega “and” bilan bog‘langan uyushiq egadir.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The eleventh-century scholar al-Biruni, who estimated the radius of Earth by measuring how far the horizon appeared to dip below level when viewed from the top of a mountain, ______ a value remarkably close to the one accepted by modern scientists.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"obtaining\",\"option_b\":\"having obtained\",\"option_c\":\"obtained\",\"option_d\":\"to obtain\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The subject of the sentence is “The eleventh-century scholar al-Biruni,” and the long clause “who estimated the radius of Earth … from the top of a mountain” describes him. After this interrupting clause, the sentence still needs a main verb for its subject. Only choice C, “obtained,” is a finite past-tense verb that can serve as that main verb.\\n\\nChoices A (“obtaining”), B (“having obtained”), and D (“to obtain”) are nonfinite verb forms. With any of them, the sentence has no main verb and is therefore a fragment. The long clause between the subject and the blank makes this easy to miss.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gapning egasi — “The eleventh-century scholar al-Biruni”, “who estimated the radius of Earth … from the top of a mountain” degan uzun ergash gap esa uni tasvirlaydi. Bu oraliq gapdan keyin ham ega uchun asosiy kesim kerak. Faqat C — “obtained” — o‘tgan zamondagi shaxsli fe’l bo‘lib, kesim vazifasini bajara oladi.\\n\\nA (“obtaining”), B (“having obtained”) va D (“to obtain”) — shaxssiz fe’l shakllari. Ularning birortasi qo‘yilsa, gapda asosiy kesim bo‘lmaydi va u to‘liq bo‘lmagan gapga (fragment) aylanadi. Ega bilan bo‘sh joy orasidagi uzun gap bu xatoni sezishni qiyinlashtiradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A school has 1,200 students. In a random sample of 80 students from the school, 24 students said they walk to school. Based on this sample, which of the following is the best estimate of the number of students at the school who walk to school?\",\"option_a\":\"$24$\",\"option_b\":\"$288$\",\"option_c\":\"$360$\",\"option_d\":\"$840$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"In the sample, $\\\\frac{24}{80} = 0.30$, or 30%, of the students walk to school. Because the sample was selected at random, this proportion is a reasonable estimate for the whole school: $0.30 \\\\times 1{,}200 = 360$ students. Choice B treats 24 as a percent ($0.24 \\\\times 1{,}200$), but 24 is a count out of 80 students, not out of 100. Choice D estimates the students who do **not** walk, and choice A is only the count in the sample.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tanlanmada o‘quvchilarning $\\\\frac{24}{80} = 0.30$ qismi, ya’ni 30% i maktabga piyoda keladi. Tanlanma tasodifiy olingani uchun bu ulush butun maktab uchun ham asosli baho bo‘ladi: $0.30 \\\\times 1{,}200 = 360$ o‘quvchi. B javob 24 ni foiz deb olgan ($0.24 \\\\times 1{,}200$), vaholanki 24 — 100 emas, 80 o‘quvchi ichidagi son. D javob piyoda **kelmaydigan** o‘quvchilar bahosi, A javob esa faqat tanlanmadagi son.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A polling organization surveyed a random sample of registered voters in a region. Based on the sample, it estimated that 46% of all registered voters in the region support a proposed law, with a margin of error of 3 percentage points. Based on this estimate and margin of error, the greatest plausible percentage of the region's registered voters who support the law is $p\\\\%$. What is the value of $p$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"49\"],\"explanation_en\":\"A margin of error gives a range of plausible values for the population percentage: $46\\\\% \\\\pm 3\\\\%$, or from 43% to 49%. The greatest plausible value is $46 + 3 = 49$, so $p = 49$. Entering 43 gives the least plausible value, not the greatest.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Xatolik chegarasi bosh to‘plamdagi foiz uchun ehtimoliy qiymatlar oralig‘ini beradi: $46\\\\% \\\\pm 3\\\\%$, ya’ni 43% dan 49% gacha. Eng katta ehtimoliy qiymat $46 + 3 = 49$, demak $p = 49$. 43 deb yozish — eng kichik ehtimoliy qiymatni berish, eng kattasini emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Each member in a random sample of 150 members of a city's public library was asked how many books they read each month. The sample mean was 4.2 books, with an associated margin of error of 0.6 book. Which of the following is a plausible value for the mean number of books read each month by all members of the library?\",\"option_a\":\"$3.4$\",\"option_b\":\"$3.7$\",\"option_c\":\"$4.9$\",\"option_d\":\"$5.2$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Plausible values for the population mean lie within one margin of error of the sample mean: from $4.2 - 0.6 = 3.6$ to $4.2 + 0.6 = 4.8$ books. Of the choices, only 3.7 is in this interval. Choice C, 4.9, is close to 4.8 but lies outside the interval; 3.4 and 5.2 are farther outside.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bosh to‘plam o‘rta qiymatining ehtimoliy qiymatlari tanlanma o‘rta qiymatidan bitta xatolik chegarasi masofasida yotadi: $4.2 - 0.6 = 3.6$ dan $4.2 + 0.6 = 4.8$ gacha. Variantlar ichida faqat 3.7 shu oraliqda. C javob (4.9) 4.8 ga yaqin, lekin oraliqdan tashqarida; 3.4 va 5.2 esa undan ham uzoqroq.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Researchers selected a random sample of 150 commuters in a city and estimated the mean commute time of all commuters in the city, with a margin of error of 4.1 minutes. A second team will select a random sample of 600 commuters from the same city and use the same method and the same confidence level. Which of the following is most likely true about the margin of error of the second team's estimate?\",\"option_a\":\"It will be less than 4.1 minutes.\",\"option_b\":\"It will be equal to 4.1 minutes.\",\"option_c\":\"It will be greater than 4.1 minutes.\",\"option_d\":\"It will be about 16.4 minutes, because the sample is 4 times as large.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"With the same population, method and confidence level, a larger random sample gives a more precise estimate, so its margin of error is most likely smaller. A sample of 600 is 4 times as large as a sample of 150, so the margin of error would most likely be less than 4.1 minutes (theory suggests roughly half as large). Choices C and D get the relationship backward: collecting more data reduces uncertainty; it does not increase it.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bosh to‘plam, usul va ishonch darajasi bir xil bo‘lsa, kattaroq tasodifiy tanlanma aniqroq baho beradi, shuning uchun uning xatolik chegarasi kichikroq bo‘lishi ehtimoli katta. 600 — 150 dan 4 marta katta, demak xatolik chegarasi 4.1 daqiqadan kichik bo‘ladi (nazariyaga ko‘ra, taxminan ikki baravar kichik). C va D javoblar munosabatni teskari tushungan: ko‘proq ma’lumot noaniqlikni oshirmaydi, balki kamaytiradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A town has 18,000 households. In a random sample of 250 households in the town, 35 have no internet connection. Based on the sample, it is estimated that 14% of all households in the town have no internet connection, with a margin of error of 4 percentage points. Based on this estimate and margin of error, what is the greatest plausible number of households in the town that have no internet connection?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3240\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The plausible percentages are $14\\\\% \\\\pm 4\\\\%$, or from 10% to 18%. The greatest plausible number of households is 18% of all 18,000 households: $0.18 \\\\times 18{,}000 = 3{,}240$. Entering 2,520 ($0.14 \\\\times 18{,}000$) gives the point estimate, not the greatest plausible value. Applying 18% to the 250 sampled households instead of the whole town gives 45, which describes the sample rather than the population. Enter 3240 (without a comma).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ehtimoliy foizlar $14\\\\% \\\\pm 4\\\\%$, ya’ni 10% dan 18% gacha. Eng katta ehtimoliy son — barcha 18,000 xonadonning 18% i: $0.18 \\\\times 18{,}000 = 3{,}240$. 2,520 ($0.14 \\\\times 18{,}000$) — bu nuqtaviy baho, eng katta ehtimoliy qiymat emas. 18% ni butun shaharcha o‘rniga 250 talik tanlanmaga qo‘llash 45 ni beradi — bu bosh to‘plamni emas, tanlanmani ta’riflaydi. Javob maydoniga vergulsiz 3240 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A researcher selected a random sample of 500 adults in a region and recorded how many hours each adult slept on a particular night. Based on the sample, the researcher reported that plausible values for the mean number of hours of sleep that night for all adults in the region are between 6.6 hours and 7.0 hours. Which of the following conclusions is best supported by this information?\",\"option_a\":\"Every adult in the sample slept between 6.6 hours and 7.0 hours that night.\",\"option_b\":\"Most adults in the region slept between 6.6 hours and 7.0 hours that night.\",\"option_c\":\"The mean number of hours of sleep that night for all adults in the country is likely between 6.6 hours and 7.0 hours.\",\"option_d\":\"The mean number of hours of sleep that night for all adults in the region is likely between 6.6 hours and 7.0 hours.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The interval estimates a population **mean**, and the population is the group that was randomly sampled: adults in the region. So it is plausible that the mean for all adults in the region is between 6.6 and 7.0 hours. Choice B is a common misreading: the interval describes the mean, not individual adults, and many adults could have slept much more or much less than 6.6 to 7.0 hours. Choice A makes the same mistake about the sample. Choice C extends the result to the whole country, which was not sampled.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Oraliq bosh to‘plamning **o‘rta qiymatini** baholaydi, bosh to‘plam esa tasodifiy tanlab olingan guruh — mintaqadagi kattalar. Demak mintaqadagi barcha kattalarning o‘rtacha uyqu vaqti 6.6 va 7.0 soat orasida bo‘lishi ehtimoliy. B javob — keng tarqalgan noto‘g‘ri talqin: oraliq alohida odamlarni emas, o‘rta qiymatni ta’riflaydi; ko‘p kattalar 6.6–7.0 soatdan ancha ko‘p yoki ancha kam uxlagan bo‘lishi mumkin. A javob xuddi shu xatoni tanlanma uchun qiladi. C javob natijani tanlanma olinmagan butun mamlakatga yoyadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Two towns each surveyed a random sample of their adult residents about a proposed sports center. In Town A, 42% of the sample supported the sports center, with a margin of error of 4 percentage points. In Town B, 49% of the sample supported the sports center, with a margin of error of 5 percentage points. Which of the following statements is best supported by these results?\",\"option_a\":\"The percentage of adults who support the sports center is greater in Town B than in Town A, because 49% is greater than 42%.\",\"option_b\":\"It is plausible that the percentage of adults who support the sports center is the same in both towns.\",\"option_c\":\"The percentage of adults who support the sports center is exactly 7 percentage points greater in Town B than in Town A.\",\"option_d\":\"Because Town B's margin of error is greater, Town B's survey must have included more residents than Town A's survey.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The plausible values are $42\\\\% \\\\pm 4\\\\%$, or 38% to 46%, for Town A and $49\\\\% \\\\pm 5\\\\%$, or 44% to 54%, for Town B. The intervals overlap from 44% to 46%, so a value such as 45% is plausible for both towns, and the results do not establish that the two percentages differ. Choice A treats the sample percentages as exact population values, and choice C does the same with their difference. Choice D reverses the relationship between sample size and margin of error: other things being equal, a greater margin of error points to a smaller sample, not a larger one.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ehtimoliy qiymatlar: A shaharcha uchun $42\\\\% \\\\pm 4\\\\%$, ya’ni 38% dan 46% gacha; B shaharcha uchun $49\\\\% \\\\pm 5\\\\%$, ya’ni 44% dan 54% gacha. Oraliqlar 44% dan 46% gacha ustma-ust tushadi, shuning uchun, masalan, 45% ikkala shaharcha uchun ham ehtimoliy — natijalar ikki foiz har xil ekanini isbotlamaydi. A javob tanlanmadagi foizlarni bosh to‘plamning aniq qiymatlari deb oladi, C javob esa ularning farqi bilan xuddi shunday qiladi. D javob tanlanma hajmi va xatolik chegarasi orasidagi munosabatni teskari tushungan: boshqa shartlar teng bo‘lsa, kattaroq xatolik chegarasi kattaroq emas, kichikroq tanlanmaga ishora qiladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A factory produced 9,600 phone chargers in one week. A random sample of 400 of these chargers was tested, and the percentage of defective chargers in the sample was used to estimate the number of defective chargers among all 9,600. The estimate, plus or minus its margin of error, gives plausible numbers of defective chargers from 1,104 to 1,488. How many of the 400 sampled chargers were defective?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"54\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The estimate is the center of the range: $\\\\frac{1{,}104 + 1{,}488}{2} = 1{,}296$ chargers (the margin of error is $1{,}488 - 1{,}296 = 192$ chargers). This estimate came from applying the sample percentage to all 9,600 chargers, so the sample percentage is $\\\\frac{1{,}296}{9{,}600} = 0.135$, or 13.5%. In the sample, $0.135 \\\\times 400 = 54$ chargers were defective. Answers such as 46 or 62 come from using an endpoint of the range instead of its center ($\\\\frac{1{,}104}{9{,}600} \\\\times 400 = 46$ and $\\\\frac{1{,}488}{9{,}600} \\\\times 400 = 62$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Baho — oraliqning markazi: $\\\\frac{1{,}104 + 1{,}488}{2} = 1{,}296$ ta quvvatlagich (xatolik chegarasi $1{,}488 - 1{,}296 = 192$ ta). Bu baho tanlanmadagi foizni barcha 9,600 ta quvvatlagichga qo‘llash orqali olingan, demak tanlanmadagi ulush $\\\\frac{1{,}296}{9{,}600} = 0.135$, ya’ni 13.5%. Tanlanmada $0.135 \\\\times 400 = 54$ ta quvvatlagich nuqsonli bo‘lgan. 46 yoki 62 kabi javoblar oraliq markazi o‘rniga uning chegaralaridan foydalanishdan kelib chiqadi ($\\\\frac{1{,}104}{9{,}600} \\\\times 400 = 46$ va $\\\\frac{1{,}488}{9{,}600} \\\\times 400 = 62$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In 2023, the only bridge over the Kass River in the town of Rellim was closed for six months of repairs. During that time, residents of the town's east side had to take a detour that added about twenty minutes to each trip to the west side. Shop owners on the west side reported that many of their regular customers from the east side stopped coming during the closure. This suggests that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"many shops on the west side closed permanently in 2023.\",\"option_b\":\"the longer trip discouraged some east-side residents from shopping on the west side.\",\"option_c\":\"the bridge repairs were finished earlier than planned.\",\"option_d\":\"east-side residents generally prefer west-side shops to the shops on their own side of town.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text links the bridge closure to a twenty-minute detour and reports that many east-side customers stopped visiting west-side shops during that time. The most logical conclusion is that the longer trip discouraged them, as choice B says. Choice A goes too far: the text reports lost customers, not shop closures. Choice C is unsupported: nothing is said about when the repairs ended. Choice D is unsupported: the text does not say how east-side residents compare the shops on the two sides of town, and such a preference would not explain why they stopped coming.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn ko‘prik yopilishini yigirma daqiqalik aylanma yo‘l bilan bog‘laydi va shu davrda sharqiy qismdagi ko‘plab doimiy xaridorlar g‘arbiy qismdagi do‘konlarga kelmay qo‘yganini aytadi. Eng mantiqiy xulosa — uzoqroq yo‘l ularni bundan qaytargan. To‘g‘ri javob — B. A haddan oshib ketadi: matnda do‘konlar yopilgani emas, xaridorlar kamaygani aytilgan. C asossiz: ta’mirlash qachon tugagani haqida gap yo‘q. D ham asossiz: matnda sharqiy qism aholisi shaharning ikki tomonidagi do‘konlarni qanday solishtirishi aytilmagan, bunday afzal ko‘rish esa ularning nega kelmay qo‘yganini tushuntirmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Biologist Marta Sousa hung two identical bird feeders, filled with the same seed, in a city park where hawks often hunt small birds. One feeder hung over an open lawn; the other hung beside dense bushes where small birds can quickly hide. Over one month, small birds made three times as many visits to the feeder beside the bushes as to the feeder over the lawn. These results suggest that small birds ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"may prefer to feed in places where they can quickly escape from predators.\",\"option_b\":\"are unable to find food on open lawns.\",\"option_c\":\"are rarely hunted by hawks in city parks.\",\"option_d\":\"prefer the type of seed in the feeder beside the bushes.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The two feeders were identical and held the same seed; the only difference was that one hung near bushes where birds can hide, in a park where hawks hunt. That birds visited this feeder three times as often suggests they prefer feeding where they can escape predators, as choice A says. Choice B is too extreme: birds still visited the feeder over the lawn. Choice C contradicts the text, which says that hawks often hunt small birds in the park. Choice D is ruled out because both feeders held the same seed.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala oziqlantirgich bir xil bo‘lgan va ularda bir xil don bo‘lgan; yagona farq — ulardan biri qushlar tez yashirina oladigan butalar yonida osilgan, park esa qirg‘iylar ov qiladigan joy. Qushlarning shu oziqlantirgichga uch baravar ko‘p kelgani ular yirtqichdan tez qochish mumkin bo‘lgan joyda ovqatlanishni afzal ko‘rishini ko‘rsatadi — to‘g‘ri javob A. B haddan tashqari kuchli: qushlar maysazor ustidagi oziqlantirgichga ham kelgan. C matnga zid: matnda qirg‘iylar parkda kichik qushlarni tez-tez ovlashi aytilgan. D istisno qilinadi, chunki ikkala oziqlantirgichda ham bir xil don bo‘lgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Historians studying the travel diary of Edith Marr noticed that her entries about the city of Dorran describe the cathedral bells, the crowded fish market and the smell of the tanneries but never mention the city's famous stone bridge, which today appears in nearly every description of Dorran. The bridge was completed in 1871, and Marr's entries about Dorran are dated 1866. This suggests that Marr ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"did not consider the bridge worth describing.\",\"option_b\":\"wrote her entries about Dorran after 1871.\",\"option_c\":\"did not mention the bridge because it had not yet been completed when she visited.\",\"option_d\":\"never visited Dorran's fish market.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Marr wrote about Dorran in 1866, but the bridge was not completed until 1871, so the most logical explanation for her silence is that the finished bridge did not yet exist when she visited, as choice C says. Choice A assumes she saw the completed bridge, which the dates make unlikely. Choice B contradicts the 1866 date of the entries. Choice D contradicts the text, which says her entries describe the crowded fish market.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Marr Dorran haqida 1866-yilda yozgan, ko‘prik esa faqat 1871-yilda qurib bitkazilgan. Demak, uning ko‘prikni tilga olmaganining eng mantiqiy izohi — u shaharga borganida ko‘prik hali qurib bitkazilmagan edi. To‘g‘ri javob — C. A Marr tayyor ko‘prikni ko‘rgan deb faraz qiladi, sanalar esa buni ehtimoldan uzoq qiladi. B yozuvlarning 1866-yilga oid ekaniga zid. D matnga zid: uning yozuvlarida gavjum baliq bozori tasvirlangan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Each spring, caterpillars of the winter moth feed on the new leaves of the Tarvan oak. The caterpillars hatch at roughly the same time every year, and they feed best on young, tender leaves; as oak leaves mature, they quickly become tougher and harder to digest. Ecologist Simone Albrecht found that in years when the oaks' leaves opened unusually early, caterpillar damage to the trees was low. This finding suggests that when oak leaves open early, ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"the caterpillars hatch earlier than they do in other years.\",\"option_b\":\"the leaves remain young and tender for a longer period than usual.\",\"option_c\":\"the oaks produce fewer leaves than they do in other years.\",\"option_d\":\"many of the leaves have already become tough by the time the caterpillars hatch.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The caterpillars hatch at about the same time each year and feed best on young leaves, which toughen as they mature. If the leaves open early, they have extra time to mature before the caterpillars appear, so many will already be tough, which explains the low damage, as choice D says. Choice A contradicts the statement that the caterpillars hatch at roughly the same time every year. Choice B would make the leaves easier to eat and should increase damage, not reduce it. Choice C is unsupported: the text says nothing about the number of leaves.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qurtlar har yili taxminan bir vaqtda tuxumdan chiqadi va yosh, yumshoq barglar bilan yaxshi oziqlanadi; barglar yetilgan sari qattiqlashadi. Agar barglar erta ochilsa, qurtlar chiqquncha ular yetilishga ko‘proq vaqt topadi va ko‘plari allaqachon qattiq bo‘lib qoladi — bu zarar kamligini tushuntiradi. To‘g‘ri javob — D. A qurtlar har yili taxminan bir vaqtda chiqadi degan gapga zid. B barglarni yeyishni osonlashtirar edi, ya’ni zararni kamaytirmas, balki oshirar edi. C asossiz: matnda barglar soni haqida hech narsa aytilmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Scholars have long debated whether the anonymous medieval poem *The Ferrier's Lament* was composed in the northern or the southern part of the kingdom of Aldren. The poem's only surviving manuscript was copied by a scribe in the south. However, several of the poem's rhymes work only in the northern dialect of the period: when the lines are read with southern pronunciation, those rhyming words no longer sound alike. This evidence suggests that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"the poem was probably composed in the north, even though the surviving copy was made in the south.\",\"option_b\":\"the southern scribe deliberately changed the poem's rhymes to match northern pronunciation.\",\"option_c\":\"readers in the south did not enjoy poems that used rhyme.\",\"option_d\":\"the poem was composed much later than scholars had assumed.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The rhymes work only in the northern dialect, which suggests that the poet composed the poem using northern pronunciation. The manuscript's southern origin is easily explained by a southern scribe copying a northern poem. Choice A is therefore the most logical conclusion. Choice B is unsupported: nothing suggests the scribe altered the rhymes, and a southern scribe would have no clear reason to make them fit a different dialect. Choice C is unsupported: the text says nothing about southern readers' tastes. Choice D is unsupported: the evidence concerns where the poem was composed, not when.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qofiyalar faqat shimoliy shevada mos tushadi — bu shoir she’rni shimoliy talaffuzga tayanib yozganini ko‘rsatadi. Qo‘lyozmaning janubda ko‘chirilganini esa janublik kotib shimoliy she’rni ko‘chirib yozgani bilan osongina izohlash mumkin. Demak, eng mantiqiy xulosa — A. B asossiz: kotib qofiyalarni o‘zgartirganiga hech qanday ishora yo‘q, janublik kotibning ularni boshqa shevaga moslashtirishi uchun aniq sabab ham yo‘q. C asossiz: matnda janubiy o‘quvchilarning didi haqida gap yo‘q. D ham asossiz: dalil she’r qachon emas, qayerda yozilgani haqida.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Economist Javier Molina studied a city that replaced its coin-operated parking meters with a smartphone app. With the app, drivers can pay for parking and add more time from wherever they are, instead of having to return to the meter. After the app was introduced, the city's income from parking fees rose, while its income from fines for overstaying paid parking time fell sharply. The number of drivers parking in the city each day did not change. These findings suggest that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"drivers parked for shorter periods after the app was introduced.\",\"option_b\":\"many drivers who previously would have overstayed their paid time were instead using the app to pay for extra time.\",\"option_c\":\"most drivers stopped parking in the city after the app was introduced.\",\"option_d\":\"the app made it more difficult for drivers to pay for parking.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"With the same number of drivers, income from fees rose and income from fines fell. Because the app lets drivers add time remotely, the most logical explanation is that drivers who once would have run out of time and been fined now paid for extra time instead, as choice B says; this accounts for both changes. Choice A would tend to lower fee income, not raise it. Choice C contradicts the statement that the number of drivers did not change. Choice D conflicts with the rise in fee income and is not supported by anything in the text.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Haydovchilar soni o‘zgarmagan holda to‘lovlardan tushum oshgan, jarimalardan tushum esa keskin kamaygan. Ilova haydovchilarga masofadan turib vaqt qo‘shish imkonini bergani uchun eng mantiqiy izoh shunday: avval vaqti tugab jarimaga tortiladigan haydovchilar endi qo‘shimcha vaqt uchun to‘lay boshlagan — to‘g‘ri javob B. Bu ikkala o‘zgarishni ham tushuntiradi. A to‘lovlardan tushumni oshirmas, aksincha kamaytirar edi. C haydovchilar soni o‘zgarmagani haqidagi gapga zid. D to‘lovlardan tushum oshganiga zid va matnda unga hech qanday asos yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Lake Varn sits in a mountain basin and is fed almost entirely by melting snow from the surrounding peaks. Each year a thin layer of sediment settles on the lake floor; in years with heavy snowfall, the larger volume of meltwater carries more sediment into the lake, producing thicker layers. Geologist Hanna Berg found that layers deposited between about 1450 and 1600 are, on average, much thicker than those from the centuries before and after. Records from a nearby monastery describe frequent crop failures during the same period caused by long, cold winters. Taken together, these findings suggest that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"the crop failures near the monastery were caused by flooding from Lake Varn rather than by cold weather.\",\"option_b\":\"snowfall in the region was lighter between 1450 and 1600 than in the centuries before and after.\",\"option_c\":\"the region likely experienced unusually heavy snowfall and cold winters between about 1450 and 1600.\",\"option_d\":\"the sediment layers in Lake Varn grew steadily thicker every year from 1450 to 1600.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Thicker layers come from heavy snowfall, and the layers from about 1450 to 1600 are unusually thick, which points to heavy snowfall during that period. The monastery's records of long, cold winters in the same period agree with this. Together, the two lines of evidence suggest unusually snowy, cold conditions, as choice C says. Choice A contradicts the records, which blame cold winters for the crop failures. Choice B reverses the meaning of the thick layers. Choice D is too specific: Berg's finding concerns the average thickness of layers over the period, not a steady increase every year.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qalinroq qatlamlar kuchli qor yoqqan yillarda hosil bo‘ladi, 1450–1600-yillar oralig‘idagi qatlamlar esa odatdagidan ancha qalin — bu o‘sha davrda qor ko‘p yoqqanini ko‘rsatadi. Monastir yozuvlarida xuddi shu davrda uzoq va sovuq qishlar bo‘lgani qayd etilgan, bu ham shunga mos keladi. Ikkala dalil birgalikda o‘sha davrda odatdan tashqari qorli va sovuq sharoit bo‘lganini ko‘rsatadi — to‘g‘ri javob C. A yozuvlarga zid: ularda hosil nobud bo‘lishiga sovuq qishlar sabab deyilgan. B qalin qatlamlarning ma’nosini teskari tushunadi. D haddan tashqari aniq: Berg topilmasi davr bo‘yicha qatlamlarning o‘rtacha qalinligi haqida, har yili muntazam qalinlashish haqida emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In the archives of a nineteenth-century shipping company, historian Sun-mi Kwon found two versions of the logbook from an 1852 voyage: the captain's original handwritten log and a clean copy that was submitted to the company's owners. The two versions agree on nearly every detail, but the copy leaves out three days on which the original log records that the ship sailed well off its planned route so that the captain could trade privately at a port the company had not scheduled. At the time, company rules forbade captains from trading for their own profit. Kwon's findings suggest that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"the original log was written after the copy was submitted to the owners.\",\"option_b\":\"the company's owners had approved the captain's private trading in advance.\",\"option_c\":\"the captain was unaware of the company's rules about trading for profit.\",\"option_d\":\"the copy may have been edited to hide activities that broke company rules.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The copy given to the owners matches the original except for the three days of private trading, which company rules forbade. The most logical explanation is that those days were deliberately left out to conceal the rule-breaking, as choice D says. Choice A is unsupported: nothing suggests the original was written later, and as the captain's handwritten log it was presumably kept during the voyage. Choice B is unlikely: if the owners had approved the trading, there would be little reason to remove it from their copy. Choice C is undercut by the selective omission, which suggests that whoever prepared the copy knew the trading was forbidden.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Egalarga topshirilgan nusxa asl jurnal bilan deyarli bir xil, faqat kompaniya qoidalari taqiqlagan xususiy savdo qilingan uch kun tushirib qoldirilgan. Eng mantiqiy izoh — qoidabuzarlikni yashirish uchun bu kunlar ataylab olib tashlangan. To‘g‘ri javob — D. A asossiz: asl jurnal keyinroq yozilganiga hech qanday ishora yo‘q, u kapitanning qo‘lda yozilgan jurnali bo‘lgani uchun, ehtimol, safar davomida yuritilgan. B ehtimoldan uzoq: agar egalar savdoga oldindan ruxsat bergan bo‘lsa, uni ularning nusxasidan olib tashlashga sabab bo‘lmas edi. C ni aynan tanlab tushirib qoldirish rad etadi: bu nusxani tayyorlagan kishi savdo taqiqlanganini bilganini ko‘rsatadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What value of $x$ is the solution to the equation $7x - 15 = 2x + 20$?\",\"option_a\":\"$1$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{35}{9}$\",\"option_c\":\"$7$\",\"option_d\":\"$35$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Subtract $2x$ from both sides: $5x - 15 = 20$. Add $15$ to both sides: $5x = 35$. Divide both sides by $5$: $x = 7$.\\n\\nCheck: $7(7) - 15 = 34$ and $2(7) + 20 = 34$, so both sides are equal.\\n\\nChoice A is tempting if $-15$ is moved to the right side without changing its sign, which gives $5x = 20 - 15$ and $x = 1$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomondan $2x$ ni ayiramiz: $5x - 15 = 20$. Ikkala tomonga $15$ ni qo‘shamiz: $5x = 35$. Ikkala tomonni $5$ ga bo‘lamiz: $x = 7$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $7(7) - 15 = 34$ va $2(7) + 20 = 34$ — ikkala tomon teng.\\n\\nA variant — tuzoq: $-15$ ni o‘ng tomonga ishorasini o‘zgartirmasdan o‘tkazsangiz, $5x = 20 - 15$ va $x = 1$ hosil bo‘ladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A school club is ordering T-shirts for its members. The supplier charges \\\\$12 per T-shirt plus a one-time shipping fee of \\\\$36. The club's total bill was \\\\$396. How many T-shirts did the club order?\",\"option_a\":\"$30$\",\"option_b\":\"$33$\",\"option_c\":\"$36$\",\"option_d\":\"$360$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $n$ be the number of T-shirts. The total cost is $12n + 36 = 396$.\\n\\nSubtract $36$ from both sides: $12n = 360$. Divide by $12$: $n = 30$.\\n\\nChoice B ($33$) divides the whole bill by $12$, ignoring the shipping fee that is paid only once.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$n$ — futbolkalar soni bo‘lsin. Umumiy narx: $12n + 36 = 396$.\\n\\nIkkala tomondan $36$ ni ayiramiz: $12n = 360$. $12$ ga bo‘lamiz: $n = 30$.\\n\\nB variant ($33$) — butun summani $12$ ga bo‘lish natijasi; bunda faqat bir marta to‘lanadigan yetkazib berish haqi hisobga olinmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"If $5x + 3 = 23$, what is the value of $10x - 4$?\",\"option_a\":\"$4$\",\"option_b\":\"$36$\",\"option_c\":\"$42$\",\"option_d\":\"$46$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Subtract $3$ from both sides: $5x = 20$, so $x = 4$. Then $10x - 4 = 10(4) - 4 = 36$.\\n\\nFaster: $10x = 2(5x) = 2(20) = 40$, so $10x - 4 = 36$.\\n\\nChoice A ($4$) is the value of $x$, not the value of the expression $10x - 4$ that the question asks for.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomondan $3$ ni ayiramiz: $5x = 20$, demak $x = 4$. U holda $10x - 4 = 10(4) - 4 = 36$.\\n\\nQisqa yo‘l: $10x = 2(5x) = 2(20) = 40$, demak $10x - 4 = 36$.\\n\\nA variant ($4$) — bu $x$ ning qiymati, savol esa $10x - 4$ ifodaning qiymatini so‘rayapti.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What is the solution to the equation $\\\\dfrac{2x - 1}{3} = \\\\dfrac{x + 4}{2}$?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{11}{4}$\",\"option_b\":\"$5$\",\"option_c\":\"$6$\",\"option_d\":\"$14$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Multiply both sides by $6$, the least common denominator: $2(2x - 1) = 3(x + 4)$.\\n\\nDistribute: $4x - 2 = 3x + 12$. Subtract $3x$ from both sides and add $2$: $x = 14$.\\n\\nCheck: $\\\\frac{2(14) - 1}{3} = \\\\frac{27}{3} = 9$ and $\\\\frac{14 + 4}{2} = \\\\frac{18}{2} = 9$.\\n\\nChoice C ($6$) comes from multiplying only $x$ by $3$ on the right side and forgetting the $4$: $4x - 2 = 3x + 4$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomonni umumiy maxraj $6$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $2(2x - 1) = 3(x + 4)$.\\n\\nQavslarni ochamiz: $4x - 2 = 3x + 12$. Ikkala tomondan $3x$ ni ayirib, $2$ ni qo‘shamiz: $x = 14$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $\\\\frac{2(14) - 1}{3} = \\\\frac{27}{3} = 9$ va $\\\\frac{14 + 4}{2} = \\\\frac{18}{2} = 9$.\\n\\nC variant ($6$) — o‘ng tomonda faqat $x$ ni $3$ ga ko‘paytirib, $4$ ni unutish natijasi: $4x - 2 = 3x + 4$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A plumber charges a fixed fee of \\\\$60 for a house call plus \\\\$40 per hour of work. An electrician charges a fixed fee of \\\\$15 for a house call plus \\\\$55 per hour of work. For how many hours of work would the plumber and the electrician charge the same total amount?\",\"option_a\":\"$3$\",\"option_b\":\"$5$\",\"option_c\":\"$45$\",\"option_d\":\"$180$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"For $h$ hours of work, the plumber charges $60 + 40h$ dollars and the electrician charges $15 + 55h$ dollars.\\n\\nSet the totals equal: $60 + 40h = 15 + 55h$. Subtract $40h$ and $15$ from both sides: $45 = 15h$, so $h = 3$.\\n\\nCheck: for 3 hours, both charge $60 + 120 = 15 + 165 = 180$ dollars.\\n\\nChoice D ($180$) is the equal total charge in dollars, not the number of hours the question asks for.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$h$ soatlik ish uchun santexnik $60 + 40h$ dollar, elektrik esa $15 + 55h$ dollar oladi.\\n\\nUlarni tenglashtiramiz: $60 + 40h = 15 + 55h$. Ikkala tomondan $40h$ va $15$ ni ayiramiz: $45 = 15h$, demak $h = 3$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: 3 soat uchun ikkalasi ham $60 + 120 = 15 + 165 = 180$ dollar oladi.\\n\\nD variant ($180$) — bu soatlar soni emas, balki teng bo‘lgan umumiy to‘lov (dollarda).\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\frac{2}{3}(x + 5) = \\\\frac{1}{4}x + 3$$\\n\\nWhat is the solution to the given equation?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"-4/5\",\"-.8\",\"-0.8\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Multiply both sides by $12$ to clear the fractions: $8(x + 5) = 3x + 36$.\\n\\nDistribute: $8x + 40 = 3x + 36$. Subtract $3x$ and $40$ from both sides: $5x = -4$, so $x = -\\\\frac{4}{5}$. Enter -4/5 or -.8.\\n\\nA common mistake is multiplying only $\\\\frac{1}{4}x$ by $12$ and not the constant $3$, which gives $8x + 40 = 3x + 3$ and the wrong value $x = -\\\\frac{37}{5}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kasrlardan qutulish uchun ikkala tomonni $12$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $8(x + 5) = 3x + 36$.\\n\\nQavsni ochamiz: $8x + 40 = 3x + 36$. Ikkala tomondan $3x$ va $40$ ni ayiramiz: $5x = -4$, demak $x = -\\\\frac{4}{5}$. Javobni -4/5 yoki -.8 shaklida kiriting.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $12$ ga faqat $\\\\frac{1}{4}x$ ni ko‘paytirib, ozod had $3$ ni unutish. Unda $8x + 40 = 3x + 3$ va noto‘g‘ri javob $x = -\\\\frac{37}{5}$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$a(3x - 2) + 5x = 17x - b$$\\n\\nIn the given equation, $a$ and $b$ are constants. If the equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $a + b$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"12\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Expand the left side: $3ax - 2a + 5x = (3a + 5)x - 2a$.\\n\\nAn equation has infinitely many solutions only when both sides are identical, so the coefficients of $x$ and the constant terms must match: $3a + 5 = 17$ and $-2a = -b$.\\n\\nFrom $3a + 5 = 17$, $a = 4$. Then $b = 2a = 8$, so $a + b = 4 + 8 = 12$.\\n\\nA tempting slip is writing $b = -2a = -8$ (losing a negative sign), which gives the wrong sum $-4$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Chap tomondagi qavsni ochamiz: $3ax - 2a + 5x = (3a + 5)x - 2a$.\\n\\nTenglama cheksiz ko‘p yechimga ega bo‘lishi uchun ikkala tomon aynan bir xil bo‘lishi kerak: $x$ oldidagi koeffitsiyentlar ham, ozod hadlar ham teng: $3a + 5 = 17$ va $-2a = -b$.\\n\\n$3a + 5 = 17$ dan $a = 4$. U holda $b = 2a = 8$, demak $a + b = 4 + 8 = 12$.\\n\\nTuzoq: manfiy ishorani yo‘qotib $b = -2a = -8$ deb yozsangiz, noto‘g‘ri yig‘indi $-4$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\frac{1}{2}(ax + 6) - 4 = 3x - b$$\\n\\nIn the given equation, $a$ and $b$ are constants. If the equation has no solution, which of the following must be true?\",\"option_a\":\"$a = 3$ and $b \\\\ne 1$\",\"option_b\":\"$a = 6$ and $b = 1$\",\"option_c\":\"$a = 6$ and $b \\\\ne -2$\",\"option_d\":\"$a = 6$ and $b \\\\ne 1$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Simplify the left side: $\\\\frac{1}{2}(ax + 6) - 4 = \\\\frac{a}{2}x + 3 - 4 = \\\\frac{a}{2}x - 1$. The equation becomes $\\\\frac{a}{2}x - 1 = 3x - b$.\\n\\nA linear equation has no solution when the coefficients of $x$ are equal but the constant terms are different.\\n\\nEqual coefficients: $\\\\frac{a}{2} = 3$, so $a = 6$. Different constants: $-1 \\\\ne -b$, so $b \\\\ne 1$. (If $b = 1$, both sides would be identical and the equation would have infinitely many solutions, which rules out choice B.)\\n\\nChoice C comes from multiplying only $ax$ by $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ and not the $6$, which gives the constant $6 - 4 = 2$ and the incorrect condition $b \\\\ne -2$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Chap tomonni soddalashtiramiz: $\\\\frac{1}{2}(ax + 6) - 4 = \\\\frac{a}{2}x + 3 - 4 = \\\\frac{a}{2}x - 1$. Tenglama $\\\\frac{a}{2}x - 1 = 3x - b$ ko‘rinishiga keladi.\\n\\nChiziqli tenglamaning yechimi yo‘q bo‘lishi uchun $x$ oldidagi koeffitsiyentlar teng, ozod hadlar esa har xil bo‘lishi kerak.\\n\\nKoeffitsiyentlar teng: $\\\\frac{a}{2} = 3$, demak $a = 6$. Ozod hadlar har xil: $-1 \\\\ne -b$, demak $b \\\\ne 1$. ($b = 1$ bo‘lsa, ikkala tomon bir xil bo‘lib, tenglama cheksiz ko‘p yechimga ega bo‘ladi — shuning uchun B variant ham noto‘g‘ri.)\\n\\nC variant — $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ ni faqat $ax$ ga ko‘paytirib, $6$ ga ko‘paytirmaslik natijasi: unda ozod had $6 - 4 = 2$ bo‘lib, noto‘g‘ri shart $b \\\\ne -2$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which point $(x, y)$ lies on the graph of $3x - 2y = 12$ in the $xy$-plane?\",\"option_a\":\"$(2, -3)$\",\"option_b\":\"$(2, 3)$\",\"option_c\":\"$(0, 6)$\",\"option_d\":\"$(-4, 0)$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute each point into $3x - 2y$. For $(2, -3)$: $3(2) - 2(-3) = 6 + 6 = 12$, so this point is on the graph.\\n\\nThe others fail: $(2, 3)$ gives $6 - 6 = 0$; $(0, 6)$ gives $0 - 12 = -12$; $(-4, 0)$ gives $-12 - 0 = -12$.\\n\\nChoice C is tempting if the $y$-intercept is found with a sign error: setting $x = 0$ gives $-2y = 12$, so $y = -6$, not $6$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir nuqtani $3x - 2y$ ifodaga qo‘yamiz. $(2, -3)$ uchun: $3(2) - 2(-3) = 6 + 6 = 12$, demak bu nuqta grafikda yotadi.\\n\\nQolganlari mos kelmaydi: $(2, 3)$ uchun $6 - 6 = 0$; $(0, 6)$ uchun $0 - 12 = -12$; $(-4, 0)$ uchun $-12 - 0 = -12$.\\n\\nC variant — tuzoq: $x = 0$ bo‘lganda $-2y = 12$, ya’ni $y = -6$ bo‘ladi, $6$ emas. Ishorani yo‘qotsangiz, shu variantni tanlab qo‘yasiz.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A bakery sells muffins for \\\\$3 each and loaves of bread for \\\\$5 each. On Monday, the bakery's sales of muffins and loaves of bread totaled \\\\$420. If $m$ is the number of muffins sold and $b$ is the number of loaves of bread sold on Monday, which equation represents this situation?\",\"option_a\":\"$3m + 5b = 420$\",\"option_b\":\"$5m + 3b = 420$\",\"option_c\":\"$m + b = 420$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{m}{3} + \\\\frac{b}{5} = 420$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The muffins bring in $3m$ dollars and the loaves of bread bring in $5b$ dollars. Together they total $420$ dollars: $3m + 5b = 420$.\\n\\nChoice B attaches each price to the wrong item: muffins cost \\\\$3 each, so the muffin term must be $3m$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Keksdan $3m$ dollar, nondan esa $5b$ dollar tushum bo‘ladi. Ularning yig‘indisi $420$ dollar: $3m + 5b = 420$.\\n\\nB variantda narxlar almashib qolgan: keks \\\\$3 turadi, shuning uchun keks hadi $3m$ bo‘lishi kerak.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, the graph of $y = -\\\\frac{2}{5}x + 6$ crosses the $x$-axis at the point $(a, 0)$. What is the value of $a$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-15$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{12}{5}$\",\"option_c\":\"$6$\",\"option_d\":\"$15$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"On the $x$-axis, $y = 0$. So $0 = -\\\\frac{2}{5}a + 6$, which gives $\\\\frac{2}{5}a = 6$ and $a = 6 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{5}{2} = 15$.\\n\\nChoice C ($6$) is the $y$-intercept, where the line crosses the $y$-axis, not the $x$-axis.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x$ o‘qida $y = 0$ bo‘ladi. Demak $0 = -\\\\frac{2}{5}a + 6$, bundan $\\\\frac{2}{5}a = 6$ va $a = 6 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{5}{2} = 15$.\\n\\nC variant ($6$) — chiziq $x$ o‘qini emas, $y$ o‘qini kesib o‘tadigan nuqtaning ordinatasi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What is the slope of the line with equation $4x + 7y = 21$ in the $xy$-plane?\",\"option_a\":\"$-\\\\frac{7}{4}$\",\"option_b\":\"$-\\\\frac{4}{7}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{4}{7}$\",\"option_d\":\"$3$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Solve for $y$: $7y = -4x + 21$, so $y = -\\\\frac{4}{7}x + 3$. The slope is the coefficient of $x$: $-\\\\frac{4}{7}$.\\n\\nChoice C forgets that $4x$ becomes $-4x$ when it is moved to the other side; choice D ($3$) is the $y$-intercept, not the slope.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tenglamani $y$ ga nisbatan yechamiz: $7y = -4x + 21$, demak $y = -\\\\frac{4}{7}x + 3$. Qiyalik — $x$ oldidagi koeffitsiyent: $-\\\\frac{4}{7}$.\\n\\nC variantda $4x$ ni boshqa tomonga o‘tkazganda ishora o‘zgarishi unutilgan; D variant ($3$) esa qiyalik emas, $y$ o‘qini kesish nuqtasi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A line in the $xy$-plane passes through the points $(-3, 8)$ and $(5, -4)$. What is the $y$-coordinate of the $y$-intercept of the line?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"7/2\",\"3.5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The slope is $\\\\frac{-4 - 8}{5 - (-3)} = \\\\frac{-12}{8} = -\\\\frac{3}{2}$.\\n\\nMoving from $x = -3$ to $x = 0$ increases $x$ by $3$, so $y$ changes by $3 \\\\cdot \\\\left(-\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\right) = -\\\\frac{9}{2}$. The $y$-intercept is $8 - \\\\frac{9}{2} = \\\\frac{7}{2}$. Enter 7/2 or 3.5.\\n\\nCheck with the other point: $-\\\\frac{3}{2}(5) + \\\\frac{7}{2} = -\\\\frac{15}{2} + \\\\frac{7}{2} = -4$.\\n\\nA common mistake is writing $5 - 3 = 2$ in the denominator instead of $5 - (-3) = 8$, which gives a slope of $-6$ and the wrong intercept $-10$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qiyalik: $\\\\frac{-4 - 8}{5 - (-3)} = \\\\frac{-12}{8} = -\\\\frac{3}{2}$.\\n\\n$x = -3$ dan $x = 0$ ga o‘tganda $x$ $3$ ga oshadi, demak $y$ $3 \\\\cdot \\\\left(-\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\right) = -\\\\frac{9}{2}$ ga o‘zgaradi. $y$ o‘qini kesish nuqtasi: $8 - \\\\frac{9}{2} = \\\\frac{7}{2}$. Javobni 7/2 yoki 3.5 shaklida kiriting.\\n\\nIkkinchi nuqta bilan tekshiramiz: $-\\\\frac{3}{2}(5) + \\\\frac{7}{2} = -\\\\frac{15}{2} + \\\\frac{7}{2} = -4$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — maxrajda $5 - (-3) = 8$ o‘rniga $5 - 3 = 2$ yozish. Unda qiyalik $-6$ va noto‘g‘ri javob $-10$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Line $k$ is perpendicular to the line $2x - 5y = 10$ in the $xy$-plane and passes through the point $(4, 1)$. Which equation defines line $k$?\",\"option_a\":\"$y = \\\\frac{2}{5}x - \\\\frac{3}{5}$\",\"option_b\":\"$y = -\\\\frac{2}{5}x + \\\\frac{13}{5}$\",\"option_c\":\"$y = \\\\frac{5}{2}x - 9$\",\"option_d\":\"$y = -\\\\frac{5}{2}x + 11$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Rewrite the given line in slope-intercept form: $-5y = -2x + 10$, so $y = \\\\frac{2}{5}x - 2$. Its slope is $\\\\frac{2}{5}$.\\n\\nA perpendicular line has the negative reciprocal slope, $-\\\\frac{5}{2}$. Through $(4, 1)$: $y - 1 = -\\\\frac{5}{2}(x - 4)$, so $y = -\\\\frac{5}{2}x + 10 + 1 = -\\\\frac{5}{2}x + 11$.\\n\\nChoice C takes the reciprocal $\\\\frac{5}{2}$ but forgets to change the sign; choice A is the line through $(4, 1)$ that is parallel, not perpendicular, to the given line.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Berilgan chiziqni $y = mx + b$ ko‘rinishiga keltiramiz: $-5y = -2x + 10$, demak $y = \\\\frac{2}{5}x - 2$. Uning qiyaligi $\\\\frac{2}{5}$.\\n\\nPerpendikulyar chiziqning qiyaligi — teskari va qarama-qarshi ishorali son: $-\\\\frac{5}{2}$. $(4, 1)$ nuqtadan o‘tadi: $y - 1 = -\\\\frac{5}{2}(x - 4)$, demak $y = -\\\\frac{5}{2}x + 10 + 1 = -\\\\frac{5}{2}x + 11$.\\n\\nC variantda teskari son $\\\\frac{5}{2}$ olingan, lekin ishora o‘zgartirilmagan; A variant esa $(4, 1)$ dan o‘tuvchi parallel chiziq, perpendikulyar emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A café spends exactly \\\\$540 each week on milk and coffee beans. Milk costs \\\\$1.20 per liter and coffee beans cost \\\\$18 per kilogram, so $1.2m + 18c = 540$, where $m$ is the number of liters of milk and $c$ is the number of kilograms of coffee beans the café buys in a week. Next week, the café will buy $3$ more kilograms of coffee beans than it bought this week and will still spend exactly \\\\$540. How many fewer liters of milk will the café buy next week than this week?\",\"option_a\":\"$0.2$\",\"option_b\":\"$3.6$\",\"option_c\":\"$45$\",\"option_d\":\"$54$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Buying $3$ more kilograms of coffee beans costs an extra $18 \\\\cdot 3 = 54$ dollars.\\n\\nSince the total stays at $540$ dollars, spending on milk must decrease by $54$ dollars, which is $\\\\frac{54}{1.2} = 45$ liters.\\n\\nAlgebraically: if the milk decreases by $d$ liters, then $1.2(m - d) + 18(c + 3) = 540$. Subtracting $1.2m + 18c = 540$ gives $-1.2d + 54 = 0$, so $d = 45$.\\n\\nChoice D ($54$) is the change in spending in dollars, not the change in the number of liters of milk.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$3$ kilogramm qo‘shimcha kofe donasi $18 \\\\cdot 3 = 54$ dollar qo‘shimcha xarajat demakdir.\\n\\nUmumiy xarajat $540$ dollarligicha qolgani uchun sutga sarflanadigan pul $54$ dollarga kamayishi kerak, bu $\\\\frac{54}{1.2} = 45$ litr.\\n\\nAlgebraik usul: sut $d$ litrga kamaysa, $1.2(m - d) + 18(c + 3) = 540$. Bundan $1.2m + 18c = 540$ ni ayirsak, $-1.2d + 54 = 0$, demak $d = 45$.\\n\\nD variant ($54$) — sut litrlaridagi emas, dollardagi o‘zgarish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, a line with slope $-2$ passes through the points $(1, 5)$ and $(k, 2k)$, where $k$ is a constant. What is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"7/4\",\"1.75\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Use the slope formula: $\\\\frac{2k - 5}{k - 1} = -2$.\\n\\nMultiply both sides by $k - 1$: $2k - 5 = -2k + 2$. Then $4k = 7$, so $k = \\\\frac{7}{4}$. Enter 7/4 or 1.75.\\n\\nCheck: the second point is $\\\\left(\\\\frac{7}{4}, \\\\frac{7}{2}\\\\right)$, and $\\\\frac{\\\\frac{7}{2} - 5}{\\\\frac{7}{4} - 1} = \\\\frac{-\\\\frac{3}{2}}{\\\\frac{3}{4}} = -2$.\\n\\nA common slip is distributing $-2(k - 1)$ as $-2k - 2$, which gives $4k = 3$ and the wrong value $\\\\frac{3}{4}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qiyalik formulasidan foydalanamiz: $\\\\frac{2k - 5}{k - 1} = -2$.\\n\\nIkkala tomonni $k - 1$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $2k - 5 = -2k + 2$. Bundan $4k = 7$, demak $k = \\\\frac{7}{4}$. Javobni 7/4 yoki 1.75 shaklida kiriting.\\n\\nTekshiruv: ikkinchi nuqta $\\\\left(\\\\frac{7}{4}, \\\\frac{7}{2}\\\\right)$, va $\\\\frac{\\\\frac{7}{2} - 5}{\\\\frac{7}{4} - 1} = \\\\frac{-\\\\frac{3}{2}}{\\\\frac{3}{4}} = -2$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $-2(k - 1)$ ni $-2k - 2$ deb ochish. Unda $4k = 3$ va noto‘g‘ri javob $\\\\frac{3}{4}$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":125,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = 4x - 9$. What is the value of $f(-3)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-21$\",\"option_b\":\"$-3$\",\"option_c\":\"$3$\",\"option_d\":\"$21$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $-3$ for $x$: $f(-3) = 4(-3) - 9 = -12 - 9 = -21$.\\n\\nChoice B ($-3$) comes from adding $9$ instead of subtracting it: $-12 + 9 = -3$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x$ o‘rniga $-3$ ni qo‘yamiz: $f(-3) = 4(-3) - 9 = -12 - 9 = -21$.\\n\\nB variant ($-3$) — $9$ ni ayirish o‘rniga qo‘shish natijasi: $-12 + 9 = -3$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A candle burns at a constant rate after it is lit. The function $h(t) = 30 - 2.5t$ gives the height $h$, in centimeters, of the candle $t$ hours after it is lit. What is the best interpretation of $2.5$ in this context?\",\"option_a\":\"The candle is $2.5$ centimeters tall when it is first lit.\",\"option_b\":\"The candle burns out $2.5$ hours after it is lit.\",\"option_c\":\"The candle is $2.5$ centimeters tall $1$ hour after it is lit.\",\"option_d\":\"The height of the candle decreases by $2.5$ centimeters each hour.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"In $h(t) = 30 - 2.5t$, the coefficient of $t$ is the rate of change. Each time $t$ increases by $1$ hour, $h$ changes by $-2.5$, so the candle becomes $2.5$ centimeters shorter every hour.\\n\\nThe constant $30$ is the height when $t = 0$, and the candle burns out when $h(t) = 0$, which happens at $t = 12$ hours.\\n\\nChoice A describes the initial height, but the initial height is given by the constant term $30$, not by $2.5$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$h(t) = 30 - 2.5t$ da $t$ oldidagi koeffitsiyent — o‘zgarish tezligi. $t$ har safar $1$ soatga oshganda $h$ $2.5$ ga kamayadi, ya’ni sham har soatda $2.5$ santimetrga qisqaradi.\\n\\nOzod had $30$ — $t = 0$ dagi balandlik; sham esa $h(t) = 0$ bo‘lganda, ya’ni $t = 12$ soatda yonib tugaydi.\\n\\nA variant boshlang‘ich balandlikni tasvirlaydi, lekin boshlang‘ich balandlik $2.5$ emas, ozod had $30$ ga teng.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $p$ is defined by $p(x) = \\\\frac{2}{3}x + 8$. For what value of $x$ is $p(x) = 20$?\",\"option_a\":\"$8$\",\"option_b\":\"$12$\",\"option_c\":\"$18$\",\"option_d\":\"$42$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Set $\\\\frac{2}{3}x + 8 = 20$. Subtract $8$ from both sides: $\\\\frac{2}{3}x = 12$. Multiply both sides by $\\\\frac{3}{2}$: $x = 18$.\\n\\nCheck: $p(18) = \\\\frac{2}{3}(18) + 8 = 12 + 8 = 20$.\\n\\nChoice B ($12$) is the value of $\\\\frac{2}{3}x$, which is one step before the value of $x$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$\\\\frac{2}{3}x + 8 = 20$ tenglamani tuzamiz. Ikkala tomondan $8$ ni ayiramiz: $\\\\frac{2}{3}x = 12$. Ikkala tomonni $\\\\frac{3}{2}$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $x = 18$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $p(18) = \\\\frac{2}{3}(18) + 8 = 12 + 8 = 20$.\\n\\nB variant ($12$) — bu $\\\\frac{2}{3}x$ ning qiymati, ya’ni $x$ ni topishdan bir qadam oldingi natija.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"For the linear function $f$, $f(3) = 14$ and $f(7) = 26$. What is the value of $f(12)$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"41\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The slope is $\\\\frac{26 - 14}{7 - 3} = \\\\frac{12}{4} = 3$, so $f(x)$ increases by $3$ each time $x$ increases by $1$.\\n\\nFrom $x = 7$ to $x = 12$, $x$ increases by $5$, so $f(12) = 26 + 5(3) = 41$. (Equivalently, $f(x) = 3x + 5$, and $f(12) = 36 + 5 = 41$.)\\n\\nA common mistake is to compute the slope upside down, $\\\\frac{7 - 3}{26 - 14} = \\\\frac{1}{3}$, which gives $f(12) = 26 + 5 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{3} \\\\approx 27.67$ instead of $41$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qiyalik: $\\\\frac{26 - 14}{7 - 3} = \\\\frac{12}{4} = 3$, ya’ni $x$ har safar $1$ ga oshganda $f(x)$ $3$ ga oshadi.\\n\\n$x = 7$ dan $x = 12$ gacha $x$ $5$ ga oshadi, demak $f(12) = 26 + 5(3) = 41$. (Boshqacha: $f(x) = 3x + 5$ va $f(12) = 36 + 5 = 41$.)\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — qiyalikni teskari hisoblash: $\\\\frac{7 - 3}{26 - 14} = \\\\frac{1}{3}$. Unda $f(12) = 26 + 5 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{3} \\\\approx 27.67$ chiqadi, $41$ emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The daily cost $C$, in dollars, to rent a moving truck is a linear function of the number of miles $m$ the truck is driven. Renting the truck for a day and driving it $40$ miles costs \\\\$68, and renting it for a day and driving it $120$ miles costs \\\\$88. Which equation gives $C$ in terms of $m$?\",\"option_a\":\"$C = 0.25m + 58$\",\"option_b\":\"$C = 0.25m + 68$\",\"option_c\":\"$C = 4m + 58$\",\"option_d\":\"$C = 58m + 0.25$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The slope is $\\\\frac{88 - 68}{120 - 40} = \\\\frac{20}{80} = 0.25$ dollar per mile.\\n\\nUse the point $(40, 68)$ to find the constant: $68 = 0.25(40) + b = 10 + b$, so $b = 58$. Therefore $C = 0.25m + 58$. Check: $0.25(120) + 58 = 30 + 58 = 88$.\\n\\nChoice B uses \\\\$68 as the starting value, but \\\\$68 is the cost after $40$ miles, not the cost for $0$ miles.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qiyalik: $\\\\frac{88 - 68}{120 - 40} = \\\\frac{20}{80} = 0.25$ dollar/mil.\\n\\nOzod hadni $(40, 68)$ nuqta yordamida topamiz: $68 = 0.25(40) + b = 10 + b$, demak $b = 58$. Shunday qilib, $C = 0.25m + 58$. Tekshiruv: $0.25(120) + 58 = 30 + 58 = 88$.\\n\\nB variant \\\\$68 ni boshlang‘ich qiymat deb oladi, lekin \\\\$68 — $0$ mil emas, $40$ mil yurilgandagi narx.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The cost $C$, in dollars, to print $n$ copies of a brochure is given by $C(n) = 0.25n + 30$. A school increased the size of its brochure order, and as a result, the cost of the order increased by \\\\$12. By how many copies did the order increase?\",\"option_a\":\"$3$\",\"option_b\":\"$48$\",\"option_c\":\"$120$\",\"option_d\":\"$168$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Each additional copy adds $0.25$ dollar to the cost; the fixed $30$ dollars does not change. If the order increases by $k$ copies, the cost increases by $0.25k$ dollars.\\n\\nSo $0.25k = 12$, which gives $k = \\\\frac{12}{0.25} = 48$ copies.\\n\\nChoice A ($3$) multiplies $12$ by $0.25$ instead of dividing $12$ by $0.25$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir qo‘shimcha nusxa narxga $0.25$ dollar qo‘shadi; doimiy $30$ dollar o‘zgarmaydi. Buyurtma $k$ nusxaga oshsa, narx $0.25k$ dollarga oshadi.\\n\\nDemak $0.25k = 12$, bundan $k = \\\\frac{12}{0.25} = 48$ nusxa.\\n\\nA variant ($3$) — $12$ ni $0.25$ ga bo‘lish o‘rniga ko‘paytirish natijasi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"For the linear function $k$, $k(5) - k(1) = 18$ and $k(3) = 2$. What is the value of $k(-1)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-70$\",\"option_b\":\"$-16$\",\"option_c\":\"$-\\\\frac{23}{2}$\",\"option_d\":\"$20$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"From $x = 1$ to $x = 5$, $x$ increases by $4$ and $k(x)$ increases by $18$, so the slope is $\\\\frac{18}{4} = 4.5$.\\n\\nFrom $x = 3$ to $x = -1$, $x$ decreases by $4$, so $k(x)$ decreases by $4(4.5) = 18$. Therefore $k(-1) = 2 - 18 = -16$.\\n\\nChoice A treats $18$ as the slope (the change for a $1$-unit step), which gives $2 - 4(18) = -70$; choice C is $k(0)$, not $k(-1)$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x = 1$ dan $x = 5$ gacha $x$ $4$ ga oshadi, $k(x)$ esa $18$ ga oshadi, demak qiyalik $\\\\frac{18}{4} = 4.5$.\\n\\n$x = 3$ dan $x = -1$ gacha $x$ $4$ ga kamayadi, shuning uchun $k(x)$ $4(4.5) = 18$ ga kamayadi. Demak $k(-1) = 2 - 18 = -16$.\\n\\nA variant $18$ ni qiyalik (ya’ni $1$ birlik qadamdagi o‘zgarish) deb oladi va $2 - 4(18) = -70$ hosil qiladi; C variant esa $k(-1)$ emas, $k(0)$ ning qiymati.\",\"estimated_seconds\":115,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"For the linear function $f$, $f(2) = 3 \\\\cdot f(0)$ and $f(4) = 21$. What is the value of $f(0)$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"21/5\",\"4.2\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Write $f(x) = mx + b$, so $f(0) = b$.\\n\\nThe condition $f(2) = 3 \\\\cdot f(0)$ gives $2m + b = 3b$, so $2m = 2b$ and $m = b$.\\n\\nThen $f(4) = 4m + b = 4b + b = 5b = 21$, so $b = \\\\frac{21}{5} = 4.2$. Enter 21/5 or 4.2.\\n\\nA common error is to read $f(2) = 3 \\\\cdot f(0)$ as “the slope is $3$,” which leads to $f(x) = 3x + 9$ and the wrong answer $9$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$f(x) = mx + b$ deb yozamiz, unda $f(0) = b$.\\n\\n$f(2) = 3 \\\\cdot f(0)$ shartidan $2m + b = 3b$, ya’ni $2m = 2b$ va $m = b$.\\n\\nU holda $f(4) = 4m + b = 4b + b = 5b = 21$, demak $b = \\\\frac{21}{5} = 4.2$. Javobni 21/5 yoki 4.2 shaklida kiriting.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $f(2) = 3 \\\\cdot f(0)$ shartini «qiyalik $3$ ga teng» deb tushunish. Unda $f(x) = 3x + 9$ va noto‘g‘ri javob $9$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following values of $x$ satisfies the inequality $-7 \\\\le 3x + 2 < 11$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-4$\",\"option_b\":\"$-3$\",\"option_c\":\"$3$\",\"option_d\":\"$4$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Subtract $2$ from all three parts: $-9 \\\\le 3x < 9$. Divide all three parts by $3$: $-3 \\\\le x < 3$.\\n\\nOnly $-3$ is in this interval. It is included because the left inequality uses $\\\\le$: $3(-3) + 2 = -7$, and $-7 \\\\le -7$ is true.\\n\\nChoice C ($3$) is excluded because the right inequality is strict: $3(3) + 2 = 11$, and $11 < 11$ is false.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Uchala qismdan $2$ ni ayiramiz: $-9 \\\\le 3x < 9$. Uchala qismni $3$ ga bo‘lamiz: $-3 \\\\le x < 3$.\\n\\nVariantlardan faqat $-3$ shu oraliqda. U kiradi, chunki chap tomonda $\\\\le$ belgisi bor: $3(-3) + 2 = -7$ va $-7 \\\\le -7$ to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nC variant ($3$) kirmaydi, chunki o‘ng tomondagi tengsizlik qat’iy: $3(3) + 2 = 11$, $11 < 11$ esa noto‘g‘ri.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"To qualify for free shipping, an online order must total at least \\\\$75. Aziz has already placed items worth \\\\$41.50 in his cart. He wants to add bottles of shampoo that cost \\\\$6.70 each. Which inequality represents the numbers of bottles of shampoo, $b$, that Aziz can add so that his order qualifies for free shipping?\",\"option_a\":\"$41.50 + 6.70b \\\\le 75$\",\"option_b\":\"$6.70b \\\\ge 75$\",\"option_c\":\"$6.70 + 41.50b \\\\ge 75$\",\"option_d\":\"$41.50 + 6.70b \\\\ge 75$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The order total is the amount already in the cart plus the cost of the shampoo: $41.50 + 6.70b$ dollars.\\n\\n“At least \\\\$75” means greater than or equal to $75$, so $41.50 + 6.70b \\\\ge 75$.\\n\\nChoice A uses $\\\\le$, which would mean the total is at most \\\\$75, the opposite of “at least.”\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Buyurtma summasi — savatdagi mahsulotlar narxi va shampunlar narxining yig‘indisi: $41.50 + 6.70b$ dollar.\\n\\n«Kamida \\\\$75» — $75$ dan katta yoki teng degani, shuning uchun $41.50 + 6.70b \\\\ge 75$.\\n\\nA variantda $\\\\le$ belgisi ishlatilgan; bu «ko‘pi bilan \\\\$75» degan ma’noni beradi, ya’ni «kamida» ning aksi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What is the greatest integer $x$ that satisfies the inequality $4x - 9 \\\\le 2x + 8$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-1$\",\"option_b\":\"$2$\",\"option_c\":\"$8$\",\"option_d\":\"$9$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Subtract $2x$ from both sides: $2x - 9 \\\\le 8$. Add $9$: $2x \\\\le 17$. Divide by $2$: $x \\\\le 8.5$.\\n\\nThe greatest integer that is less than or equal to $8.5$ is $8$.\\n\\nChoice D ($9$) rounds $8.5$ up, but $9$ does not satisfy the inequality: $4(9) - 9 = 27$, which is greater than $2(9) + 8 = 26$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomondan $2x$ ni ayiramiz: $2x - 9 \\\\le 8$. $9$ ni qo‘shamiz: $2x \\\\le 17$. $2$ ga bo‘lamiz: $x \\\\le 8.5$.\\n\\n$8.5$ dan katta bo‘lmagan eng katta butun son — $8$.\\n\\nD variant ($9$) — $8.5$ ni yuqoriga yaxlitlash natijasi, lekin $9$ tengsizlikni qanoatlantirmaydi: $4(9) - 9 = 27$, bu esa $2(9) + 8 = 26$ dan katta.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} y &\\\\ge 3x - 4 \\\\\\\\ x + 2y &< 10 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nWhich point $(x, y)$ is a solution to the given system of inequalities?\",\"option_a\":\"$(1, 3)$\",\"option_b\":\"$(2, 4)$\",\"option_c\":\"$(3, 2)$\",\"option_d\":\"$(4, 9)$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Test each point in both inequalities.\\n\\n$(1, 3)$: $3 \\\\ge 3(1) - 4 = -1$ is true, and $1 + 2(3) = 7 < 10$ is true, so $(1, 3)$ is a solution.\\n\\n$(2, 4)$: $4 \\\\ge 2$ is true, but $2 + 2(4) = 10$, and $10 < 10$ is false. $(3, 2)$: $2 \\\\ge 5$ is false. $(4, 9)$: $9 \\\\ge 8$ is true, but $4 + 18 = 22 < 10$ is false.\\n\\nChoice B is tempting because it lies on the boundary line $x + 2y = 10$, but that line is not included in the solution region because the inequality is strict.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir nuqtani ikkala tengsizlikka qo‘yib tekshiramiz.\\n\\n$(1, 3)$: $3 \\\\ge 3(1) - 4 = -1$ to‘g‘ri va $1 + 2(3) = 7 < 10$ to‘g‘ri, demak $(1, 3)$ — yechim.\\n\\n$(2, 4)$: $4 \\\\ge 2$ to‘g‘ri, lekin $2 + 2(4) = 10$ va $10 < 10$ noto‘g‘ri. $(3, 2)$: $2 \\\\ge 5$ noto‘g‘ri. $(4, 9)$: $9 \\\\ge 8$ to‘g‘ri, lekin $4 + 18 = 22 < 10$ noto‘g‘ri.\\n\\nB variant — tuzoq: u $x + 2y = 10$ chegara chizig‘ida yotadi, lekin tengsizlik qat’iy bo‘lgani uchun chegara chizig‘i yechimlar sohasiga kirmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A charity concert costs \\\\$2,350 to organize. Tickets sell for \\\\$18 each, and a local business donates \\\\$400 to the concert. What is the minimum number of tickets that must be sold so that the ticket sales plus the donation are at least the cost of organizing the concert?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"109\"],\"explanation_en\":\"If $t$ tickets are sold, the money collected is $18t + 400$ dollars. It must be at least the cost: $18t + 400 \\\\ge 2{,}350$.\\n\\nSubtract $400$: $18t \\\\ge 1{,}950$. Divide by $18$: $t \\\\ge 108.33\\\\ldots$\\n\\nThe number of tickets must be a whole number, so the minimum is $109$. Check: $18(108) + 400 = 2{,}344$ is less than $2{,}350$, but $18(109) + 400 = 2{,}362$ is enough.\\n\\nEntering $108$ (rounding down) is a common error: $108$ tickets leave the concert \\\\$6 short.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$t$ ta chipta sotilsa, yig‘ilgan pul $18t + 400$ dollar bo‘ladi. U xarajatdan kam bo‘lmasligi kerak: $18t + 400 \\\\ge 2{,}350$.\\n\\n$400$ ni ayiramiz: $18t \\\\ge 1{,}950$. $18$ ga bo‘lamiz: $t \\\\ge 108.33\\\\ldots$\\n\\nChiptalar soni butun son bo‘lishi kerak, shuning uchun eng kichik qiymat $109$. Tekshiruv: $18(108) + 400 = 2{,}344$ — bu $2{,}350$ dan kam, $18(109) + 400 = 2{,}362$ esa yetarli.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — pastga yaxlitlab $108$ ni kiritish: $108$ ta chipta bilan \\\\$6 yetmay qoladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following inequalities is equivalent to $-\\\\frac{2}{3}(x - 6) \\\\ge x + 9$?\",\"option_a\":\"$x \\\\ge 3$\",\"option_b\":\"$x \\\\ge -3$\",\"option_c\":\"$x \\\\le -9$\",\"option_d\":\"$x \\\\le -3$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Distribute: $-\\\\frac{2}{3}x + 4 \\\\ge x + 9$. Subtract $x$ and $4$ from both sides: $-\\\\frac{5}{3}x \\\\ge 5$.\\n\\nMultiply both sides by $-\\\\frac{3}{5}$. Multiplying by a negative number reverses the inequality sign: $x \\\\le -3$.\\n\\nCheck with $x = -6$: $-\\\\frac{2}{3}(-12) = 8$ and $-6 + 9 = 3$, and $8 \\\\ge 3$ is true.\\n\\nChoice B is the result of forgetting to reverse the inequality sign when multiplying by a negative number.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qavsni ochamiz: $-\\\\frac{2}{3}x + 4 \\\\ge x + 9$. Ikkala tomondan $x$ va $4$ ni ayiramiz: $-\\\\frac{5}{3}x \\\\ge 5$.\\n\\nIkkala tomonni $-\\\\frac{3}{5}$ ga ko‘paytiramiz. Manfiy songa ko‘paytirganda tengsizlik belgisi teskarisiga o‘zgaradi: $x \\\\le -3$.\\n\\nTekshiruv, $x = -6$: $-\\\\frac{2}{3}(-12) = 8$ va $-6 + 9 = 3$; $8 \\\\ge 3$ to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nB variant — manfiy songa ko‘paytirganda tengsizlik belgisini aylantirishni unutish natijasi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A bakery has $50$ kilograms of flour for today's baking. Each loaf of bread uses $0.4$ kilogram of flour, and each cake uses $0.75$ kilogram of flour. The bakery must bake at least $30$ loaves of bread today. What is the maximum number of cakes the bakery can bake today without using more than $50$ kilograms of flour?\",\"option_a\":\"$26$\",\"option_b\":\"$50$\",\"option_c\":\"$51$\",\"option_d\":\"$66$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"If the bakery bakes $\\\\ell$ loaves and $c$ cakes, then $0.4\\\\ell + 0.75c \\\\le 50$ and $\\\\ell \\\\ge 30$.\\n\\nTo bake as many cakes as possible, bake the fewest loaves allowed, $\\\\ell = 30$, which uses $0.4(30) = 12$ kilograms of flour. Then $0.75c \\\\le 38$, so $c \\\\le 50.66\\\\ldots$\\n\\nThe number of cakes is a whole number, so the maximum is $50$. Check: $12 + 0.75(50) = 49.5 \\\\le 50$, but $12 + 0.75(51) = 50.25 > 50$.\\n\\nChoice C ($51$) rounds $50.66\\\\ldots$ up, but $51$ cakes would require more than $50$ kilograms of flour.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Novvoyxona $\\\\ell$ ta non va $c$ ta tort pishirsa, $0.4\\\\ell + 0.75c \\\\le 50$ va $\\\\ell \\\\ge 30$.\\n\\nIloji boricha ko‘p tort pishirish uchun eng kam ruxsat etilgan miqdorda non pishiramiz: $\\\\ell = 30$, bunga $0.4(30) = 12$ kilogramm un ketadi. U holda $0.75c \\\\le 38$, ya’ni $c \\\\le 50.66\\\\ldots$\\n\\nTortlar soni butun son, shuning uchun eng ko‘pi $50$. Tekshiruv: $12 + 0.75(50) = 49.5 \\\\le 50$, lekin $12 + 0.75(51) = 50.25 > 50$.\\n\\nC variant ($51$) — $50.66\\\\ldots$ ni yuqoriga yaxlitlash natijasi, lekin $51$ ta tort uchun $50$ kilogrammdan ko‘p un kerak bo‘ladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"How many integers $x$ satisfy both $3x - 5 < 2x + 4$ and $-2x \\\\le 3x + 20$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"13\"],\"explanation_en\":\"First inequality: subtract $2x$ and add $5$ to both sides: $x < 9$.\\n\\nSecond inequality: subtract $3x$ from both sides: $-5x \\\\le 20$. Divide by $-5$ and reverse the sign: $x \\\\ge -4$.\\n\\nSo $-4 \\\\le x < 9$. The integers are $-4, -3, -2, \\\\ldots, 8$, and there are $8 - (-4) + 1 = 13$ of them.\\n\\nCommon errors are forgetting to reverse the sign in the second inequality, or counting only $8 - (-4) = 12$ and leaving out one endpoint.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi tengsizlik: ikkala tomondan $2x$ ni ayirib, $5$ ni qo‘shamiz: $x < 9$.\\n\\nIkkinchi tengsizlik: ikkala tomondan $3x$ ni ayiramiz: $-5x \\\\le 20$. $-5$ ga bo‘lamiz va belgini aylantiramiz: $x \\\\ge -4$.\\n\\nDemak $-4 \\\\le x < 9$. Butun sonlar: $-4, -3, -2, \\\\ldots, 8$, ularning soni $8 - (-4) + 1 = 13$ ta.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xatolar: ikkinchi tengsizlikda belgini aylantirishni unutish yoki faqat $8 - (-4) = 12$ ni hisoblab, chetki sonlardan birini tushirib qoldirish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Two lines intersect at a point, forming four angles. One of the angles measures $3x^\\\\circ$, and the angle vertical to it measures $(x + 50)^\\\\circ$. What is the value of $x$?\",\"option_a\":\"25\",\"option_b\":\"32.5\",\"option_c\":\"75\",\"option_d\":\"105\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Vertical angles are congruent, so $3x = x + 50$. Then $2x = 50$ and $x = 25$, which is choice A. Each of these two angles measures $75^\\\\circ$.\\n\\nChoice B comes from treating the angles as supplementary: $3x + (x + 50) = 180$ gives $x = 32.5$. Choice C (75) is the measure of the angle, not the value of $x$. Choice D (105) is the measure of each of the other two angles, $180 - 75$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Vertikal burchaklar o‘zaro teng, shuning uchun $3x = x + 50$. Bundan $2x = 50$ va $x = 25$, ya’ni to‘g‘ri javob A. Bu ikki burchakning har biri $75^\\\\circ$ ga teng.\\n\\nB — burchaklar qo‘shni (yig‘indisi $180^\\\\circ$) deb olingan: $3x + (x + 50) = 180$ dan $x = 32.5$ chiqadi. C (75) — bu $x$ emas, burchakning o‘lchovi. D (105) — qolgan ikki burchakning har biri, $180 - 75$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The measures of the three angles of a triangle are in the ratio $2 : 3 : 7$. What is the measure, in degrees, of the largest angle of the triangle?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"105\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Write the angles as $2k$, $3k$, and $7k$. The angles of a triangle add up to $180^\\\\circ$, so $12k = 180$ and $k = 15$. The largest angle is $7k = 105$ degrees. Check: the angles are $30^\\\\circ$, $45^\\\\circ$, and $105^\\\\circ$, and $30 + 45 + 105 = 180$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Burchaklarni $2k$, $3k$ va $7k$ deb belgilaymiz. Uchburchak burchaklarining yig‘indisi $180^\\\\circ$, demak $12k = 180$ va $k = 15$. Eng katta burchak $7k = 105$ gradus. Tekshiramiz: burchaklar $30^\\\\circ$, $45^\\\\circ$ va $105^\\\\circ$, ularning yig‘indisi $30 + 45 + 105 = 180$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Lines $\\\\ell$ and $m$ are parallel, and line $t$ intersects both of them. Angle 1 is formed where $t$ meets $\\\\ell$, and angle 2 is formed where $t$ meets $m$. Both angles lie between lines $\\\\ell$ and $m$, on the same side of line $t$. If the measure of angle 1 is $118^\\\\circ$, what is the measure of angle 2?\",\"option_a\":\"$28^\\\\circ$\",\"option_b\":\"$62^\\\\circ$\",\"option_c\":\"$118^\\\\circ$\",\"option_d\":\"$242^\\\\circ$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Angles 1 and 2 are same-side interior angles. When parallel lines are cut by a transversal, same-side interior angles are supplementary, so angle 2 measures $180^\\\\circ - 118^\\\\circ = 62^\\\\circ$. Choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoice C ($118^\\\\circ$) would be correct for alternate interior or corresponding angles, which are congruent, but angles 1 and 2 are on the same side of $t$. Choice A ($28^\\\\circ$) subtracts from $90^\\\\circ$ instead of $180^\\\\circ$, and choice D ($242^\\\\circ$) subtracts from $360^\\\\circ$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"1- va 2-burchaklar kesuvchining bir tomonida, parallel to‘g‘ri chiziqlar orasida yotadi — bular bir tomonli ichki burchaklar. Parallel to‘g‘ri chiziqlarni kesuvchi kesib o‘tganda, bir tomonli ichki burchaklarning yig‘indisi $180^\\\\circ$ bo‘ladi. Demak, 2-burchak $180^\\\\circ - 118^\\\\circ = 62^\\\\circ$. To‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nC ($118^\\\\circ$) ichki almashinuvchi yoki mos burchaklar uchun to‘g‘ri bo‘lardi (ular teng), lekin bu burchaklar $t$ ning bir tomonida joylashgan. A ($28^\\\\circ$) — $180^\\\\circ$ o‘rniga $90^\\\\circ$ dan ayirilgan, D ($242^\\\\circ$) esa $360^\\\\circ$ dan ayirilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In triangle $ABC$, the measure of angle $A$ is $40^\\\\circ$. Side $\\\\overline{BC}$ is extended beyond point $C$ to point $D$, and the measure of angle $ACD$ is $115^\\\\circ$. What is the measure of angle $B$?\",\"option_a\":\"$75^\\\\circ$\",\"option_b\":\"$115^\\\\circ$\",\"option_c\":\"$140^\\\\circ$\",\"option_d\":\"$155^\\\\circ$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Angle $ACD$ is an exterior angle of triangle $ABC$, and an exterior angle equals the sum of the two remote interior angles: $m\\\\angle ACD = m\\\\angle A + m\\\\angle B$. So $115 = 40 + m\\\\angle B$, and $m\\\\angle B = 75^\\\\circ$. Check: angle $ACB$ measures $180 - 115 = 65^\\\\circ$, and $40 + 75 + 65 = 180$. Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B ($115^\\\\circ$) assumes angle $B$ equals the exterior angle. Choice C ($140^\\\\circ$) is $180 - 40$, the sum of angles $B$ and $ACB$, not angle $B$ alone. Choice D ($155^\\\\circ$) adds 115 and 40.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$ACD$ burchak $ABC$ uchburchakning tashqi burchagi. Tashqi burchak o‘ziga qo‘shni bo‘lmagan ikki ichki burchak yig‘indisiga teng: $m\\\\angle ACD = m\\\\angle A + m\\\\angle B$. Demak, $115 = 40 + m\\\\angle B$ va $m\\\\angle B = 75^\\\\circ$. Tekshiramiz: $ACB$ burchak $180 - 115 = 65^\\\\circ$, va $40 + 75 + 65 = 180$. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB ($115^\\\\circ$) — $B$ burchak tashqi burchakka teng deb olingan. C ($140^\\\\circ$) — bu $180 - 40$, ya’ni $B$ va $ACB$ burchaklarning yig‘indisi, yolg‘iz $B$ emas. D ($155^\\\\circ$) — 115 va 40 qo‘shib yuborilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"At the same time of day, a person who is 1.8 meters tall casts a shadow 2.4 meters long, and a nearby vertical flagpole casts a shadow 16 meters long. The ground is level. What is the height, in meters, of the flagpole?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"12\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The sun's rays meet the level ground at the same angle for both objects, and both objects are vertical. So the right triangle formed by the person and the person's shadow is similar to the right triangle formed by the flagpole and its shadow. Corresponding sides are proportional: $\\\\frac{h}{16} = \\\\frac{1.8}{2.4}$, so $h = 16 \\\\cdot 0.75 = 12$ meters.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Quyosh nurlari ikkala jism uchun ham tekis yerga bir xil burchak ostida tushadi, ikkala jism ham vertikal. Shuning uchun odam va uning soyasi hosil qilgan to‘g‘ri burchakli uchburchak bayroq ustuni va uning soyasi hosil qilgan uchburchakka o‘xshash. Mos tomonlar proporsional: $\\\\frac{h}{16} = \\\\frac{1.8}{2.4}$, demak $h = 16 \\\\cdot 0.75 = 12$ metr.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Triangle $DEF$ is similar to triangle $JKL$, where vertices $D$, $E$, and $F$ correspond to vertices $J$, $K$, and $L$, respectively. In triangle $DEF$, $DE = 8$, $EF = 12$, and $DF = 10$. If $JK = 20$, what is the perimeter of triangle $JKL$?\",\"option_a\":\"30\",\"option_b\":\"50\",\"option_c\":\"66\",\"option_d\":\"75\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Side $DE$ corresponds to side $JK$, so the scale factor from triangle $DEF$ to triangle $JKL$ is $\\\\frac{20}{8} = 2.5$. The perimeters of similar triangles have the same ratio as their corresponding sides. The perimeter of $DEF$ is $8 + 12 + 10 = 30$, so the perimeter of $JKL$ is $2.5 \\\\cdot 30 = 75$. Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A (30) is the perimeter of $DEF$. Choice B (50) matches $JK$ with $EF$ instead of $DE$, giving a factor of $\\\\frac{20}{12}$. Choice C (66) adds $20 - 8 = 12$ to every side instead of multiplying by the scale factor.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$DE$ tomon $JK$ tomonga mos keladi, shuning uchun $DEF$ dan $JKL$ ga o‘tish koeffitsiyenti $\\\\frac{20}{8} = 2.5$. O‘xshash uchburchaklarning perimetrlari ham mos tomonlar kabi shu nisbatda bo‘ladi. $DEF$ ning perimetri $8 + 12 + 10 = 30$, demak $JKL$ ning perimetri $2.5 \\\\cdot 30 = 75$. To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA (30) — bu $DEF$ ning perimetri. B (50) — $JK$ tomon $DE$ ga emas, $EF$ ga moslangan, koeffitsiyent $\\\\frac{20}{12}$ bo‘lib qolgan. C (66) — har bir tomonga ko‘paytirish o‘rniga $20 - 8 = 12$ qo‘shilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In triangle $ABC$, $AB = AC$. Point $D$ lies on $\\\\overline{AB}$ and point $E$ lies on $\\\\overline{AC}$ so that $\\\\overline{DE}$ is parallel to $\\\\overline{BC}$. The measure of angle $A$ is $(x + 20)^\\\\circ$, and the measure of angle $ADE$ is $(2x + 10)^\\\\circ$. What is the measure of angle $DEC$?\",\"option_a\":\"$28^\\\\circ$\",\"option_b\":\"$48^\\\\circ$\",\"option_c\":\"$66^\\\\circ$\",\"option_d\":\"$114^\\\\circ$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Because $\\\\overline{DE} \\\\parallel \\\\overline{BC}$, angles $ADE$ and $ABC$ are corresponding angles, so $m\\\\angle B = (2x + 10)^\\\\circ$. Since $AB = AC$, angle $C$ has the same measure as angle $B$. The angles of triangle $ABC$ add up to $180^\\\\circ$: $(x + 20) + 2(2x + 10) = 180$, so $5x + 40 = 180$ and $x = 28$. Then $m\\\\angle AED = m\\\\angle ACB = 2(28) + 10 = 66^\\\\circ$. Angles $AED$ and $DEC$ form a linear pair along $\\\\overline{AC}$, so $m\\\\angle DEC = 180 - 66 = 114^\\\\circ$. Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A (28) is the value of $x$, not an angle measure. Choice B ($48^\\\\circ$) is angle $A$. Choice C ($66^\\\\circ$) is angle $AED$, the angle on the other side of point $E$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$\\\\overline{DE} \\\\parallel \\\\overline{BC}$ bo‘lgani uchun $ADE$ va $ABC$ mos burchaklar, demak $m\\\\angle B = (2x + 10)^\\\\circ$. $AB = AC$ bo‘lgani uchun $C$ burchak $B$ burchakka teng. $ABC$ uchburchak burchaklarining yig‘indisi $180^\\\\circ$: $(x + 20) + 2(2x + 10) = 180$, bundan $5x + 40 = 180$ va $x = 28$. U holda $m\\\\angle AED = m\\\\angle ACB = 2(28) + 10 = 66^\\\\circ$. $AED$ va $DEC$ burchaklar $\\\\overline{AC}$ bo‘ylab qo‘shni burchaklar, shuning uchun $m\\\\angle DEC = 180 - 66 = 114^\\\\circ$. To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA (28) — bu $x$ ning qiymati, burchak emas. B ($48^\\\\circ$) — $A$ burchak. C ($66^\\\\circ$) — $AED$ burchak, ya’ni $E$ nuqtaning boshqa tomonidagi burchak.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"Segments $\\\\overline{AE}$ and $\\\\overline{BD}$ intersect at point $C$, and $\\\\overline{AB}$ is parallel to $\\\\overline{DE}$. If $AC = x$, $CE = 8$, $BC = 3$, and $CD = x - 2$, what is the length of $\\\\overline{AE}$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"14\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Because $\\\\overline{AB} \\\\parallel \\\\overline{DE}$, alternate interior angles are congruent ($\\\\angle BAC \\\\cong \\\\angle DEC$ and $\\\\angle ABC \\\\cong \\\\angle EDC$), so triangle $ABC$ is similar to triangle $EDC$. Corresponding sides are proportional: $\\\\frac{AC}{EC} = \\\\frac{BC}{DC}$, so $\\\\frac{x}{8} = \\\\frac{3}{x - 2}$. Cross-multiplying gives $x^2 - 2x = 24$, or $(x - 6)(x + 4) = 0$. A length must be positive, so $x = 6$ (then $CD = 4$). Therefore $AE = AC + CE = 6 + 8 = 14$.\\n\\nA common slip is to stop at $x = 6$, which is only the length of $\\\\overline{AC}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$\\\\overline{AB} \\\\parallel \\\\overline{DE}$ bo‘lgani uchun ichki almashinuvchi burchaklar teng ($\\\\angle BAC \\\\cong \\\\angle DEC$ va $\\\\angle ABC \\\\cong \\\\angle EDC$), demak $ABC$ uchburchak $EDC$ uchburchakka o‘xshash. Mos tomonlar proporsional: $\\\\frac{AC}{EC} = \\\\frac{BC}{DC}$, ya’ni $\\\\frac{x}{8} = \\\\frac{3}{x - 2}$. Ko‘paytirsak, $x^2 - 2x = 24$, yoki $(x - 6)(x + 4) = 0$. Uzunlik musbat bo‘lishi kerak, shuning uchun $x = 6$ (u holda $CD = 4$). Demak $AE = AC + CE = 6 + 8 = 14$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $x = 6$ da to‘xtab qolish; bu faqat $\\\\overline{AC}$ ning uzunligi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":135,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What are the solutions to the equation $x^2 - 2x - 24 = 0$?\",\"option_a\":\"$x = -4$ and $x = 6$\",\"option_b\":\"$x = -6$ and $x = 4$\",\"option_c\":\"$x = -8$ and $x = 3$\",\"option_d\":\"$x = -2$ and $x = 12$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Look for two numbers whose product is $-24$ and whose sum is $-2$: they are $-6$ and $4$. So $x^2 - 2x - 24 = (x - 6)(x + 4) = 0$.\\n\\nThen $x - 6 = 0$ or $x + 4 = 0$, so $x = 6$ or $x = -4$. Check: $36 - 12 - 24 = 0$ and $16 + 8 - 24 = 0$.\\n\\nChoice B uses the numbers $-6$ and $4$ from the factoring step as the solutions, but $(x - 6)(x + 4) = 0$ means $x = 6$ or $x = -4$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ko‘paytmasi $-24$, yig‘indisi $-2$ bo‘lgan ikki sonni topamiz: $-6$ va $4$. Demak $x^2 - 2x - 24 = (x - 6)(x + 4) = 0$.\\n\\nU holda $x - 6 = 0$ yoki $x + 4 = 0$, ya’ni $x = 6$ yoki $x = -4$. Tekshiruv: $36 - 12 - 24 = 0$ va $16 + 8 - 24 = 0$.\\n\\nB variant ko‘paytuvchilarga ajratishdagi $-6$ va $4$ sonlarini yechim deb oladi, lekin $(x - 6)(x + 4) = 0$ dan $x = 6$ yoki $x = -4$ kelib chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$(x - 3)^2 = 49$$\\n\\nWhat is the negative solution to the given equation?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"-4\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Take the square root of both sides, remembering both signs: $x - 3 = 7$ or $x - 3 = -7$.\\n\\nSo $x = 10$ or $x = -4$. The negative solution is $-4$.\\n\\nCommon errors are taking only the positive square root, which loses $x = -4$, or entering $-7$, which is the value of $x - 3$, not of $x$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomondan kvadrat ildiz olamiz, ikkala ishorani ham hisobga olib: $x - 3 = 7$ yoki $x - 3 = -7$.\\n\\nDemak $x = 10$ yoki $x = -4$. Manfiy yechim — $-4$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xatolar: faqat musbat ildizni olib, $x = -4$ ni yo‘qotish yoki $x$ ning emas, $x - 3$ ning qiymati $-7$ ni kiritish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What is the solution to the equation $\\\\sqrt{3x - 2} = 5$?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{7}{3}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{23}{3}$\",\"option_c\":\"$9$\",\"option_d\":\"$27$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Square both sides: $3x - 2 = 25$. Add $2$: $3x = 27$. Divide by $3$: $x = 9$.\\n\\nCheck: $\\\\sqrt{3(9) - 2} = \\\\sqrt{25} = 5$.\\n\\nChoice A skips the squaring step and solves $3x - 2 = 5$ instead of $3x - 2 = 25$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomonni kvadratga ko‘taramiz: $3x - 2 = 25$. $2$ ni qo‘shamiz: $3x = 27$. $3$ ga bo‘lamiz: $x = 9$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $\\\\sqrt{3(9) - 2} = \\\\sqrt{25} = 5$.\\n\\nA variant kvadratga ko‘tarish bosqichini tashlab ketadi va $3x - 2 = 25$ o‘rniga $3x - 2 = 5$ ni yechadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} y &= x^2 - 3x - 4 \\\\\\\\ y &= x - 4 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nWhich of the following points $(x, y)$ is a solution to the given system of equations?\",\"option_a\":\"$(-1, 0)$\",\"option_b\":\"$(0, 4)$\",\"option_c\":\"$(1, -3)$\",\"option_d\":\"$(4, 0)$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Set the two expressions for $y$ equal: $x^2 - 3x - 4 = x - 4$, so $x^2 - 4x = 0$ and $x(x - 4) = 0$. Thus $x = 0$ or $x = 4$.\\n\\nUsing $y = x - 4$, the solutions are $(0, -4)$ and $(4, 0)$. Only $(4, 0)$ is among the choices.\\n\\nChoice A, $(-1, 0)$, lies on the parabola (it is one of its $x$-intercepts) but not on the line, since $-1 - 4 = -5$, not $0$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y$ uchun ikkala ifodani tenglashtiramiz: $x^2 - 3x - 4 = x - 4$, ya’ni $x^2 - 4x = 0$ va $x(x - 4) = 0$. Demak $x = 0$ yoki $x = 4$.\\n\\n$y = x - 4$ dan yechimlar: $(0, -4)$ va $(4, 0)$. Variantlar orasida faqat $(4, 0)$ bor.\\n\\nA variant $(-1, 0)$ parabolada yotadi (u parabolaning $x$ o‘qi bilan kesishish nuqtalaridan biri), lekin to‘g‘ri chiziqda yotmaydi: $-1 - 4 = -5$, $0$ emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What is the sum of the solutions to the equation $2x^2 - 7x - 15 = 0$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-\\\\frac{15}{2}$\",\"option_b\":\"$-\\\\frac{7}{2}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{7}{2}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{13}{2}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Factor: $2x^2 - 7x - 15 = (2x + 3)(x - 5)$, so the solutions are $x = -\\\\frac{3}{2}$ and $x = 5$. Their sum is $5 - \\\\frac{3}{2} = \\\\frac{7}{2}$.\\n\\nShortcut: for $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$, the sum of the solutions is $-\\\\frac{b}{a} = -\\\\frac{-7}{2} = \\\\frac{7}{2}$.\\n\\nChoice B uses $\\\\frac{b}{a}$ without the negative sign, and choice A is the product of the solutions, $\\\\frac{c}{a}$, not their sum.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ko‘paytuvchilarga ajratamiz: $2x^2 - 7x - 15 = (2x + 3)(x - 5)$, demak yechimlar $x = -\\\\frac{3}{2}$ va $x = 5$. Ularning yig‘indisi $5 - \\\\frac{3}{2} = \\\\frac{7}{2}$.\\n\\nQisqa yo‘l: $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$ tenglama yechimlarining yig‘indisi $-\\\\frac{b}{a} = -\\\\frac{-7}{2} = \\\\frac{7}{2}$.\\n\\nB variant manfiy ishorasiz $\\\\frac{b}{a}$ ni oladi, A variant esa yechimlar yig‘indisi emas, ko‘paytmasi $\\\\frac{c}{a}$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What are all the solutions to the equation $\\\\dfrac{x}{x - 3} + \\\\dfrac{2}{x} = \\\\dfrac{3}{x - 3}$?\",\"option_a\":\"$x = -3$ and $x = 2$\",\"option_b\":\"$x = -2$ only\",\"option_c\":\"$x = -2$ and $x = 3$\",\"option_d\":\"There is no solution.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The denominators show that $x \\\\ne 0$ and $x \\\\ne 3$. Multiply both sides by $x(x - 3)$: $x^2 + 2(x - 3) = 3x$.\\n\\nSimplify: $x^2 + 2x - 6 - 3x = 0$, so $x^2 - x - 6 = 0$ and $(x - 3)(x + 2) = 0$. This gives $x = 3$ or $x = -2$.\\n\\nThe value $x = 3$ makes the denominators $x - 3$ equal to $0$, so it is an extraneous solution and must be rejected. The only solution is $x = -2$. Check: $\\\\frac{-2}{-5} + \\\\frac{2}{-2} = 0.4 - 1 = -0.6$ and $\\\\frac{3}{-5} = -0.6$.\\n\\nChoice C keeps $x = 3$, but at $x = 3$ the original equation is undefined.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maxrajlardan $x \\\\ne 0$ va $x \\\\ne 3$ ekanini ko‘ramiz. Ikkala tomonni $x(x - 3)$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $x^2 + 2(x - 3) = 3x$.\\n\\nSoddalashtiramiz: $x^2 + 2x - 6 - 3x = 0$, ya’ni $x^2 - x - 6 = 0$ va $(x - 3)(x + 2) = 0$. Bundan $x = 3$ yoki $x = -2$.\\n\\n$x = 3$ da $x - 3$ maxraj $0$ ga aylanadi, shuning uchun bu begona (soxta) yechim va u tashlab yuboriladi. Yagona yechim $x = -2$. Tekshiruv: $\\\\frac{-2}{-5} + \\\\frac{2}{-2} = 0.4 - 1 = -0.6$ va $\\\\frac{3}{-5} = -0.6$.\\n\\nC variant $x = 3$ ni ham qoldiradi, lekin $x = 3$ da dastlabki tenglama ma’noga ega emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} y &= x^2 + 6x + c \\\\\\\\ y &= 2x - 1 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nIn the given system of equations, $c$ is a constant. The graphs of the equations in the $xy$-plane intersect at exactly one point. What is the value of $c$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-5$\",\"option_b\":\"$3$\",\"option_c\":\"$4$\",\"option_d\":\"$15$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Set the expressions for $y$ equal: $x^2 + 6x + c = 2x - 1$, which becomes $x^2 + 4x + (c + 1) = 0$.\\n\\nThe graphs meet at exactly one point when this quadratic has exactly one real solution, that is, when its discriminant is $0$: $4^2 - 4(1)(c + 1) = 0$. So $16 = 4c + 4$ and $c = 3$.\\n\\nCheck: with $c = 3$ the equation is $x^2 + 4x + 4 = (x + 2)^2 = 0$, giving the single point $(-2, -5)$.\\n\\nChoice C ($4$) forgets to move the $-1$ to the left side and uses $x^2 + 4x + c = 0$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y$ uchun ifodalarni tenglashtiramiz: $x^2 + 6x + c = 2x - 1$, bu $x^2 + 4x + (c + 1) = 0$ ko‘rinishga keladi.\\n\\nGrafiklar aynan bitta nuqtada kesishishi uchun bu kvadrat tenglama aynan bitta haqiqiy yechimga ega bo‘lishi, ya’ni diskriminanti $0$ ga teng bo‘lishi kerak: $4^2 - 4(1)(c + 1) = 0$. Demak $16 = 4c + 4$ va $c = 3$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $c = 3$ da tenglama $x^2 + 4x + 4 = (x + 2)^2 = 0$ bo‘ladi va yagona nuqta $(-2, -5)$ hosil bo‘ladi.\\n\\nC variant ($4$) — $-1$ ni chap tomonga o‘tkazishni unutib, $x^2 + 4x + c = 0$ dan foydalanish natijasi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":125,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$x^4 - 13x^2 + 36 = 0$$\\n\\nWhat is the sum of all the positive solutions to the given equation?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The equation is quadratic in $x^2$. Let $u = x^2$: $u^2 - 13u + 36 = 0$, so $(u - 4)(u - 9) = 0$ and $u = 4$ or $u = 9$.\\n\\nThen $x^2 = 4$ gives $x = 2$ or $x = -2$, and $x^2 = 9$ gives $x = 3$ or $x = -3$.\\n\\nThe positive solutions are $2$ and $3$, so their sum is $5$.\\n\\nA common error is stopping at $u = 4$ and $u = 9$ and entering $13$, which is the sum of the values of $x^2$, not of $x$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tenglama $x^2$ ga nisbatan kvadrat tenglama. $u = x^2$ deb belgilaymiz: $u^2 - 13u + 36 = 0$, ya’ni $(u - 4)(u - 9) = 0$, bundan $u = 4$ yoki $u = 9$.\\n\\nU holda $x^2 = 4$ dan $x = 2$ yoki $x = -2$, $x^2 = 9$ dan esa $x = 3$ yoki $x = -3$.\\n\\nMusbat yechimlar $2$ va $3$, ularning yig‘indisi $5$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $u = 4$ va $u = 9$ da to‘xtab, $13$ ni kiritish: bu $x$ larning emas, $x^2$ qiymatlarining yig‘indisi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":115,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = 2x^2 - 3x + 1$. What is the value of $f(-2)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-1$\",\"option_b\":\"$3$\",\"option_c\":\"$15$\",\"option_d\":\"$23$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $-2$ for $x$, keeping it in parentheses: $f(-2) = 2(-2)^2 - 3(-2) + 1 = 2(4) + 6 + 1 = 15$.\\n\\nChoice A comes from evaluating $-2^2$ as $-4$ instead of $(-2)^2 = 4$, which gives $-8 + 6 + 1 = -1$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x$ o‘rniga $-2$ ni qavs ichida qo‘yamiz: $f(-2) = 2(-2)^2 - 3(-2) + 1 = 2(4) + 6 + 1 = 15$.\\n\\nA variant — $(-2)^2 = 4$ o‘rniga $-2^2 = -4$ deb hisoblash natijasi: $-8 + 6 + 1 = -1$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $P(t) = 84{,}000(1.03)^t$ models the population of a city $t$ years after 2020. What is the best interpretation of $1.03$ in this context?\",\"option_a\":\"The population increases by 3% each year.\",\"option_b\":\"The population increases by 103% each year.\",\"option_c\":\"The population increases by 1.03% each year.\",\"option_d\":\"The population increases by 2,520 people each year.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"In an exponential model of the form $a(1 + r)^t$, the base $1 + r$ is the growth factor and $r$ is the growth rate per time period.\\n\\nHere $1.03 = 1 + 0.03$, so each year the population is multiplied by $1.03$; that is, it increases by 3% of the previous year's population.\\n\\nChoice D describes a constant increase of $0.03 \\\\cdot 84{,}000 = 2{,}520$ people per year, which would be linear growth; in this model, the yearly increase gets larger as the population grows.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$a(1 + r)^t$ ko‘rinishidagi ko‘rsatkichli modelda asos $1 + r$ — o‘sish ko‘paytuvchisi, $r$ esa har bir davrdagi o‘sish sur’ati.\\n\\nBu yerda $1.03 = 1 + 0.03$, ya’ni har yili aholi soni $1.03$ ga ko‘paytiriladi: u har yili oldingi yilga nisbatan 3 foizga oshadi.\\n\\nD variant har yili bir xil $0.03 \\\\cdot 84{,}000 = 2{,}520$ kishiga oshishni tasvirlaydi — bu chiziqli o‘sish bo‘lardi; bu modelda esa aholi ko‘paygani sari yillik o‘sish ham kattalashadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $h$ is defined by $h(x) = 5(2)^x - 7$. What is the value of $h(3)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$23$\",\"option_b\":\"$33$\",\"option_c\":\"$38$\",\"option_d\":\"$993$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Evaluate the power first: $h(3) = 5(2)^3 - 7 = 5(8) - 7 = 40 - 7 = 33$.\\n\\nChoice D multiplies before applying the exponent, $(5 \\\\cdot 2)^3 - 7 = 1{,}000 - 7$, but the exponent applies only to the base $2$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Avval darajani hisoblaymiz: $h(3) = 5(2)^3 - 7 = 5(8) - 7 = 40 - 7 = 33$.\\n\\nD variantda darajaga ko‘tarishdan oldin ko‘paytirilgan: $(5 \\\\cdot 2)^3 - 7 = 1{,}000 - 7$. Lekin daraja faqat $2$ asosiga tegishli.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = (x - 3)(x + 7)$. For what value of $x$ does $f(x)$ reach its minimum value?\",\"option_a\":\"$-25$\",\"option_b\":\"$-2$\",\"option_c\":\"$2$\",\"option_d\":\"$5$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The zeros of $f$ are $x = 3$ and $x = -7$. Expanding gives $x^2 + 4x - 21$, so the graph is a parabola that opens upward and has a minimum at its vertex.\\n\\nThe vertex lies midway between the zeros: $x = \\\\frac{3 + (-7)}{2} = -2$. (The minimum value itself is $f(-2) = (-5)(5) = -25$.)\\n\\nChoice A ($-25$) is the minimum value of $f(x)$, not the value of $x$ at which the minimum occurs.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$f$ ning nollari: $x = 3$ va $x = -7$. Qavslarni ochsak, $x^2 + 4x - 21$; demak grafik — yuqoriga ochilgan parabola va uning uchida minimum bor.\\n\\nParabola uchi nollarning o‘rtasida joylashgan: $x = \\\\frac{3 + (-7)}{2} = -2$. (Minimal qiymatning o‘zi $f(-2) = (-5)(5) = -25$.)\\n\\nA variant ($-25$) — bu $f(x)$ ning minimal qiymati, savol esa minimum qaysi $x$ da erishilishini so‘rayapti.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The amount of a medication, in milligrams, remaining in a patient's bloodstream $t$ hours after a $400$-milligram dose is modeled by the function $A(t) = 400(0.85)^t$. According to the model, which of the following is closest to the amount of the medication, in milligrams, remaining in the bloodstream $3$ hours after the dose?\",\"option_a\":\"$154$\",\"option_b\":\"$220$\",\"option_c\":\"$246$\",\"option_d\":\"$340$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Evaluate the function at $t = 3$: $A(3) = 400(0.85)^3 = 400(0.614125) = 245.65$, which is closest to $246$ milligrams.\\n\\nChoice B assumes the amount drops by the same $60$ milligrams ($15\\\\%$ of $400$) every hour, but in an exponential model each hour removes $15\\\\%$ of the amount remaining at that time.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Funksiyani $t = 3$ da hisoblaymiz: $A(3) = 400(0.85)^3 = 400(0.614125) = 245.65$, bu $246$ milligrammga eng yaqin.\\n\\nB variant har soatda miqdor bir xil $60$ milligrammga ($400$ ning 15 foizi) kamayadi deb hisoblaydi. Lekin ko‘rsatkichli modelda har soatda o‘sha paytda qolgan miqdorning 15 foizi kamayadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = x^2 - 6x + c$, where $c$ is a constant. In the $xy$-plane, the vertex of the graph of $y = f(x)$ is $(3, -5)$. What is the value of $c$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"4\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The vertex is a point on the graph, so $f(3) = -5$: $3^2 - 6(3) + c = -5$, which gives $9 - 18 + c = -5$ and $c = 4$.\\n\\nAlternatively, in vertex form, $f(x) = (x - 3)^2 - 5 = x^2 - 6x + 9 - 5 = x^2 - 6x + 4$.\\n\\nA common error is entering $-5$, the $y$-coordinate of the vertex; $c$ is the $y$-intercept $f(0)$, not the height of the vertex.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Parabola uchi grafikda yotadi, demak $f(3) = -5$: $3^2 - 6(3) + c = -5$, ya’ni $9 - 18 + c = -5$ va $c = 4$.\\n\\nBoshqa usul — uch shakli: $f(x) = (x - 3)^2 - 5 = x^2 - 6x + 9 - 5 = x^2 - 6x + 4$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — uchning $y$ koordinatasi $-5$ ni kiritish; $c$ esa uchning balandligi emas, $f(0)$, ya’ni $y$ o‘qini kesish nuqtasi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The value $V$, in dollars, of an investment $t$ years after it was made is modeled by $V(t) = 2{,}500(1.21)^t$. Which of the following functions models the value $V$, in dollars, of the investment $m$ half-years after it was made?\",\"option_a\":\"$V = 2{,}500(1.105)^m$\",\"option_b\":\"$V = 2{,}500(1.21)^{2m}$\",\"option_c\":\"$V = 2{,}500(1.4641)^m$\",\"option_d\":\"$V = 2{,}500(1.1)^m$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Since $m$ half-years equal $t = \\\\frac{m}{2}$ years, substitute: $V = 2{,}500(1.21)^{m/2} = 2{,}500\\\\left((1.21)^{1/2}\\\\right)^m = 2{,}500(1.1)^m$, because $\\\\sqrt{1.21} = 1.1$.\\n\\nCheck: after $m = 2$ half-years (1 year), $2{,}500(1.1)^2 = 2{,}500(1.21)$, which matches $V(1)$.\\n\\nChoice A halves the growth rate (21% becomes 10.5%), but growing by 10.5% twice gives a factor of $1.105^2 \\\\approx 1.221$, not $1.21$; choice B substitutes $t = 2m$ instead of $t = \\\\frac{m}{2}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$m$ ta yarim yil $t = \\\\frac{m}{2}$ yilga teng, shuning uchun o‘rniga qo‘yamiz: $V = 2{,}500(1.21)^{m/2} = 2{,}500\\\\left((1.21)^{1/2}\\\\right)^m = 2{,}500(1.1)^m$, chunki $\\\\sqrt{1.21} = 1.1$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $m = 2$ yarim yildan (1 yildan) keyin $2{,}500(1.1)^2 = 2{,}500(1.21)$, bu $V(1)$ ga mos keladi.\\n\\nA variant o‘sish sur’atini ikkiga bo‘ladi (21% o‘rniga 10.5%), lekin ikki marta 10.5% ga o‘sish $1.105^2 \\\\approx 1.221$ ko‘paytuvchini beradi, $1.21$ ni emas; B variantda esa $t = \\\\frac{m}{2}$ o‘rniga $t = 2m$ qo‘yilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":125,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c$, where $a$, $b$, and $c$ are constants. In the $xy$-plane, the graph of $y = f(x)$ is symmetric about the line $x = 3$ and passes through the points $(1, 0)$ and $(0, -10)$. What is the value of $f(4)$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"6\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The graph is symmetric about $x = 3$, and $(1, 0)$ is $2$ units to the left of that line, so $(5, 0)$ is also on the graph. The zeros are $1$ and $5$, so $f(x) = a(x - 1)(x - 5)$.\\n\\nUse $(0, -10)$: $a(0 - 1)(0 - 5) = 5a = -10$, so $a = -2$.\\n\\nThen $f(4) = -2(4 - 1)(4 - 5) = -2(3)(-1) = 6$. (By symmetry, $f(4) = f(2)$, and indeed $f(2) = -2(1)(-3) = 6$.)\\n\\nDropping the negative sign when solving $5a = -10$ gives $a = 2$ and the wrong answer $-6$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Grafik $x = 3$ chiziqqa nisbatan simmetrik, $(1, 0)$ nuqta esa bu chiziqdan $2$ birlik chapda, demak $(5, 0)$ ham grafikda yotadi. Nollar $1$ va $5$, shuning uchun $f(x) = a(x - 1)(x - 5)$.\\n\\n$(0, -10)$ nuqtadan foydalanamiz: $a(0 - 1)(0 - 5) = 5a = -10$, demak $a = -2$.\\n\\nU holda $f(4) = -2(4 - 1)(4 - 5) = -2(3)(-1) = 6$. (Simmetriya bo‘yicha $f(4) = f(2)$, va haqiqatan $f(2) = -2(1)(-3) = 6$.)\\n\\n$5a = -10$ ni yechishda manfiy ishorani yo‘qotsangiz, $a = 2$ va noto‘g‘ri javob $-6$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The list shows the number of minutes each of 6 students spent on homework last night.\\n\\n35, 42, 28, 50, 40, 45\\n\\nWhat is the mean number of minutes these students spent on homework?\",\"option_a\":\"$22$\",\"option_b\":\"$40$\",\"option_c\":\"$41$\",\"option_d\":\"$48$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The mean is the sum of the values divided by the number of values: $35 + 42 + 28 + 50 + 40 + 45 = 240$, and $240 \\\\div 6 = 40$ minutes. Choice C, 41, is the median (the average of the two middle values, 40 and 42, after the list is ordered). Choice D divides the sum by 5 instead of 6, and choice A is the range, $50 - 28 = 22$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"O‘rta qiymat (mean) — qiymatlar yig‘indisi ularning soniga bo‘linadi: $35 + 42 + 28 + 50 + 40 + 45 = 240$, $240 \\\\div 6 = 40$ daqiqa. C javob (41) — mediana (ro‘yxat tartiblangandan keyin o‘rtadagi 40 va 42 ning o‘rtachasi). D javob yig‘indini 6 emas, 5 ga bo‘lgan, A javob esa qiymatlar oralig‘i (range): $50 - 28 = 22$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"What is the mean number of goals the team scored per match in these 20 matches?\",\"passage\":\"A football team played 20 matches in a season. The table shows how many matches the team played with each number of goals scored.\\n\\n| Goals scored | Number of matches |\\n| ---: | ---: |\\n| 0 | 1 |\\n| 1 | 3 |\\n| 2 | 5 |\\n| 3 | 7 |\\n| 4 | 4 |\",\"spr_answers\":[\"2.5\",\"5/2\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Multiply each number of goals by the number of matches with that score, then add: $0(1) + 1(3) + 2(5) + 3(7) + 4(4) = 0 + 3 + 10 + 21 + 16 = 50$ goals. Divide by the 20 matches: $50 \\\\div 20 = 2.5$. A common error is to average only the listed goal values, $\\\\frac{0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4}{5} = 2$, which ignores how many matches had each score. Enter 2.5 or 5/2.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir gollar sonini shuncha gol urilgan o‘yinlar soniga ko‘paytirib, natijalarni qo‘shamiz: $0(1) + 1(3) + 2(5) + 3(7) + 4(4) = 0 + 3 + 10 + 21 + 16 = 50$ gol. Uni 20 o‘yinga bo‘lamiz: $50 \\\\div 20 = 2.5$. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — faqat jadvaldagi gol qiymatlarini o‘rtachalash: $\\\\frac{0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4}{5} = 2$; bunda har bir natija nechta o‘yinda qayd etilgani hisobga olinmaydi. Javob maydoniga 2.5 yoki 5/2 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The heights, in centimeters, of 5 seedlings in a greenhouse are 12, 15, 15, 18, and 40. Which of the following statements about the mean and the median of these heights is true?\",\"option_a\":\"The mean and the median are equal.\",\"option_b\":\"The median is 5 centimeters greater than the mean.\",\"option_c\":\"The mean is 10 centimeters greater than the median.\",\"option_d\":\"The mean is 5 centimeters greater than the median.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The values are already in order, so the median is the middle (3rd) value, 15. The mean is $\\\\frac{12 + 15 + 15 + 18 + 40}{5} = \\\\frac{100}{5} = 20$. So the mean is $20 - 15 = 5$ centimeters greater than the median: the unusually large value 40 pulls the mean up but does not affect the median. Choice B reverses the relationship, and choice C divides the sum by 4 instead of 5.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qiymatlar allaqachon tartiblangan, shuning uchun mediana — o‘rtadagi (3-) qiymat, ya’ni 15. O‘rta qiymat: $\\\\frac{12 + 15 + 15 + 18 + 40}{5} = \\\\frac{100}{5} = 20$. Demak o‘rta qiymat medianadan $20 - 15 = 5$ santimetr katta: chetga chiqqan katta qiymat (40) o‘rta qiymatni yuqoriga tortadi, medianaga esa ta’sir qilmaydi. B javob munosabatni teskari olgan, C javob esa yig‘indini 5 emas, 4 ga bo‘lgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A teacher gave a test to 28 students. After grading the test, the teacher added 5 points to every student's score. Which of the following correctly describes how adding the 5 points changed the mean and the standard deviation of the scores?\",\"option_a\":\"The mean increased by 5, and the standard deviation did not change.\",\"option_b\":\"The mean increased by 5, and the standard deviation increased by 5.\",\"option_c\":\"The mean did not change, and the standard deviation increased by 5.\",\"option_d\":\"Neither the mean nor the standard deviation changed.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Adding 5 to every score adds $28 \\\\times 5 = 140$ points to the total, so the mean increases by $140 \\\\div 28 = 5$. The standard deviation measures how spread out the scores are around the mean. Every score and the mean move up together by 5, so each score's distance from the mean stays the same, and the standard deviation does not change. Choice B is the most tempting, but shifting all values by the same amount does not change their spread (the range, for example, also stays the same).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir ballga 5 qo‘shilsa, umumiy yig‘indi $28 \\\\times 5 = 140$ ballga oshadi, o‘rta qiymat esa $140 \\\\div 28 = 5$ ga oshadi. Standart chetlanish ballarning o‘rta qiymat atrofida qanchalik tarqoqligini o‘lchaydi. Barcha ballar ham, o‘rta qiymat ham birgalikda 5 ga siljiydi, shuning uchun har bir ballning o‘rta qiymatdan uzoqligi o‘zgarmaydi — standart chetlanish ham o‘zgarmaydi. Eng jozibali xato — B javob: barcha qiymatlarni bir xil songa siljitish ularning tarqoqligini o‘zgartirmaydi (masalan, range ham o‘zgarmay qoladi).\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In one class, 20 students took a quiz, and their mean score was 78. In a second class, 30 students took the same quiz, and their mean score was 83. What is the mean quiz score of all 50 students?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"81\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Find each class's total: $20 \\\\times 78 = 1{,}560$ and $30 \\\\times 83 = 2{,}490$. The combined total is $4{,}050$, so the combined mean is $4{,}050 \\\\div 50 = 81$. Averaging the two means, $\\\\frac{78 + 83}{2} = 80.5$, is wrong because the classes have different sizes; the larger class pulls the combined mean closer to 83.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir sinfning umumiy ballini topamiz: $20 \\\\times 78 = 1{,}560$ va $30 \\\\times 83 = 2{,}490$. Jami $4{,}050$, demak umumiy o‘rta qiymat $4{,}050 \\\\div 50 = 81$. Ikki o‘rta qiymatni o‘rtachalash ($\\\\frac{78 + 83}{2} = 80.5$) xato, chunki sinflardagi o‘quvchilar soni har xil: kattaroq sinf umumiy o‘rta qiymatni 83 ga yaqinroq tortadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which interval contains the median commute time of these 40 employees?\",\"passage\":\"The table summarizes the commute times, in minutes, of 40 employees at a company.\\n\\n| Commute time (minutes) | Number of employees |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| 0 to 9 | 4 |\\n| 10 to 19 | 13 |\\n| 20 to 29 | 8 |\\n| 30 to 39 | 7 |\\n| 40 to 49 | 5 |\\n| 50 to 59 | 3 |\",\"option_a\":\"0 to 9 minutes\",\"option_b\":\"10 to 19 minutes\",\"option_c\":\"20 to 29 minutes\",\"option_d\":\"30 to 39 minutes\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"With 40 values, the median is the average of the 20th and 21st values when the times are listed in order. Count through the intervals: the first holds values 1 through 4, the second holds values 5 through 17, and the third holds values 18 through 25. Both the 20th and 21st values are in the 20 to 29 minute interval, so the median is in that interval. Choice B is the interval with the most employees (the mode), but the median depends on where the middle values fall, not on which interval is largest.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"40 ta qiymat bo‘lgani uchun mediana — vaqtlar tartib bilan yozilganda 20- va 21-qiymatlarning o‘rtachasi. Oraliqlar bo‘yicha sanab chiqamiz: birinchisida 1–4-qiymatlar, ikkinchisida 5–17-qiymatlar, uchinchisida 18–25-qiymatlar. 20- va 21-qiymatlar ikkalasi ham 20–29 daqiqa oralig‘ida, demak mediana shu oraliqda. B javob — eng ko‘p xodim tushgan oraliq (moda), lekin mediana eng katta guruhga emas, o‘rtadagi qiymatlar qayerga tushishiga bog‘liq.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A data set consists of 9 values. The mean of the data set is 52, and the median is 50. The greatest value in the data set was recorded as 95, but the correct value is 59. When this error is corrected, what are the mean and the median of the data set?\",\"option_a\":\"Mean: 48; median: 50\",\"option_b\":\"Mean: 48; median: 46\",\"option_c\":\"Mean: 16; median: 50\",\"option_d\":\"Mean: 52; median: 50\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The original sum is $9 \\\\times 52 = 468$. Replacing 95 with 59 lowers the sum by $95 - 59 = 36$, so the new sum is 432 and the new mean is $432 \\\\div 9 = 48$ (a decrease of $36 \\\\div 9 = 4$). The median is the 5th value in order. The recorded value 95 and the corrected value 59 are both greater than 50, so the corrected value still lies above the middle, and the 5th value is still 50. Choice B assumes the median also drops by 4, and choice C subtracts the full 36 from the mean instead of spreading the change over 9 values.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Dastlabki yig‘indi $9 \\\\times 52 = 468$. 95 ni 59 ga almashtirish yig‘indini $95 - 59 = 36$ ga kamaytiradi: yangi yig‘indi 432, yangi o‘rta qiymat $432 \\\\div 9 = 48$ (ya’ni $36 \\\\div 9 = 4$ ga kamaydi). Mediana — tartiblangan ro‘yxatdagi 5-qiymat. Xato yozilgan 95 ham, to‘g‘ri qiymat 59 ham 50 dan katta, shuning uchun tuzatilgan qiymat ham o‘rtadan yuqorida qoladi va 5-qiymat yana 50 bo‘ladi. B javob mediana ham 4 ga kamayadi deb hisoblagan, C javob esa 36 ni 9 ta qiymatga taqsimlamasdan, o‘rta qiymatdan to‘liq ayirgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A data set of $n$ values has a mean of 15. When the value 39 is added to the data set, the mean of the $n + 1$ values is 17. What is the value of $n$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"11\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The sum of the original values is $15n$. After 39 is added, the sum is $15n + 39$ and there are $n + 1$ values, so $\\\\frac{15n + 39}{n + 1} = 17$. Then $15n + 39 = 17n + 17$, so $22 = 2n$ and $n = 11$. Check: the original sum is 165, and $\\\\frac{165 + 39}{12} = \\\\frac{204}{12} = 17$. A common error is to write $15n + 39 = 17n$, which gives 19.5; this forgets that the number of values also increases by 1.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Dastlabki qiymatlar yig‘indisi $15n$. 39 qo‘shilgach, yig‘indi $15n + 39$, qiymatlar soni esa $n + 1$ bo‘ladi: $\\\\frac{15n + 39}{n + 1} = 17$. Bundan $15n + 39 = 17n + 17$, $22 = 2n$ va $n = 11$. Tekshiruv: dastlabki yig‘indi 165, $\\\\frac{165 + 39}{12} = \\\\frac{204}{12} = 17$ ✓. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — $15n + 39 = 17n$ deb yozish (bundan 19.5 chiqadi): qiymatlar soni ham 1 taga oshganini unutmang.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Of the 260 students in a school's tenth grade, 35% take a foreign-language elective. How many tenth-grade students take a foreign-language elective?\",\"option_a\":\"$91$\",\"option_b\":\"$169$\",\"option_c\":\"$225$\",\"option_d\":\"$351$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"35% of 260 is $0.35 \\\\times 260 = 91$. Choice B, 169, is the number of students who do **not** take the elective (65% of 260). Choice C subtracts 35 from 260, treating the percent as a number of students. Choice D increases 260 by 35% ($1.35 \\\\times 260$) instead of finding 35% of 260.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"260 ning 35% i: $0.35 \\\\times 260 = 91$. B javob (169) — tanlov fanini **o‘qimaydigan** o‘quvchilar soni (260 ning 65% i). C javob foizni o‘quvchilar soni deb olib, 260 dan 35 ni ayirgan. D javob esa 260 ning 35% ini topish o‘rniga 260 ni 35% ga oshirgan ($1.35 \\\\times 260$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A phone plan costs \\\\$32 per month. Next year, the monthly price will increase by 12.5%. What will the new monthly price be, in dollars?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"36\"],\"explanation_en\":\"A 12.5% increase multiplies the price by $1 + 0.125 = 1.125$: $32 \\\\times 1.125 = 36$. (The increase itself is $0.125 \\\\times 32 = 4$ dollars.) Entering 4 gives only the amount of the increase, not the new price. Enter 36 without a dollar sign.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"12.5% ga oshish narxni $1 + 0.125 = 1.125$ ga ko‘paytiradi: $32 \\\\times 1.125 = 36$. (Oshishning o‘zi $0.125 \\\\times 32 = 4$ dollar.) 4 deb yozsangiz, bu yangi narx emas, faqat oshish miqdori bo‘ladi. Javob maydoniga dollar belgisisiz 36 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In a parking lot, 18 of the 72 cars are white. What percent of the cars in the parking lot are white?\",\"option_a\":\"4%\",\"option_b\":\"18%\",\"option_c\":\"25%\",\"option_d\":\"75%\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Divide the part by the whole: $\\\\frac{18}{72} = 0.25$, which is 25%. Choice D, 75%, is the percent of cars that are **not** white. Choice B treats the number of white cars as a percent, and choice A divides the whole by the part ($72 \\\\div 18 = 4$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qismni butunga bo‘lamiz: $\\\\frac{18}{72} = 0.25$, ya’ni 25%. D javob (75%) — oq **bo‘lmagan** mashinalar ulushi. B javob oq mashinalar sonini foiz deb olgan, A javob esa butunni qismga bo‘lgan ($72 \\\\div 18 = 4$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A city's buses carried 40,000 riders in March and 50,000 riders in April. The number of riders in April was what percent greater than the number of riders in March?\",\"option_a\":\"10%\",\"option_b\":\"20%\",\"option_c\":\"25%\",\"option_d\":\"125%\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Percent increase $= \\\\frac{\\\\text{new} - \\\\text{original}}{\\\\text{original}} \\\\times 100\\\\%$, and the original value is March's: $\\\\frac{50{,}000 - 40{,}000}{40{,}000} = \\\\frac{10{,}000}{40{,}000} = 0.25$, or 25%. Choice B divides the increase by April's value ($\\\\frac{10{,}000}{50{,}000} = 20\\\\%$); that answers the different question “March was what percent less than April?” Choice D, 125%, is April's ridership as a percent **of** March's, not the percent greater. Choice A treats the increase of 10 thousand riders as 10%.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Foiz o‘zgarishi $= \\\\frac{\\\\text{new} - \\\\text{original}}{\\\\text{original}} \\\\times 100\\\\%$, bunda asos (eski qiymat) — mart oyi: $\\\\frac{50{,}000 - 40{,}000}{40{,}000} = \\\\frac{10{,}000}{40{,}000} = 0.25$, ya’ni 25%. B javob farqni aprel qiymatiga bo‘lgan ($\\\\frac{10{,}000}{50{,}000} = 20\\\\%$) — bu “mart apreldan necha foiz kam?” degan boshqa savolning javobi. D javob (125%) — aprel yo‘lovchilari martdagilarning necha foizini **tashkil etishi**, necha foiz ko‘pligi emas. A javob 10 ming yo‘lovchilik farqni 10% deb olgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The population of a town increased by 8% from 2020 to 2025. The population in 2025 was 16,200. What was the population of the town in 2020?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"15000\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Let $x$ be the 2020 population. An 8% increase multiplies it by 1.08, so $1.08x = 16{,}200$ and $x = \\\\frac{16{,}200}{1.08} = 15{,}000$. A tempting shortcut is to decrease 16,200 by 8%: $0.92 \\\\times 16{,}200 = 14{,}904$. That is wrong because the 8% was calculated from the 2020 population, not from the 2025 population. Check: $15{,}000 \\\\times 1.08 = 16{,}200$. Enter 15000 (without a comma).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"2020 yilgi aholini $x$ deb olamiz. 8% ga oshish uni 1.08 ga ko‘paytiradi: $1.08x = 16{,}200$, demak $x = \\\\frac{16{,}200}{1.08} = 15{,}000$. 16,200 ni 8% ga kamaytirish ($0.92 \\\\times 16{,}200 = 14{,}904$) — tuzoq: 8% 2025 yilgi emas, 2020 yilgi aholidan hisoblangan. Tekshiruv: $15{,}000 \\\\times 1.08 = 16{,}200$ ✓. Javob maydoniga vergulsiz 15000 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A store reduced the price of a laptop by 30%. Later, the store reduced the new price by an additional 20%. The final price is what percent less than the original price?\",\"option_a\":\"10%\",\"option_b\":\"44%\",\"option_c\":\"50%\",\"option_d\":\"56%\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Apply the reductions one after the other. A 30% reduction multiplies the price by 0.70, and a further 20% reduction multiplies the new price by 0.80, so the final price is $0.70 \\\\times 0.80 \\\\times P = 0.56P$. The final price is 56% of the original price, so it is $100\\\\% - 56\\\\% = 44\\\\%$ less than the original. Choice C, 50%, adds the two percents, but the second 20% is taken from the already reduced price, so it removes less than 20% of the original price. Choice D, 56%, is the final price as a percent **of** the original, not the percent decrease, and choice A subtracts the percents.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Chegirmalarni ketma-ket qo‘llaymiz. 30% chegirma narxni 0.70 ga, keyingi 20% chegirma esa yangi narxni 0.80 ga ko‘paytiradi: oxirgi narx $0.70 \\\\times 0.80 \\\\times P = 0.56P$. Oxirgi narx dastlabki narxning 56% i, demak u dastlabki narxdan $100\\\\% - 56\\\\% = 44\\\\%$ kam. C javob (50%) ikki foizni qo‘shgan, lekin ikkinchi 20% allaqachon kamaygan narxdan olinadi, shuning uchun u dastlabki narxning 20% idan kamroq qismini olib tashlaydi. D javob (56%) — oxirgi narx dastlabki narxning **necha foizi** ekani, kamayish foizi emas. A javob esa foizlarni ayirgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The positive number $k$ is 60% greater than the positive number $m$, and $m$ is 25% less than the positive number $n$. The value of $k$ is what percent of the value of $n$?\",\"option_a\":\"120%\",\"option_b\":\"128%\",\"option_c\":\"135%\",\"option_d\":\"160%\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Translate each statement into a multiplier. “60% greater than $m$” means $k = 1.6m$, and “25% less than $n$” means $m = 0.75n$. Substituting, $k = 1.6(0.75n) = 1.2n$, so $k$ is 120% of $n$. Choice C adds and subtracts the percents ($100\\\\% + 60\\\\% - 25\\\\%$), which ignores that the 60% is a percent of $m$, not of $n$. Choice B comes from writing $n = 1.25m$ instead of $m = 0.75n$; in “25% less than $n$,” the base is $n$. Choice D compares $k$ with $m$ only.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir jumlani ko‘paytuvchiga aylantiramiz. “$m$ dan 60% katta” — $k = 1.6m$; “$n$ dan 25% kichik” — $m = 0.75n$. O‘rniga qo‘ysak: $k = 1.6(0.75n) = 1.2n$, ya’ni $k$ son $n$ ning 120% i. C javob foizlarni qo‘shib-ayirgan ($100\\\\% + 60\\\\% - 25\\\\%$), lekin 60% $n$ dan emas, $m$ dan olinadi. B javob $m = 0.75n$ o‘rniga $n = 1.25m$ deb yozishdan kelib chiqadi; “$n$ dan 25% kichik” jumlasida asos — $n$. D javob esa $k$ ni faqat $m$ bilan solishtirgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The price of a backpack was increased by $p\\\\%$, where $p > 0$. Later, the new price was decreased by $p\\\\%$. The final price was 96% of the original price. What is the value of $p$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"20\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Let the original price be $P$. After the increase and the decrease, the price is $P\\\\left(1 + \\\\frac{p}{100}\\\\right)\\\\left(1 - \\\\frac{p}{100}\\\\right) = P\\\\left(1 - \\\\frac{p^2}{10{,}000}\\\\right)$. Setting this equal to $0.96P$ gives $\\\\frac{p^2}{10{,}000} = 0.04$, so $p^2 = 400$ and $p = 20$ (since $p > 0$). Check: $1.20 \\\\times 0.80 = 0.96$. A common mistake is to assume that equal percent increases and decreases cancel, or to split the 4% loss and enter 2. They never cancel: the decrease is applied to a larger amount, so the final price is always $\\\\frac{p^2}{100}$ percent below the original.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Dastlabki narx $P$ bo‘lsin. Oshirish va kamaytirishdan keyin narx $P\\\\left(1 + \\\\frac{p}{100}\\\\right)\\\\left(1 - \\\\frac{p}{100}\\\\right) = P\\\\left(1 - \\\\frac{p^2}{10{,}000}\\\\right)$ bo‘ladi. Buni $0.96P$ ga tenglaymiz: $\\\\frac{p^2}{10{,}000} = 0.04$, ya’ni $p^2 = 400$ va $p = 20$ (shartga ko‘ra $p > 0$). Tekshiruv: $1.20 \\\\times 0.80 = 0.96$ ✓. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — bir xil foizga oshirish va kamaytirish bir-birini yo‘qqa chiqaradi deb o‘ylash yoki 4% yo‘qotishni ikkiga bo‘lib, 2 deb yozish. Ular hech qachon teng kuchli emas: kamaytirish kattaroq narxga qo‘llanadi, shuning uchun oxirgi narx har doim dastlabkisidan $\\\\frac{p^2}{100}$ foiz past bo‘ladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A jar contains 6 strawberry candies, 9 lemon candies, and 5 mint candies. If one candy is selected at random from the jar, what is the probability that it is **not** a lemon candy?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{1}{4}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{9}{20}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{11}{20}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{9}{11}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"There are $6 + 9 + 5 = 20$ candies, and $6 + 5 = 11$ of them are not lemon, so the probability is $\\\\frac{11}{20}$. (Equivalently, $1 - \\\\frac{9}{20} = \\\\frac{11}{20}$.) Choice B is the probability that the candy **is** lemon. Choice D compares the lemon candies with the other candies instead of dividing by the total, and choice A counts only the mint candies.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Jami $6 + 9 + 5 = 20$ ta konfet bor, ulardan $6 + 5 = 11$ tasi limonli emas, demak ehtimollik $\\\\frac{11}{20}$. (Yoki: $1 - \\\\frac{9}{20} = \\\\frac{11}{20}$.) B javob — konfetning limonli **bo‘lish** ehtimolligi. D javob limonli konfetlarni qolganlari bilan solishtirgan, jami songa bo‘lmagan, A javob esa faqat yalpizli konfetlarni hisoblagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A fair spinner is divided into 8 equal sections numbered 1 through 8. If the spinner is spun once, what is the probability that it lands on a number greater than 5?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3/8\",\".375\",\"0.375\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The numbers greater than 5 are 6, 7 and 8: 3 of the 8 equally likely outcomes. The probability is $\\\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375$. Including 5 itself would give $\\\\frac{4}{8}$, but “greater than 5” does not include 5. Enter 3/8 or .375.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"5 dan katta sonlar — 6, 7 va 8: teng imkoniyatli 8 ta natijadan 3 tasi. Ehtimollik $\\\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375$. 5 ning o‘zini ham sanash $\\\\frac{4}{8}$ ni beradi, lekin “5 dan katta” shartiga 5 kirmaydi. Javob maydoniga 3/8 yoki .375 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"At a factory, the probability that a randomly selected light bulb is defective is 0.02. Based on this probability, how many defective bulbs would be expected in a shipment of 1,500 bulbs?\",\"option_a\":\"$3$\",\"option_b\":\"$30$\",\"option_c\":\"$300$\",\"option_d\":\"$1{,}470$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The expected number is the probability times the number of bulbs: $0.02 \\\\times 1{,}500 = 30$. Choice C uses 0.2 instead of 0.02, choice A uses 0.002, and choice D is the expected number of bulbs that are **not** defective.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kutilgan son — ehtimollik ko‘paytirilgan lampalar soni: $0.02 \\\\times 1{,}500 = 30$. C javob 0.02 o‘rniga 0.2 ni, A javob esa 0.002 ni ishlatgan. D javob — nuqsonsiz lampalarning kutilgan soni.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"If one of the residents who usually travel to work by metro is selected at random, what is the probability that the resident is under 30 years old?\",\"passage\":\"A city surveyed 250 residents about how they usually travel to work. The results, by age group, are shown in the table.\\n\\n| Age group | Bus | Metro | Car | Total |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| Under 30 years old | 40 | 65 | 15 | 120 |\\n| 30 years old or older | 35 | 45 | 50 | 130 |\\n| Total | 75 | 110 | 65 | 250 |\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{13}{50}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{11}{25}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{13}{24}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{13}{22}$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The selection is made only from the residents who travel by metro, so the denominator is $65 + 45 = 110$. Of these, 65 are under 30, so the probability is $\\\\frac{65}{110} = \\\\frac{13}{22}$. Choice C reverses the condition: $\\\\frac{65}{120}$ is the probability that a resident under 30 travels by metro. Choice A divides by all 250 residents, and choice B is the fraction of all residents surveyed who travel by metro.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tanlov faqat metroda qatnaydigan aholi orasidan amalga oshiriladi, shuning uchun maxraj $65 + 45 = 110$. Ulardan 65 nafari 30 yoshdan kichik, demak ehtimollik $\\\\frac{65}{110} = \\\\frac{13}{22}$. C javobda shart teskari olingan: $\\\\frac{65}{120}$ — 30 yoshdan kichik odamning metroda qatnash ehtimolligi. A javob barcha 250 kishiga bo‘lgan, B javob esa metroda qatnaydiganlarning barcha so‘ralganlar ichidagi ulushi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A sports club has 180 members: 75 are in grade 10, and the rest are in grade 11. All members took a swimming test. Of the grade 10 members, 48 passed the test, and of the grade 11 members, 63 passed the test. If one of the members who did **not** pass the test is selected at random, what is the probability that the member is in grade 11?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"14/23\",\"42/69\",\".6086\",\".6087\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Grade 11 has $180 - 75 = 105$ members. The members who did not pass are $75 - 48 = 27$ in grade 10 and $105 - 63 = 42$ in grade 11, for a total of 69. The selection is made from these 69 members, so the probability is $\\\\frac{42}{69} = \\\\frac{14}{23} \\\\approx 0.6087$. A common error is to divide by 105, the number of grade 11 members: $\\\\frac{42}{105}$ is the probability that a grade 11 member did not pass, which reverses the condition. Enter 14/23, .6086 or .6087.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"11-sinfda $180 - 75 = 105$ a’zo bor. Testdan o‘tmaganlar: 10-sinfda $75 - 48 = 27$ nafar, 11-sinfda $105 - 63 = 42$ nafar, jami 69 nafar. Tanlov shu 69 kishi orasidan, demak ehtimollik $\\\\frac{42}{69} = \\\\frac{14}{23} \\\\approx 0.6087$. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — 105 ga, ya’ni 11-sinf a’zolari soniga bo‘lish: $\\\\frac{42}{105}$ — 11-sinf a’zosining testdan o‘tmaslik ehtimolligi, bunda shart teskari olingan. Javob maydoniga 14/23, .6086 yoki .6087 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Of the 60 students in a science program, 28 take chemistry, 22 take physics, and 10 take both chemistry and physics. If one student in the program is selected at random, what is the probability that the student takes chemistry or physics (or both)?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{1}{6}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{1}{3}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{2}{3}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{5}{6}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Adding $28 + 22 = 50$ counts the 10 students who take both subjects twice. The number of students who take at least one of the subjects is $28 + 22 - 10 = 40$, so the probability is $\\\\frac{40}{60} = \\\\frac{2}{3}$. Choice D, $\\\\frac{50}{60}$, is the double-counting error. Choice B, $\\\\frac{20}{60}$, is the probability that the student takes neither subject, and choice A is the probability that the student takes both.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$28 + 22 = 50$ deb qo‘shsak, ikkala fanni o‘qiydigan 10 o‘quvchi ikki marta sanaladi. Kamida bitta fanni o‘qiydiganlar soni: $28 + 22 - 10 = 40$, demak ehtimollik $\\\\frac{40}{60} = \\\\frac{2}{3}$. D javob ($\\\\frac{50}{60}$) — ikki marta sanash xatosi. B javob ($\\\\frac{20}{60}$) — hech bir fanni o‘qimaslik ehtimolligi, A javob esa ikkala fanni o‘qish ehtimolligi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"At a company, 40% of the employees work remotely, and the rest work on-site. Of the employees who work remotely, 30% are engineers. Of the employees who work on-site, 45% are engineers. If one of the company's engineers is selected at random, what is the probability that the engineer works remotely?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{3}{10}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{4}{13}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{39}{100}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{2}{5}$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Imagine the company has 1,000 employees. Then 400 work remotely, and $0.30 \\\\times 400 = 120$ of them are engineers; 600 work on-site, and $0.45 \\\\times 600 = 270$ of them are engineers. There are $120 + 270 = 390$ engineers, and the selection is made from them, so the probability is $\\\\frac{120}{390} = \\\\frac{4}{13}$. Choice A, $\\\\frac{3}{10}$, is the probability that a **remote** employee is an engineer, which reverses the condition. Choice C is the fraction of all employees who are engineers, and choice D is the fraction of all employees who work remotely.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kompaniyada 1,000 xodim bor deb tasavvur qiling. Unda 400 kishi masofadan ishlaydi va ulardan $0.30 \\\\times 400 = 120$ nafari muhandis; 600 kishi ofisda ishlaydi va ulardan $0.45 \\\\times 600 = 270$ nafari muhandis. Jami $120 + 270 = 390$ muhandis bor va tanlov shular orasidan, demak ehtimollik $\\\\frac{120}{390} = \\\\frac{4}{13}$. A javob ($\\\\frac{3}{10}$) — **masofadan ishlovchi** xodimning muhandis bo‘lish ehtimolligi, ya’ni shart teskari olingan. C javob — barcha xodimlar ichida muhandislar ulushi, D javob esa barcha xodimlar ichida masofadan ishlovchilar ulushi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A box contains only red pens and blue pens, and $\\\\frac{2}{5}$ of the pens are red. After 9 blue pens are removed from the box, the probability of selecting a red pen at random from the box is $\\\\frac{1}{2}$. How many pens were in the box before any pens were removed?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"45\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Let $n$ be the original number of pens. Then there are $\\\\frac{2}{5}n$ red pens and $\\\\frac{3}{5}n$ blue pens. After 9 blue pens are removed, a probability of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ means the numbers of red and blue pens are equal: $\\\\frac{2}{5}n = \\\\frac{3}{5}n - 9$. So $\\\\frac{1}{5}n = 9$ and $n = 45$. Check: there are 18 red pens and 27 blue pens; after 9 blue pens are removed, there are 18 of each. Entering 36 gives the number of pens **after** the removal, not before.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Dastlabki ruchkalar soni $n$ bo‘lsin. Unda qizil ruchkalar $\\\\frac{2}{5}n$ ta, ko‘klari $\\\\frac{3}{5}n$ ta. 9 ta ko‘k ruchka olingach, qizil ruchkani tanlash ehtimolligi $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ ga teng bo‘lishi qizil va ko‘k ruchkalar soni tengligini bildiradi: $\\\\frac{2}{5}n = \\\\frac{3}{5}n - 9$. Bundan $\\\\frac{1}{5}n = 9$ va $n = 45$. Tekshiruv: 18 ta qizil va 27 ta ko‘k ruchka; 9 ta ko‘k ruchka olingach, har biridan 18 tadan qoladi ✓. 36 deb yozish — bu olib tashlangandan **keyingi** ruchkalar soni, savol esa dastlabki sonni so‘rayapti.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A printer prints 18 pages every 45 seconds. At this rate, how many pages does the printer print in 3 minutes?\",\"option_a\":\"$54$\",\"option_b\":\"$72$\",\"option_c\":\"$135$\",\"option_d\":\"$450$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Convert 3 minutes to seconds: $3 \\\\times 60 = 180$ seconds. The printer's rate is $\\\\frac{18}{45} = 0.4$ page per second, so in 180 seconds it prints $0.4 \\\\times 180 = 72$ pages. (Equivalently, 180 seconds contains $180 \\\\div 45 = 4$ intervals of 45 seconds, and $4 \\\\times 18 = 72$.) Choice A, 54, treats the rate as 18 pages per minute ($18 \\\\times 3$), but the 18 pages take 45 seconds, not 60. Choice D uses the inverted rate (seconds per page), and choice C multiplies the wrong quantity, 45, by 3.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"3 daqiqani soniyaga aylantiramiz: $3 \\\\times 60 = 180$ soniya. Printerning tezligi $\\\\frac{18}{45} = 0.4$ sahifa/soniya, demak 180 soniyada $0.4 \\\\times 180 = 72$ sahifa chop etadi. (Yoki: 180 soniyada $180 \\\\div 45 = 4$ ta 45 soniyalik oraliq bor, $4 \\\\times 18 = 72$.) A javob (54) tezlikni daqiqasiga 18 sahifa deb olgan ($18 \\\\times 3$), vaholanki 18 sahifa 60 emas, 45 soniyada chiqadi. D javobda tezlik teskari olingan (bir sahifaga ketadigan soniyalar), C javob esa noto‘g‘ri miqdorni, ya’ni 45 ni 3 ga ko‘paytirgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In a school choir, the ratio of sopranos to altos is $5 : 3$. If the choir has 40 sopranos, how many altos does it have?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"24\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Write the ratio with a common multiplier: sopranos $= 5k$ and altos $= 3k$. Since $5k = 40$, $k = 8$, so there are $3 \\\\times 8 = 24$ altos. A common mistake is to scale the wrong way, $40 \\\\times \\\\frac{5}{3} \\\\approx 66.7$, which would make the altos outnumber the sopranos and contradict the ratio $5 : 3$. Another is to enter 64, which is the total number of singers ($8k$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Nisbatni umumiy ko‘paytuvchi bilan yozamiz: sopranolar $= 5k$, altlar $= 3k$. $5k = 40$ bo‘lgani uchun $k = 8$, demak altlar soni $3 \\\\times 8 = 24$. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — teskari ko‘paytirish: $40 \\\\times \\\\frac{5}{3} \\\\approx 66.7$; bunda altlar sopranolardan ko‘p bo‘lib qoladi, bu esa $5 : 3$ nisbatiga zid. Yana bir xato — 64 deb yozish: bu xordagi barcha qo‘shiqchilar soni ($8k$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A car uses 6 liters of fuel for every 100 kilometers it travels. The car's fuel tank holds 48 liters. How many kilometers can the car travel on a full tank of fuel?\",\"option_a\":\"$8$\",\"option_b\":\"$288$\",\"option_c\":\"$800$\",\"option_d\":\"$4{,}800$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Every 6 liters of fuel carries the car 100 kilometers. A full tank holds $48 \\\\div 6 = 8$ such amounts, so the car can travel $8 \\\\times 100 = 800$ kilometers. Choice A, 8, stops after finding the number of 6-liter portions. Choice B, $48 \\\\times 6 = 288$, multiplies the two quantities instead of dividing. Choice D, $48 \\\\times 100$, treats the rate as 1 liter per 100 kilometers.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har 6 litr yoqilg‘i mashinani 100 kilometrga olib boradi. To‘la bakda shunday $48 \\\\div 6 = 8$ ulush bor, demak mashina $8 \\\\times 100 = 800$ kilometr yura oladi. A javob (8) faqat 6 litrlik ulushlar sonini topib, to‘xtab qolgan. B javob ($48 \\\\times 6 = 288$) bo‘lish o‘rniga ikki miqdorni ko‘paytirgan. D javob ($48 \\\\times 100$) sarfni 100 kilometrga 1 litr deb olgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A rectangular park is 0.6 kilometer long and 0.4 kilometer wide. At noon on a certain day, 1,920 people were in the park. What was the number of people per square kilometer in the park at that time?\",\"option_a\":\"$460.8$\",\"option_b\":\"$960$\",\"option_c\":\"$1{,}920$\",\"option_d\":\"$8{,}000$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Density is the number of people divided by the area. The area of the park is $0.6 \\\\times 0.4 = 0.24$ square kilometer, so the density is $\\\\frac{1{,}920}{0.24} = 8{,}000$ people per square kilometer. The answer should be greater than 1,920: the park is smaller than 1 square kilometer, so a full square kilometer at the same crowding would hold more people. Choice A multiplies by the area instead of dividing. Choice B divides by the perimeter, $2(0.6 + 0.4) = 2$ kilometers, which is a length, not an area, and choice C divides by the sum of the two side lengths.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Zichlik — odamlar soni yuzaga bo‘linadi. Bog‘ning yuzasi $0.6 \\\\times 0.4 = 0.24$ kvadrat kilometr, shuning uchun zichlik $\\\\frac{1{,}920}{0.24} = 8{,}000$ kishi/kvadrat kilometr. Javob 1,920 dan katta bo‘lishi tabiiy: bog‘ 1 kvadrat kilometrdan kichik, demak xuddi shunday gavjumlikda butun bir kvadrat kilometrga ko‘proq odam sig‘adi. A javob yuzaga bo‘lish o‘rniga ko‘paytirgan. B javob perimetrga, $2(0.6 + 0.4) = 2$ kilometrga bo‘lgan — bu yuza emas, uzunlik. C javob esa ikki tomon uzunliklari yig‘indisiga bo‘lgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A garden hose fills a 150-gallon tank in 25 minutes. At this rate, how many **hours** will it take the hose to fill a pool that holds 2,700 gallons?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"7.5\",\"15/2\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The hose's rate is $\\\\frac{150}{25} = 6$ gallons per minute. Filling 2,700 gallons takes $\\\\frac{2{,}700}{6} = 450$ minutes, and $450 \\\\div 60 = 7.5$ hours. The most common error is to enter 450, which is the time in minutes; the question asks for hours. Enter 7.5 or 15/2.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Shlangning tezligi $\\\\frac{150}{25} = 6$ gallon/daqiqa. 2,700 gallonni to‘ldirish uchun $\\\\frac{2{,}700}{6} = 450$ daqiqa kerak, bu esa $450 \\\\div 60 = 7.5$ soat. Eng ko‘p uchraydigan xato — 450 deb yozish: bu daqiqalardagi vaqt, savol esa soatni so‘rayapti. Javob maydoniga 7.5 yoki 15/2 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A paint color is made by mixing blue paint and yellow paint in the ratio $2 : 5$ by volume. A painter needs 21 liters of this paint color. How many liters of blue paint are needed?\",\"option_a\":\"$6$\",\"option_b\":\"$8.4$\",\"option_c\":\"$10.5$\",\"option_d\":\"$15$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The mixture has $2 + 5 = 7$ equal parts, and 2 of them are blue. So blue paint is $\\\\frac{2}{7}$ of the mixture: $\\\\frac{2}{7} \\\\times 21 = 6$ liters (the other 15 liters are yellow). Choice B, 8.4, uses $\\\\frac{2}{5}$, treating the ratio of blue to yellow as if it were the ratio of blue to the whole mixture. Choice C splits the mixture in half, and choice D is the amount of yellow paint.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Aralashmada $2 + 5 = 7$ ta teng qism bor, ulardan 2 tasi ko‘k. Demak ko‘k bo‘yoq aralashmaning $\\\\frac{2}{7}$ qismi: $\\\\frac{2}{7} \\\\times 21 = 6$ litr (qolgan 15 litr — sariq). B javob (8.4) $\\\\frac{2}{5}$ ni ishlatgan, ya’ni ko‘kning sariqqa nisbatini ko‘kning butun aralashmaga nisbati deb olgan. C javob aralashmani teng ikkiga bo‘lgan, D javob esa sariq bo‘yoq miqdori.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A bag contains only red marbles and green marbles, and the ratio of red marbles to green marbles is $3 : 5$. After 12 red marbles are added to the bag, the ratio of red marbles to green marbles is $9 : 10$. How many green marbles are in the bag?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"40\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Let the original numbers be $3k$ red marbles and $5k$ green marbles. After 12 red marbles are added, $\\\\frac{3k + 12}{5k} = \\\\frac{9}{10}$. Cross-multiplying gives $10(3k + 12) = 9(5k)$, so $30k + 120 = 45k$, $15k = 120$ and $k = 8$. The number of green marbles does not change: $5k = 40$. Check: there are $24 + 12 = 36$ red marbles and 40 green marbles, and $36 : 40 = 9 : 10$. Entering 8 (the value of $k$) or 24 (the original number of red marbles) stops one step too early.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Dastlab qizil sharchalar $3k$ ta, yashillari $5k$ ta bo‘lsin. 12 ta qizil sharcha qo‘shilgach: $\\\\frac{3k + 12}{5k} = \\\\frac{9}{10}$. Ko‘paytirib chiqamiz: $10(3k + 12) = 9(5k)$, ya’ni $30k + 120 = 45k$, $15k = 120$ va $k = 8$. Yashil sharchalar soni o‘zgarmaydi: $5k = 40$. Tekshiruv: $24 + 12 = 36$ ta qizil va 40 ta yashil sharcha, $36 : 40 = 9 : 10$ ✓. 8 ($k$ ning qiymati) yoki 24 (dastlabki qizil sharchalar) deb yozish — bir qadam oldin to‘xtab qolish demakdir.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A rectangular room is 6 yards long and 4 yards wide. Carpet for the room costs \\\\$2.75 per square foot. What is the cost of carpet to cover the entire floor of the room? (1 yard = 3 feet)\",\"option_a\":\"\\\\$66\",\"option_b\":\"\\\\$198\",\"option_c\":\"\\\\$594\",\"option_d\":\"\\\\$1,782\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Convert the dimensions to feet first: $6 \\\\times 3 = 18$ feet and $4 \\\\times 3 = 12$ feet, so the area is $18 \\\\times 12 = 216$ square feet. (Equivalently, the area is 24 square yards, and 1 square yard is $3 \\\\times 3 = 9$ square feet, so $24 \\\\times 9 = 216$.) The cost is $216 \\\\times 2.75 = 594$ dollars. Choice B multiplies the area in square yards by 3, but a square yard is 9 square feet, not 3. Choice A skips the conversion entirely, and choice D multiplies by 27, the conversion factor for cubic yards.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Avval o‘lchamlarni futga o‘tkazamiz: $6 \\\\times 3 = 18$ fut va $4 \\\\times 3 = 12$ fut, demak yuza $18 \\\\times 12 = 216$ kvadrat fut. (Yoki: yuza 24 kvadrat yard, 1 kvadrat yard esa $3 \\\\times 3 = 9$ kvadrat fut, shuning uchun $24 \\\\times 9 = 216$.) Narx: $216 \\\\times 2.75 = 594$ dollar. B javob kvadrat yarddagi yuzani 3 ga ko‘paytirgan, lekin 1 kvadrat yard 3 emas, 9 kvadrat futga teng. A javob birliklarni umuman almashtirmagan, D javob esa kub yard uchun ko‘paytuvchi bo‘lgan 27 ga ko‘paytirgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":125,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- Tardigrades are tiny animals that are usually less than 1 millimeter long.\\n- They live in many environments, including mosses, soil, and ocean sediments.\\n- When their surroundings dry out, tardigrades can enter a state called a tun.\\n- In the tun state, a tardigrade pulls in its head and legs and loses most of the water in its body.\\n- A tardigrade can remain in the tun state for years and become active again when water returns.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to describe what happens to a tardigrade's body when it enters the tun state. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"Tardigrades, which are usually less than 1 millimeter long, live in mosses, soil, and ocean sediments.\",\"option_b\":\"When a tardigrade enters the tun state, it pulls in its head and legs and loses most of the water in its body.\",\"option_c\":\"Tardigrades can enter a state called a tun when their surroundings dry out.\",\"option_d\":\"A tardigrade can stay in the tun state for years before becoming active again.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to describe what happens to a tardigrade's body in the tun state. Choice B does exactly that, using the note that the animal pulls in its head and legs and loses most of its body water.\\n\\nChoice A describes the animal's size and habitats, not the tun state. Choice C says when a tardigrade enters the tun state but not what happens to its body. Choice D tells how long the state can last, which is also not a description of the body's changes.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — tardigrada tun holatiga o‘tganda uning tanasida nima sodir bo‘lishini tasvirlash. B aynan shuni qiladi: hayvon boshi va oyoqlarini ichkariga tortishi hamda tanasidagi suvning katta qismini yo‘qotishi haqidagi eslatmadan foydalanadi.\\n\\nA — tun holati haqida emas, hayvonning kattaligi va yashash joylari haqida. C — tardigrada qachon tun holatiga o‘tishini aytadi, lekin tanasida nima bo‘lishini aytmaydi. D — bu holat qancha davom etishini aytadi; bu ham tanadagi o‘zgarishlarning tavsifi emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- Ulugh Beg (1394–1449) was a ruler of Samarkand, a city in present-day Uzbekistan.\\n- He was also a mathematician and astronomer.\\n- In the 1420s, he built a large observatory in Samarkand.\\n- The observatory's main instrument was a huge arc, built partly underground, that was used to measure the positions of the Sun and stars.\\n- Astronomers working at the observatory produced a catalog of about 1,000 stars.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to introduce Ulugh Beg to an audience unfamiliar with him. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"In the 1420s, an observatory was built in Samarkand, a city in present-day Uzbekistan.\",\"option_b\":\"The observatory's main instrument, a huge arc built partly underground, measured the positions of the Sun and stars.\",\"option_c\":\"Ulugh Beg (1394–1449), a ruler of Samarkand who was also an astronomer, built an observatory in the city in the 1420s.\",\"option_d\":\"Astronomers at Ulugh Beg's observatory produced a catalog of about 1,000 stars.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"To introduce a person to readers who do not know him, a sentence should say who he was. Choice C names Ulugh Beg, gives his dates, identifies him as a ruler and an astronomer, and adds his best-known achievement, the observatory.\\n\\nChoices A and B describe the observatory without mentioning Ulugh Beg at all. Choice D mentions him only in passing (“Ulugh Beg's observatory”) and assumes the reader already knows who he was.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Shaxsni uni tanimaydigan o‘quvchilarga tanishtirish uchun gap u kim bo‘lganini aytishi kerak. C Ulug‘bekning ismini, yashagan yillarini aytadi, uni hukmdor va astronom sifatida tanishtiradi hamda eng mashhur ishi — rasadxonani qo‘shadi.\\n\\nA va B — rasadxonani tasvirlaydi, lekin Ulug‘bekni umuman tilga olmaydi. D — uni faqat o‘tib ketishda eslaydi (“Ulugh Beg’s observatory”) va o‘quvchi uni allaqachon taniydi deb hisoblaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- Mars has two small moons, Phobos and Deimos.\\n- Both moons are irregularly shaped rather than round.\\n- Phobos is about 22 kilometers across, and Deimos is about 12 kilometers across.\\n- Phobos completes one orbit around Mars about every 7.7 hours.\\n- Deimos completes one orbit around Mars about every 30.3 hours.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to emphasize a difference between the times that Phobos and Deimos take to orbit Mars. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"Phobos and Deimos, Mars's two moons, are both irregularly shaped.\",\"option_b\":\"Phobos, which is about 22 kilometers across, is larger than Deimos, which is about 12 kilometers across.\",\"option_c\":\"Mars has two small moons, one of which, Phobos, orbits the planet about once every 7.7 hours.\",\"option_d\":\"While Phobos orbits Mars in about 7.7 hours, Deimos takes about 30.3 hours to complete one orbit.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to emphasize a difference in the two moons' orbital times. Choice D gives both times (about 7.7 hours and about 30.3 hours) and uses “While” to set them against each other.\\n\\nChoice A presents a similarity, not a difference. Choice B emphasizes a difference, but in size rather than in orbital time. Choice C gives the orbital time of Phobos only, so there is nothing to compare it with.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — ikki yo‘ldoshning orbita bo‘ylab aylanish vaqtidagi farqni ta’kidlash. D ikkala vaqtni ham beradi (taxminan 7.7 soat va taxminan 30.3 soat) va “While” so‘zi bilan ularni bir-biriga qarama-qarshi qo‘yadi.\\n\\nA — farqni emas, o‘xshashlikni ko‘rsatadi. B — farqni ta’kidlaydi, lekin aylanish vaqtidagi emas, kattalikdagi farqni. C — faqat Fobosning aylanish vaqtini beradi, uni solishtiradigan narsa yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- Cities are often warmer than nearby rural areas, partly because dark roofs and pavement absorb sunlight.\\n- Engineer Laylo Rashidova led a research team that coated the roofs of 40 buildings with a white, reflective paint.\\n- The team compared the temperatures of those roofs with the temperatures of 40 similar uncoated roofs over one summer.\\n- On the hottest afternoons, the coated roofs were on average 12°C cooler than the uncoated roofs.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to present the results of the research team's study. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"In a study led by Laylo Rashidova, roofs coated with white reflective paint were on average 12°C cooler on the hottest afternoons than similar uncoated roofs.\",\"option_b\":\"Dark roofs and pavement absorb sunlight, which is one reason that cities are often warmer than nearby rural areas.\",\"option_c\":\"Rashidova's team coated 40 roofs with white reflective paint and compared them with 40 similar uncoated roofs over one summer.\",\"option_d\":\"Laylo Rashidova, an engineer, led a research team that studied the temperatures of rooftops.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Results are what a study found. Choice A presents the study's key finding: on the hottest afternoons, the coated roofs were on average 12°C cooler than similar uncoated roofs.\\n\\nChoice B gives background information about why cities are warm, not the results of the study. Choice C describes the study's method (what the team did) but not what the team found. Choice D only introduces the researcher and the general topic.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Natijalar — tadqiqot nimani aniqlaganidir. A tadqiqotning asosiy natijasini keltiradi: eng issiq kunduzgi soatlarda bo‘yalgan tomlar xuddi shunday bo‘yalmagan tomlardan o‘rtacha 12°C salqinroq bo‘lgan.\\n\\nB — shaharlar nima uchun issiq bo‘lishi haqidagi umumiy ma’lumot, tadqiqot natijasi emas. C — tadqiqot usulini (jamoa nima qilganini) tasvirlaydi, lekin nimani aniqlaganini aytmaydi. D — faqat tadqiqotchini va umumiy mavzuni tanishtiradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- The dromedary camel has one hump and lives mainly in the hot deserts of North Africa and the Middle East.\\n- The Bactrian camel has two humps and lives mainly in the cold deserts and steppes of Central Asia.\\n- A camel's hump stores fat, not water.\\n- Both species can go many days without drinking water.\\n- Bactrian camels grow a thick coat in winter and shed it in spring.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to emphasize a similarity between dromedary camels and Bactrian camels. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"The dromedary camel has one hump, while the Bactrian camel has two.\",\"option_b\":\"Both the dromedary camel and the Bactrian camel can go many days without drinking water.\",\"option_c\":\"Bactrian camels, which live mainly in Central Asia, grow a thick coat every winter.\",\"option_d\":\"Dromedaries live mainly in hot deserts, but Bactrian camels live mainly in cold deserts and steppes.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Choice B emphasizes a similarity: it uses “Both” to show that the two species share an ability, going many days without drinking water.\\n\\nChoices A and D emphasize differences (the number of humps and the climates where the camels live). Choice C gives a fact about Bactrian camels only, so it does not compare the two species at all.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"B o‘xshashlikni ta’kidlaydi: “Both” so‘zi orqali ikkala tur ham bir xil qobiliyatga — ko‘p kun suv ichmasdan yashay olishga — ega ekanini ko‘rsatadi.\\n\\nA va D — farqlarni (o‘rkachlar soni va tuyalar yashaydigan iqlim) ta’kidlaydi. C — faqat Baqtriya tuyasi haqidagi fakt, unda ikki tur umuman solishtirilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- A karez (also called a qanat) is a system of underground channels that carries water from an aquifer at the foot of the mountains to farmland at lower elevations.\\n- The channel slopes gently downhill, so the water flows through it by gravity, without pumps.\\n- Vertical shafts dug from the surface allow workers to enter the channel to clean and repair it.\\n- Because the water travels underground, much less of it evaporates than would evaporate from an open canal in a hot, dry climate.\\n- Karez systems have been used for centuries in parts of Iran, Central Asia, and western China.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to explain how a karez reduces the loss of water in a hot, dry climate. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"Because the water in a karez travels underground, much less of it evaporates than would evaporate from an open canal in a hot, dry climate.\",\"option_b\":\"Karez systems have been used for centuries in parts of Iran, Central Asia, and western China.\",\"option_c\":\"Workers can enter a karez through vertical shafts in order to clean and repair the channel.\",\"option_d\":\"A karez carries water from an aquifer at the foot of the mountains to farmland at lower elevations.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to explain how a karez keeps water from being lost in a hot, dry climate. Choice A gives that explanation: because the water travels underground, much less of it evaporates than would evaporate from an open canal.\\n\\nChoice B tells where and how long karez systems have been used. Choice C explains how the channels are maintained. Choice D tells where a karez carries water. All three are accurate, but none explains how water loss is reduced.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — korizning issiq va quruq iqlimda suv yo‘qotilishini qanday kamaytirishini tushuntirish. A aynan shuni tushuntiradi: suv yer ostidan oqqani uchun ochiq kanaldagiga qaraganda ancha kam bug‘lanadi.\\n\\nB — koriz tizimlari qayerda va qancha vaqtdan beri ishlatilishini aytadi. C — kanallar qanday ta’mirlanishini tushuntiradi. D — koriz suvni qayerdan qayerga olib borishini aytadi. Uchalasi ham to‘g‘ri ma’lumot, lekin hech biri suv yo‘qotilishi qanday kamayishini tushuntirmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- Linguist Shahnoza Ergasheva studies children who speak both Uzbek and Russian.\\n- She recorded the conversations of 30 bilingual children, ages 6 to 9, during free play at a school in Tashkent over one school year.\\n- Earlier researchers had proposed that bilingual children switch languages mainly when they do not know a word in the language they are speaking.\\n- Ergasheva found that the children often switched languages even when they knew the word in both languages.\\n- She concluded that the children switched languages mainly to signal a change in topic or to include a particular friend in the conversation.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to contrast Ergasheva's conclusion with the earlier researchers' proposal. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"Ergasheva recorded the conversations of 30 bilingual children, ages 6 to 9, during free play at a school in Tashkent over one school year.\",\"option_b\":\"Earlier researchers had proposed that bilingual children switch languages mainly when they do not know a word, but Ergasheva concluded that the children she studied switched mainly to signal a change in topic or to include a particular friend.\",\"option_c\":\"Ergasheva found that the bilingual children she recorded often switched between Uzbek and Russian even when they knew a word in both languages.\",\"option_d\":\"According to earlier researchers, bilingual children switch languages mainly when they do not know a word in the language they are speaking.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal has two parts: Ergasheva's conclusion and the earlier proposal, set against each other. Choice B includes both—the earlier idea that children switch when they lack a word, and Ergasheva's conclusion that they switch to signal a topic change or include a friend—and links them with “but” to show the contrast.\\n\\nChoice A describes only her method. Choice C reports a finding that challenges the earlier view, but it neither states her conclusion nor mentions the earlier proposal. Choice D states only the earlier proposal.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad ikki qismdan iborat: Ergashevaning xulosasi va avvalgi taxminni bir-biriga qarama-qarshi qo‘yish. B ikkalasini ham o‘z ichiga oladi — bolalar so‘zni bilmaganda tilni almashtiradi degan avvalgi fikrni ham, ular mavzu o‘zgarganini bildirish yoki do‘stini suhbatga qo‘shish uchun almashtiradi degan Ergasheva xulosasini ham — va ularni “but” bilan bog‘lab, qarama-qarshilikni ko‘rsatadi.\\n\\nA — faqat tadqiqot usulini tasvirlaydi. C — avvalgi fikrga zid bo‘lgan natijani keltiradi, lekin na Ergashevaning xulosasini, na avvalgi taxminni aytadi. D — faqat avvalgi taxminni bayon qiladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- A refracting telescope uses a lens to gather and focus light.\\n- A reflecting telescope uses a curved mirror to gather and focus light.\\n- Because light must pass through a lens, a lens can be supported only around its edges; a very large lens sags under its own weight and distorts images.\\n- Because light bounces off the front of a mirror, a mirror can be supported across its entire back surface.\\n- The largest lens used in a research telescope is about 1 meter wide, while some reflecting telescopes have mirrors about 10 meters wide.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to explain why reflecting telescopes can be built much larger than refracting telescopes. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"The largest lens used in a research telescope is about 1 meter wide, whereas some reflecting telescopes have mirrors about 10 meters wide.\",\"option_b\":\"A refracting telescope gathers and focuses light with a lens, while a reflecting telescope uses a curved mirror.\",\"option_c\":\"A very large lens sags under its own weight, which distorts the images it produces.\",\"option_d\":\"Because a mirror can be supported across its entire back surface while a lens can be supported only around its edges, reflecting telescopes can use far larger light-gathering surfaces without sagging.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to explain *why* reflecting telescopes can be so much larger. Choice D gives the reason from the notes: a mirror can be supported across its whole back, but a lens can be held only at its edges, so mirrors can be made much larger without sagging.\\n\\nChoice A is tempting because it shows the size difference, but it only states that difference and does not explain it. Choice B describes how the two kinds of telescopes work without addressing size. Choice C gives only half of the reason—the problem with large lenses—and never connects it to mirrors or reflecting telescopes.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — aks ettiruvchi teleskoplarni *nima uchun* ancha katta qilib qurish mumkinligini tushuntirish. D eslatmalardagi sababni keltiradi: ko‘zguni butun orqa yuzasi bo‘ylab tayantirib qo‘yish mumkin, linzani esa faqat chetlaridan ushlab turish mumkin, shuning uchun ko‘zgular egilib qolmasdan ancha katta qilib yasaladi.\\n\\nA jozibali, chunki o‘lchamdagi farqni ko‘rsatadi, lekin faqat farqni aytadi, uni tushuntirmaydi. B — ikki turdagi teleskop qanday ishlashini tasvirlaydi, o‘lcham haqida gapirmaydi. C — sababning faqat yarmini (katta linzalar muammosini) aytadi va uni ko‘zgular yoki aks ettiruvchi teleskoplar bilan bog‘lamaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In right triangle $XYZ$, angle $Z$ is the right angle, $XZ = 8$, and $YZ = 15$. What is the value of $\\\\sin X$?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{8}{17}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{8}{15}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{15}{17}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{15}{8}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"First find the hypotenuse: $XY = \\\\sqrt{8^2 + 15^2} = \\\\sqrt{289} = 17$. The side opposite angle $X$ is $YZ = 15$, so $\\\\sin X = \\\\frac{\\\\text{opposite}}{\\\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\\\frac{15}{17}$. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($\\\\frac{8}{17}$) is $\\\\cos X$, adjacent over hypotenuse. Choice B ($\\\\frac{8}{15}$) is $\\\\tan Y$, adjacent over opposite from angle $X$'s point of view. Choice D ($\\\\frac{15}{8}$) is $\\\\tan X$, opposite over adjacent.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Avval gipotenuzani topamiz: $XY = \\\\sqrt{8^2 + 15^2} = \\\\sqrt{289} = 17$. $X$ burchakka qarama-qarshi katet $YZ = 15$, demak $\\\\sin X = \\\\frac{\\\\text{qarama-qarshi katet}}{\\\\text{gipotenuza}} = \\\\frac{15}{17}$. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA ($\\\\frac{8}{17}$) — bu $\\\\cos X$ (yopishgan katet / gipotenuza). B ($\\\\frac{8}{15}$) — bu $\\\\tan Y$, ya’ni $X$ burchak uchun yopishgan katetning qarama-qarshi katetga nisbati. D ($\\\\frac{15}{8}$) — bu $\\\\tan X$ (qarama-qarshi katet / yopishgan katet).\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A rectangular park is 40 meters wide and 96 meters long. A straight path runs across the park from one corner to the opposite corner. What is the length, in meters, of the path?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"104\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The path is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs are two sides of the park. By the Pythagorean theorem, its length is $\\\\sqrt{40^2 + 96^2} = \\\\sqrt{1{,}600 + 9{,}216} = \\\\sqrt{10{,}816} = 104$ meters. Shortcut: 40, 96, 104 is 8 times the Pythagorean triple 5, 12, 13.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Yo‘lak katetlari parkning ikki tomoni bo‘lgan to‘g‘ri burchakli uchburchakning gipotenuzasi. Pifagor teoremasiga ko‘ra uning uzunligi $\\\\sqrt{40^2 + 96^2} = \\\\sqrt{1{,}600 + 9{,}216} = \\\\sqrt{10{,}816} = 104$ metr. Qisqa yo‘l: 40, 96, 104 — bu 5, 12, 13 Pifagor uchligining 8 barobari.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"For an acute angle that measures $x^\\\\circ$, $\\\\sin(x^\\\\circ) = \\\\cos(26^\\\\circ)$. What is the value of $x$?\",\"option_a\":\"26\",\"option_b\":\"64\",\"option_c\":\"116\",\"option_d\":\"154\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The sine of an acute angle equals the cosine of its complement: $\\\\sin(x^\\\\circ) = \\\\cos((90 - x)^\\\\circ)$. So $90 - x = 26$, and $x = 64$. Choice B is correct. (Check: $\\\\sin 64^\\\\circ \\\\approx 0.899$ and $\\\\cos 26^\\\\circ \\\\approx 0.899$.)\\n\\nChoice A assumes that the sine and cosine of the same angle are equal, which is true only for $45^\\\\circ$. Choices C ($90 + 26$) and D ($180 - 26$) are not acute angles.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"O‘tkir burchakning sinusi uni $90^\\\\circ$ gacha to‘ldiruvchi burchakning kosinusiga teng: $\\\\sin(x^\\\\circ) = \\\\cos((90 - x)^\\\\circ)$. Demak $90 - x = 26$ va $x = 64$. To‘g‘ri javob B. (Tekshiruv: $\\\\sin 64^\\\\circ \\\\approx 0.899$ va $\\\\cos 26^\\\\circ \\\\approx 0.899$.)\\n\\nA — bir xil burchakning sinusi va kosinusi teng deb olingan; bu faqat $45^\\\\circ$ uchun to‘g‘ri. C ($90 + 26$) va D ($180 - 26$) o‘tkir burchak emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In triangle $PQR$, angle $R$ is a right angle, the measure of angle $P$ is $30^\\\\circ$, and $PQ = 18$. What is the length of $\\\\overline{PR}$?\",\"option_a\":\"9\",\"option_b\":\"$6\\\\sqrt{3}$\",\"option_c\":\"$9\\\\sqrt{2}$\",\"option_d\":\"$9\\\\sqrt{3}$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Triangle $PQR$ is a $30^\\\\circ$-$60^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ triangle, so its side lengths are in the ratio $1 : \\\\sqrt{3} : 2$. The hypotenuse is $PQ = 18$, so the shorter leg, $QR$ (opposite the $30^\\\\circ$ angle at $P$), is 9, and the longer leg, $PR$ (opposite the $60^\\\\circ$ angle at $Q$), is $9\\\\sqrt{3}$. Equivalently, $PR = 18 \\\\cos 30^\\\\circ = 18 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 9\\\\sqrt{3}$. Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A (9) is $QR$, the side opposite the $30^\\\\circ$ angle. Choice B ($6\\\\sqrt{3}$) divides the hypotenuse by $\\\\sqrt{3}$. Choice C ($9\\\\sqrt{2}$) uses the side ratio of a $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ triangle.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$PQR$ — $30^\\\\circ$-$60^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ uchburchak, uning tomonlari $1 : \\\\sqrt{3} : 2$ nisbatda bo‘ladi. Gipotenuza $PQ = 18$, demak qisqa katet $QR$ ($P$ dagi $30^\\\\circ$ burchakka qarama-qarshi) 9 ga, uzun katet $PR$ ($Q$ dagi $60^\\\\circ$ burchakka qarama-qarshi) esa $9\\\\sqrt{3}$ ga teng. Boshqacha hisoblasak: $PR = 18 \\\\cos 30^\\\\circ = 18 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 9\\\\sqrt{3}$. To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA (9) — bu $QR$, ya’ni $30^\\\\circ$ burchakka qarama-qarshi tomon. B ($6\\\\sqrt{3}$) — gipotenuza $\\\\sqrt{3}$ ga bo‘lingan. C ($9\\\\sqrt{2}$) — $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ uchburchakning nisbati ishlatilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The diagonal of a square has length 12. What is the area of the square?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"72\"],\"explanation_en\":\"A diagonal divides the square into two $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ triangles, so the diagonal is $\\\\sqrt{2}$ times the side length $s$: $s\\\\sqrt{2} = 12$, which gives $s = \\\\frac{12}{\\\\sqrt{2}} = 6\\\\sqrt{2}$. The area is $s^2 = (6\\\\sqrt{2})^2 = 72$. Shortcut: by the Pythagorean theorem, $s^2 + s^2 = 12^2$, so $2s^2 = 144$ and the area $s^2$ is 72.\\n\\nA common error is answering 144, which is the square of the diagonal, not the area.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Diagonal kvadratni ikkita $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ uchburchakka ajratadi, shuning uchun diagonal tomondan $\\\\sqrt{2}$ marta uzun: $s\\\\sqrt{2} = 12$, bundan $s = \\\\frac{12}{\\\\sqrt{2}} = 6\\\\sqrt{2}$. Yuza $s^2 = (6\\\\sqrt{2})^2 = 72$. Qisqa yo‘l: Pifagor teoremasiga ko‘ra $s^2 + s^2 = 12^2$, ya’ni $2s^2 = 144$ va yuza $s^2 = 72$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — 144 deb javob berish; bu yuza emas, diagonalning kvadrati.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In right triangle $ABC$, angle $C$ is the right angle, $\\\\tan A = \\\\frac{7}{24}$, and $AB = 50$. What is the length of $\\\\overline{BC}$?\",\"option_a\":\"7\",\"option_b\":\"14\",\"option_c\":\"25\",\"option_d\":\"48\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"$\\\\tan A = \\\\frac{\\\\text{opposite}}{\\\\text{adjacent}} = \\\\frac{BC}{AC} = \\\\frac{7}{24}$, so $BC = 7k$ and $AC = 24k$ for some positive number $k$. Then $AB = \\\\sqrt{(7k)^2 + (24k)^2} = \\\\sqrt{625k^2} = 25k$. Since $AB = 50$, $k = 2$, so $BC = 14$ (and $AC = 48$). Choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoice A (7) treats the numerator of the ratio as the actual length. Choice C (25) is the hypotenuse of a 7-24-25 triangle, not of this triangle. Choice D (48) is $AC$, the side adjacent to angle $A$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$\\\\tan A = \\\\frac{\\\\text{qarama-qarshi katet}}{\\\\text{yopishgan katet}} = \\\\frac{BC}{AC} = \\\\frac{7}{24}$, demak qandaydir musbat $k$ uchun $BC = 7k$ va $AC = 24k$. U holda $AB = \\\\sqrt{(7k)^2 + (24k)^2} = \\\\sqrt{625k^2} = 25k$. $AB = 50$ bo‘lgani uchun $k = 2$, demak $BC = 14$ (va $AC = 48$). To‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA (7) — nisbatning suratini haqiqiy uzunlik deb olish. C (25) — 7-24-25 uchburchakning gipotenuzasi, bu uchburchakniki emas. D (48) — bu $AC$, ya’ni $A$ burchakka yopishgan katet.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In triangle $ABC$, the altitude from vertex $B$ meets side $\\\\overline{AC}$ at point $D$, and $BD = 6$. The measure of angle $A$ is $45^\\\\circ$, and the measure of angle $C$ is $30^\\\\circ$. What is the length of $\\\\overline{AC}$?\",\"option_a\":\"$6 + 2\\\\sqrt{3}$\",\"option_b\":\"12\",\"option_c\":\"$6 + 6\\\\sqrt{3}$\",\"option_d\":\"$12 + 6\\\\sqrt{2}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The altitude $\\\\overline{BD}$ divides triangle $ABC$ into two right triangles. In triangle $ABD$, angle $A$ is $45^\\\\circ$, so it is a $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ triangle and $AD = BD = 6$. In triangle $CBD$, angle $C$ is $30^\\\\circ$, so $\\\\tan 30^\\\\circ = \\\\frac{BD}{DC}$, which gives $DC = \\\\frac{6}{\\\\tan 30^\\\\circ} = 6\\\\sqrt{3}$ (the longer leg of a $30^\\\\circ$-$60^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ triangle is $\\\\sqrt{3}$ times the shorter leg). So $AC = AD + DC = 6 + 6\\\\sqrt{3}$. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A uses $DC = \\\\frac{6}{\\\\sqrt{3}} = 2\\\\sqrt{3}$, which puts $\\\\sqrt{3}$ on the wrong leg. Choice B treats both right triangles as $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ triangles. Choice D adds the hypotenuses $AB = 6\\\\sqrt{2}$ and $BC = 12$ instead of the two parts of $\\\\overline{AC}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$\\\\overline{BD}$ balandlik $ABC$ uchburchakni ikkita to‘g‘ri burchakli uchburchakka ajratadi. $ABD$ uchburchakda $A$ burchak $45^\\\\circ$, demak u $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ uchburchak va $AD = BD = 6$. $CBD$ uchburchakda $C$ burchak $30^\\\\circ$, shuning uchun $\\\\tan 30^\\\\circ = \\\\frac{BD}{DC}$, bundan $DC = \\\\frac{6}{\\\\tan 30^\\\\circ} = 6\\\\sqrt{3}$ ($30^\\\\circ$-$60^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ uchburchakda uzun katet qisqa katetdan $\\\\sqrt{3}$ marta uzun). Demak $AC = AD + DC = 6 + 6\\\\sqrt{3}$. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA — $DC = \\\\frac{6}{\\\\sqrt{3}} = 2\\\\sqrt{3}$ deb olingan, ya’ni $\\\\sqrt{3}$ noto‘g‘ri katetga qo‘yilgan. B — ikkala uchburchak ham $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ deb hisoblangan. D — $\\\\overline{AC}$ ning ikki bo‘lagi o‘rniga gipotenuzalar $AB = 6\\\\sqrt{2}$ va $BC = 12$ qo‘shilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the equation $\\\\sin((4x - 8)^\\\\circ) = \\\\cos((2x + 14)^\\\\circ)$, both $(4x - 8)^\\\\circ$ and $(2x + 14)^\\\\circ$ are measures of acute angles. What is the value of $x$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"14\"],\"explanation_en\":\"For acute angles, $\\\\sin(a^\\\\circ) = \\\\cos(b^\\\\circ)$ exactly when the angles are complementary, that is, when $a + b = 90$. So $(4x - 8) + (2x + 14) = 90$, which gives $6x + 6 = 90$ and $x = 14$. Check: the angles are $48^\\\\circ$ and $42^\\\\circ$, both acute, and $48 + 42 = 90$.\\n\\nSetting the two angles equal ($4x - 8 = 2x + 14$) gives $x = 11$, which is incorrect: it would require $\\\\sin 36^\\\\circ = \\\\cos 36^\\\\circ$, and that is false.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"O‘tkir burchaklar uchun $\\\\sin(a^\\\\circ) = \\\\cos(b^\\\\circ)$ tenglik faqat burchaklar bir-birini $90^\\\\circ$ gacha to‘ldirganda, ya’ni $a + b = 90$ bo‘lganda bajariladi. Demak $(4x - 8) + (2x + 14) = 90$, bundan $6x + 6 = 90$ va $x = 14$. Tekshiramiz: burchaklar $48^\\\\circ$ va $42^\\\\circ$, ikkalasi ham o‘tkir va $48 + 42 = 90$.\\n\\nBurchaklarni tenglashtirish ($4x - 8 = 2x + 14$) $x = 11$ ni beradi, lekin bu xato: u holda $\\\\sin 36^\\\\circ = \\\\cos 36^\\\\circ$ bo‘lishi kerak edi, bu esa noto‘g‘ri.\",\"estimated_seconds\":115,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} y &= 2x + 1 \\\\\\\\ 3x + y &= 21 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nWhat is the solution $(x, y)$ to the given system of equations?\",\"option_a\":\"$(9, 4)$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\left(\\\\frac{22}{5}, \\\\frac{49}{5}\\\\right)$\",\"option_c\":\"$(5, 11)$\",\"option_d\":\"$(4, 9)$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $y = 2x + 1$ into the second equation: $3x + (2x + 1) = 21$, so $5x + 1 = 21$, $5x = 20$, and $x = 4$.\\n\\nThen $y = 2(4) + 1 = 9$. Check: $3(4) + 9 = 21$.\\n\\nChoice A has the correct numbers in the wrong order; in an ordered pair, the $x$-value comes first.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y = 2x + 1$ ni ikkinchi tenglamaga qo‘yamiz: $3x + (2x + 1) = 21$, ya’ni $5x + 1 = 21$, $5x = 20$ va $x = 4$.\\n\\nU holda $y = 2(4) + 1 = 9$. Tekshiruv: $3(4) + 9 = 21$.\\n\\nA variantda sonlar to‘g‘ri, lekin tartibi teskari; tartiblangan juftlikda birinchi $x$ ning qiymati yoziladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} 2x + y &= 17 \\\\\\\\ x - y &= 4 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nIf $(x, y)$ is the solution to the given system of equations, what is the value of $y$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Add the two equations to eliminate $y$: $3x = 21$, so $x = 7$.\\n\\nSubstitute into the second equation: $7 - y = 4$, so $y = 3$. Check: $2(7) + 3 = 17$.\\n\\nBe careful to enter the value of $y$; entering $x = 7$ is a common error.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y$ ni yo‘qotish uchun tenglamalarni qo‘shamiz: $3x = 21$, demak $x = 7$.\\n\\nIkkinchi tenglamaga qo‘yamiz: $7 - y = 4$, demak $y = 3$. Tekshiruv: $2(7) + 3 = 17$.\\n\\nE’tibor bering: savol $y$ ni so‘rayapti; $x = 7$ ni kiritish — ko‘p uchraydigan xato.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The sum of two numbers is $50$. The larger number, $y$, is $8$ less than $3$ times the smaller number, $x$. Which system of equations represents this situation?\",\"option_a\":\"$x + y = 50$ and $y = 8 - 3x$\",\"option_b\":\"$x + y = 50$ and $y = 3(x - 8)$\",\"option_c\":\"$x + y = 50$ and $y = 3x - 8$\",\"option_d\":\"$x - y = 50$ and $y = 3x - 8$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"“The sum of two numbers is $50$” gives $x + y = 50$.\\n\\n“$8$ less than $3$ times the smaller number” means start with $3x$ and subtract $8$: $y = 3x - 8$.\\n\\nChoice A reverses the subtraction: “$8$ less than $3x$” is $3x - 8$, not $8 - 3x$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"«Ikki sonning yig‘indisi $50$ ga teng» — bu $x + y = 50$.\\n\\n«Kichik sonning $3$ baravaridan $8$ ta kam» — avval $3x$ ni olib, undan $8$ ni ayiramiz: $y = 3x - 8$.\\n\\nA variantda ayirish tartibi teskari: «$3x$ dan $8$ ta kam» — bu $3x - 8$, $8 - 3x$ emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A florist sold $38$ bouquets on Saturday. Each bouquet was either a small bouquet that sold for \\\\$15 or a large bouquet that sold for \\\\$40. The florist's total revenue from these bouquets was \\\\$895. How many more small bouquets than large bouquets did the florist sell on Saturday?\",\"option_a\":\"$12$\",\"option_b\":\"$13$\",\"option_c\":\"$25$\",\"option_d\":\"$38$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $s$ be the number of small bouquets and $\\\\ell$ the number of large bouquets. Then $s + \\\\ell = 38$ and $15s + 40\\\\ell = 895$.\\n\\nSubstitute $s = 38 - \\\\ell$: $15(38 - \\\\ell) + 40\\\\ell = 895$, so $570 + 25\\\\ell = 895$, $25\\\\ell = 325$, and $\\\\ell = 13$. Then $s = 38 - 13 = 25$.\\n\\nCheck: $15(25) + 40(13) = 375 + 520 = 895$. The difference is $25 - 13 = 12$.\\n\\nChoice C ($25$) is the number of small bouquets, a correct intermediate result that does not answer the question about the difference.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$s$ — kichik guldastalar soni, $\\\\ell$ — katta guldastalar soni bo‘lsin. Unda $s + \\\\ell = 38$ va $15s + 40\\\\ell = 895$.\\n\\n$s = 38 - \\\\ell$ ni qo‘yamiz: $15(38 - \\\\ell) + 40\\\\ell = 895$, ya’ni $570 + 25\\\\ell = 895$, $25\\\\ell = 325$ va $\\\\ell = 13$. U holda $s = 38 - 13 = 25$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $15(25) + 40(13) = 375 + 520 = 895$. Farq: $25 - 13 = 12$.\\n\\nC variant ($25$) — kichik guldastalar soni; bu to‘g‘ri oraliq natija, lekin savol ular orasidagi farqni so‘rayapti.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} 5x + 3y &= 29 \\\\\\\\ 3x + 5y &= 19 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nIf $(x, y)$ is the solution to the given system of equations, what is the value of $x - y$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-5$\",\"option_b\":\"$5$\",\"option_c\":\"$6$\",\"option_d\":\"$10$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Subtract the second equation from the first: $(5x - 3x) + (3y - 5y) = 29 - 19$, so $2x - 2y = 10$. Divide by $2$: $x - y = 5$.\\n\\n(Solving completely gives $x = 5.5$ and $y = 0.5$, and $5.5 - 0.5 = 5$.)\\n\\nChoice C ($6$) is the value of $x + y$, which comes from adding the equations ($8x + 8y = 48$) instead of subtracting them.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi tenglamadan ikkinchisini ayiramiz: $(5x - 3x) + (3y - 5y) = 29 - 19$, ya’ni $2x - 2y = 10$. $2$ ga bo‘lamiz: $x - y = 5$.\\n\\n(To‘liq yechsak, $x = 5.5$ va $y = 0.5$, hamda $5.5 - 0.5 = 5$.)\\n\\nC variant ($6$) — bu $x + y$ ning qiymati: tenglamalarni ayirish o‘rniga qo‘shganda ($8x + 8y = 48$) hosil bo‘ladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} 6x - 4y &= 10 \\\\\\\\ y &= 1.5x - 2.5 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nHow many solutions does the given system of equations have?\",\"option_a\":\"Zero\",\"option_b\":\"Exactly one\",\"option_c\":\"Exactly two\",\"option_d\":\"Infinitely many\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Rewrite the second equation in the same form as the first: $y = 1.5x - 2.5$ becomes $1.5x - y = 2.5$. Multiplying both sides by $4$ gives $6x - 4y = 10$.\\n\\nThis is exactly the first equation, so both equations describe the same line, and every point on that line is a solution. The system has infinitely many solutions.\\n\\nChoice A is tempting because the equations look different, but parallel lines would need different constants after matching the left sides; here the constants match too.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkinchi tenglamani birinchisi ko‘rinishiga keltiramiz: $y = 1.5x - 2.5$ dan $1.5x - y = 2.5$. Ikkala tomonni $4$ ga ko‘paytirsak, $6x - 4y = 10$ hosil bo‘ladi.\\n\\nBu aynan birinchi tenglama, ya’ni ikkala tenglama bitta chiziqni ifodalaydi va shu chiziqdagi har bir nuqta yechim bo‘ladi. Sistema cheksiz ko‘p yechimga ega.\\n\\nA variant — tuzoq: tenglamalar tashqi ko‘rinishdan farq qiladi, lekin chap tomonlarni tenglashtirganda ozod hadlar ham bir xil chiqadi, shuning uchun chiziqlar parallel emas, ustma-ust tushadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} kx + 8y &= 12 \\\\\\\\ 2x + ky &= 6 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nIn the given system of equations, $k$ is a constant. For which value of $k$ does the system have no solution?\",\"option_a\":\"$-4$\",\"option_b\":\"$2$\",\"option_c\":\"$4$\",\"option_d\":\"$16$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"A system of two linear equations has no solution when the lines are parallel and distinct: the coefficients of $x$ and $y$ are proportional, but the constants are not in the same ratio.\\n\\nProportional coefficients: $\\\\frac{k}{2} = \\\\frac{8}{k}$, so $k^2 = 16$ and $k = 4$ or $k = -4$.\\n\\nIf $k = 4$, the equations are $4x + 8y = 12$ and $2x + 4y = 6$. The first is exactly $2$ times the second, so they describe the same line (infinitely many solutions).\\n\\nIf $k = -4$, the equations are $-4x + 8y = 12$ and $2x - 4y = 6$. Multiplying the second by $-2$ gives $-4x + 8y = -12$: the same left side as the first equation but a different constant, so the lines are parallel and the system has no solution.\\n\\nChoice C ($4$) also makes the coefficients proportional, but it makes the constants proportional too, so that system has infinitely many solutions, not zero.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikki chiziqli tenglamadan iborat sistema yechimga ega bo‘lmasligi uchun chiziqlar parallel va ustma-ust tushmaydigan bo‘lishi kerak: $x$ va $y$ koeffitsiyentlari proporsional, ozod hadlar esa shu nisbatda emas.\\n\\nKoeffitsiyentlar proporsional: $\\\\frac{k}{2} = \\\\frac{8}{k}$, demak $k^2 = 16$, ya’ni $k = 4$ yoki $k = -4$.\\n\\n$k = 4$ bo‘lsa, tenglamalar $4x + 8y = 12$ va $2x + 4y = 6$. Birinchisi aynan ikkinchisining $2$ baravari, ya’ni ular bitta chiziq (cheksiz ko‘p yechim).\\n\\n$k = -4$ bo‘lsa, tenglamalar $-4x + 8y = 12$ va $2x - 4y = 6$. Ikkinchisini $-2$ ga ko‘paytirsak, $-4x + 8y = -12$: chap tomoni birinchi tenglama bilan bir xil, ozod hadi esa boshqa. Demak chiziqlar parallel va sistemaning yechimi yo‘q.\\n\\nC variant ($4$) ham koeffitsiyentlarni proporsional qiladi, lekin ozod hadlarni ham proporsional qiladi — bunda sistema yechimsiz emas, cheksiz ko‘p yechimga ega.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A chemist mixes a $12\\\\%$ saline solution with a $30\\\\%$ saline solution to make $45$ liters of a $20\\\\%$ saline solution. How many liters of the $30\\\\%$ solution does the chemist use?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"20\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Let $a$ be the number of liters of the $12\\\\%$ solution and $b$ the number of liters of the $30\\\\%$ solution.\\n\\nTotal volume: $a + b = 45$. Amount of salt: $0.12a + 0.30b = 0.20(45) = 9$.\\n\\nSubstitute $a = 45 - b$: $0.12(45 - b) + 0.30b = 9$, so $5.4 + 0.18b = 9$, $0.18b = 3.6$, and $b = 20$.\\n\\nCheck: $a = 25$, and $0.12(25) + 0.30(20) = 3 + 6 = 9$. A common mistake is entering $25$, which is the amount of the $12\\\\%$ solution.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$a$ — $12\\\\%$ li eritma miqdori (litr), $b$ — $30\\\\%$ li eritma miqdori (litr) bo‘lsin.\\n\\nUmumiy hajm: $a + b = 45$. Tuz miqdori: $0.12a + 0.30b = 0.20(45) = 9$.\\n\\n$a = 45 - b$ ni qo‘yamiz: $0.12(45 - b) + 0.30b = 9$, ya’ni $5.4 + 0.18b = 9$, $0.18b = 3.6$ va $b = 20$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $a = 25$, va $0.12(25) + 0.30(20) = 3 + 6 = 9$. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — $12\\\\%$ li eritma miqdori $25$ ni javob sifatida kiritish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":125,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"When people think of pollinators, they usually picture bees. Yet many crops depend on other animals. In a three-year study of cacao farms, entomologist Priya Nandan found that cacao flowers, which are tiny and grow directly on the tree's trunk, are pollinated almost entirely by small flies called midges. Because these midges breed in rotting leaves and fruit husks, Nandan suggests that farmers leave some of this plant material on the ground rather than clearing it away.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"To explain why bee populations have declined on cacao farms\",\"option_b\":\"To compare several methods of clearing plant material from farms\",\"option_c\":\"To present a finding about which insects pollinate a crop and describe a practical recommendation based on that finding\",\"option_d\":\"To argue that flies are more important pollinators than bees for most crops\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text notes that people usually think of bees as pollinators, reports Nandan's finding that midges pollinate cacao flowers, and ends with her suggestion that farmers leave the rotting plant material in which midges breed. Choice C captures both the finding and the recommendation. Choice A is wrong because the text never discusses a decline in bees. Choice B is wrong because the text does not compare clearing methods; it suggests not clearing some material at all. Choice D is too broad: the text discusses only cacao and says only that “many crops” depend on animals other than bees.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn avval odamlar changlatuvchi deganda odatda asalarini tasavvur qilishini aytadi, so‘ng Nandanning kakao gullarini midge deb ataladigan mayda pashshalar changlatishi haqidagi topilmasini keltiradi va oxirida fermerlarga shu pashshalar ko‘payadigan chirigan o‘simlik qoldiqlarini yerda qoldirishni tavsiya qiladi. C javob topilmani ham, tavsiyani ham qamrab oladi. A noto‘g‘ri: matnda asalarilar kamayib ketgani haqida gap yo‘q. B noto‘g‘ri: matnda tozalash usullari solishtirilmaydi, aksincha, qoldiqlarning bir qismini umuman tozalamaslik taklif qilinadi. D juda keng: matn faqat kakao haqida, boshqa ekinlar haqida esa faqat “many crops” asalarilardan boshqa hayvonlarga ham bog‘liqligi aytiladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is adapted from a short story.\\n\\nGrandfather's workshop smelled of sawdust and lamp oil. His tools hung on the walls in neat rows, and each one was outlined in white chalk so that it could be returned to its exact place. __Even the smallest chisel had its own outline, no wider than a finger.__ In all his visits, Akmal had never once seen his grandfather search for anything; whatever the old man needed was always exactly where he reached for it.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?\",\"option_a\":\"It provides a specific detail that emphasizes how carefully the grandfather has organized his workshop.\",\"option_b\":\"It suggests that the grandfather's tools are too small to be useful.\",\"option_c\":\"It introduces a contrast between the grandfather's habits and Akmal's habits.\",\"option_d\":\"It explains why Akmal rarely visits the workshop.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The sentences around the underlined one describe tools hanging in neat rows, each outlined in chalk, and a grandfather who never has to search for anything. The underlined sentence adds a precise detail (even the smallest chisel has its own outline) that reinforces this picture of careful organization, as choice A says. Choice B is unsupported: the chisel's size shows how thorough the system is, not that the tools are useless. Choice C is wrong because Akmal's own habits are never described. Choice D is wrong because the text refers to Akmal's many visits.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tagiga chizilgan jumla atrofidagi gaplar asboblar qator-qator osilgani, har birining bo‘r bilan chizilgan joyi borligi va bobo hech qachon hech narsa qidirmasligini tasvirlaydi. Tagiga chizilgan jumla bu manzarani kuchaytiruvchi aniq tafsilot qo‘shadi: hatto eng kichik iskananing ham o‘z chizig‘i bor. Demak, to‘g‘ri javob — A. B asossiz: iskananing kichikligi tizim qanchalik puxta ekanini ko‘rsatadi, asboblar yaroqsizligini emas. C noto‘g‘ri, chunki Akmalning o‘z odatlari matnda tasvirlanmagan. D noto‘g‘ri: matnda Akmalning ko‘p marta kelgani aytiladi (“In all his visits”).\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Many people assume that foxes cannot survive in busy, noisy cities. Yet red foxes have settled in a number of large cities. __Researchers in the city of Halbrecht estimated that more than 5,000 foxes live within the city limits, many of them in parks, along railway lines and in private gardens.__ Biologists think foxes do well in cities partly because they eat almost anything, from insects and fruit to food scraps left by people.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?\",\"option_a\":\"It explains why foxes prefer cities to forests.\",\"option_b\":\"It introduces a claim that the rest of the text argues against.\",\"option_c\":\"It describes the method researchers used to count foxes.\",\"option_d\":\"It provides an example supporting the statement that red foxes have settled in large cities.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The sentence before the underlined one states that red foxes “have settled in a number of large cities,” and the underlined sentence gives a specific case (thousands of foxes living in Halbrecht) that supports that statement, as choice D says. Choice A is wrong because the text never compares cities with forests or says that foxes prefer cities. Choice B is wrong because nothing in the text argues against the estimate; the next sentence explains why foxes succeed in cities. Choice C is wrong because the sentence reports an estimate without explaining how it was made.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tagiga chizilgan jumladan oldingi gapda tulkilar “bir qator yirik shaharlarga joylashgani” aytiladi. Tagiga chizilgan jumla esa shu fikrni qo‘llab-quvvatlovchi aniq misol keltiradi: Halbrecht shahrida minglab tulki yashaydi. Shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob — D. A noto‘g‘ri: matnda shahar va o‘rmon solishtirilmaydi, tulkilar shaharni afzal ko‘rishi ham aytilmagan. B noto‘g‘ri: matnda bu hisob-kitobga qarshi fikr yo‘q, keyingi gap tulkilarning shaharda nega yaxshi yashashini tushuntiradi. C noto‘g‘ri: jumlada hisob natijasi beriladi, lekin u qanday usulda olingani tushuntirilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"For much of the twentieth century, art historians described the painter Ines Valdor (1889–1954) as a minor follower of better-known artists. That view rested largely on the small number of her paintings held in museums. In 2019, however, researchers cataloging a private family archive found more than two hundred of her works, including large landscapes built up with layering techniques that the artists she supposedly imitated never attempted. Many scholars now regard Valdor as an innovator in her own right.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"It describes a painter's techniques and then explains why museums refused to display her work.\",\"option_b\":\"It presents a long-held view of a painter and then describes a discovery that has led scholars to revise that view.\",\"option_c\":\"It compares the work of two painters and then argues that one influenced the other.\",\"option_d\":\"It summarizes a disagreement among scholars and then explains why that disagreement cannot be resolved.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text opens with the twentieth-century view of Valdor as a “minor follower,” explains what that view rested on, describes the 2019 discovery of more than two hundred of her works, and ends by noting that many scholars now see her as an innovator. Choice B matches this sequence. Choice A is wrong because the text never says museums refused to display her work; it says only that few of her paintings were held in museums. Choice C is wrong because no second painter is discussed. Choice D is wrong because the text presents a shift in scholarly opinion, not an unresolved disagreement.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn XX asrdagi Valdorni “ikkinchi darajali izdosh” deb hisoblagan qarash bilan boshlanadi, bu qarash nimaga asoslanganini tushuntiradi, 2019-yilda uning ikki yuzdan ortiq asari topilganini tasvirlaydi va ko‘plab olimlar endi uni novator deb bilishini aytib tugaydi. B javob aynan shu ketma-ketlikni ifodalaydi. A noto‘g‘ri: matnda muzeylar uning asarlarini ko‘rsatishdan bosh tortgani aytilmagan, faqat muzeylarda uning rasmlari kam bo‘lgani aytilgan. C noto‘g‘ri: matnda ikkinchi rassom muhokama qilinmaydi. D noto‘g‘ri: matnda hal qilinmagan bahs emas, olimlar fikrining o‘zgarishi tasvirlangan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Chemist Yusuf Karaev studies the bright turquoise glazes on pottery made in a twelfth-century workshop in Central Asia. Earlier researchers assumed that the color required a rare copper ore that had to be imported from distant mines. __Karaev's analysis of the glazes, however, revealed a copper compound that could have been produced from scrap metal sold in local markets.__ He suggests that the workshop's potters may have melted down worn-out copper pots and jugs to make their glazes.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?\",\"option_a\":\"It presents an assumption that the rest of the text supports.\",\"option_b\":\"It describes the method Karaev used to determine the age of the pottery.\",\"option_c\":\"It presents a finding that challenges an earlier assumption and that leads to Karaev's suggestion.\",\"option_d\":\"It explains why imported copper ore was difficult for potters to obtain.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Before the underlined sentence, the text describes the earlier assumption that the glazes required imported ore. The underlined sentence, signaled by “however,” reports Karaev's finding that the copper could have come from local scrap metal, and the final sentence builds on this finding with his suggestion about recycled pots and jugs. Choice C describes both roles. Choice A is wrong because the sentence reports a finding rather than an assumption, and that finding undercuts the earlier view. Choice B is wrong because the analysis concerns the glazes' ingredients, not the pottery's age. Choice D is wrong because the sentence says nothing about difficulties in obtaining imported ore.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tagiga chizilgan jumladan oldin matnda avvalgi taxmin — sir (glazur) uchun chetdan keltirilgan noyob mis rudasi kerak bo‘lgani — tasvirlanadi. Tagiga chizilgan jumla “however” so‘zi bilan Karaevning topilmasini beradi: mis mahalliy bozorlardagi metall parchalaridan olingan bo‘lishi mumkin. Oxirgi jumla esa shu topilmaga tayanib, eski mis idishlar qayta eritilgan bo‘lishi mumkin degan taxminni ilgari suradi. C javob ikkala vazifani ham to‘g‘ri tasvirlaydi. A noto‘g‘ri: jumla taxmin emas, topilma, va u avvalgi qarashga zid. B noto‘g‘ri: tahlil kulolchilik buyumlarining yoshi haqida emas, sirning tarkibi haqida. D noto‘g‘ri: jumlada rudani olib kelish qiyinligi haqida hech narsa aytilmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is from a poem. The speaker describes her father, who worked as a lighthouse keeper.\\n\\nMy father kept the light for forty years,\\nAnd never once, he said, did he grow tired\\nOf climbing all those stairs at dusk. The sea\\nWas all the company he seemed to need.\\nWhen ships passed far out, beyond the reach of voices,\\nHe raised his hand to them as if to friends.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"To describe the dangers that ships faced near the lighthouse\",\"option_b\":\"To explain how a lighthouse keeper operated the light each evening\",\"option_c\":\"To criticize the father for isolating himself from other people\",\"option_d\":\"To portray the father's devotion to his work and the sense of connection he felt with distant ships\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The poem stresses that the father kept the light “for forty years” and never tired of climbing the stairs, which shows his devotion, and it ends with him raising his hand to passing ships “as if to friends,” which shows his sense of connection to them. Choice D captures both ideas. Choice A is wrong because no dangers to ships are described. Choice B is wrong because the poem mentions climbing the stairs but does not explain how the light was operated. Choice C is wrong because the speaker describes her father's solitude without criticizing it; her tone is admiring, not disapproving.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"She’rda ota mayoqni “qirq yil” davomida boshqargani va zinapoyadan chiqishdan hech qachon charchamagani ta’kidlanadi — bu uning ishiga sadoqatini ko‘rsatadi. She’r oxirida u uzoqdan o‘tayotgan kemalarga “do‘stlarga qilgandek” qo‘l ko‘taradi — bu uning kemalar bilan o‘zini yaqin his qilganini bildiradi. D javob ikkala fikrni ham qamrab oladi. A noto‘g‘ri: kemalarga tahdid soladigan xavflar tasvirlanmagan. B noto‘g‘ri: she’rda zinadan chiqish eslatiladi, lekin chiroq qanday yoqilgani tushuntirilmaydi. C noto‘g‘ri: so‘zlovchi otasining yolg‘izligini tanqid qilmaydi; uning ohangi tanqidiy emas, hurmat va hayratga to‘la.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Economists have long observed that when a city adds lanes to a crowded highway, traffic often returns to its earlier level within a few years, because the extra space encourages more people to drive. Urban planner Mirela Costa argues that a similar pattern can work in public transit's favor. __When the city of Dunmere began running buses every ten minutes on a route that had once carried few passengers, ridership on that route tripled within two years, far exceeding planners' forecasts.__ Costa contends that forecasts based on current ridership may therefore consistently underestimate the demand that improved service can create.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?\",\"option_a\":\"It offers an example that supports Costa's view that improving transit service can attract many new riders.\",\"option_b\":\"It presents evidence that challenges the economists' observation about highway traffic.\",\"option_c\":\"It explains why planners' forecasts of highway traffic have often been inaccurate.\",\"option_d\":\"It describes a weakness in Costa's argument that the final sentence attempts to address.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Costa argues that the pattern seen with highways (added capacity drawing more users) can also benefit transit. The underlined sentence describes a case in which more frequent buses led to tripled ridership, beyond what planners predicted, and the final sentence draws a conclusion from that case. The sentence is therefore an example supporting Costa's view, as choice A says. Choice B is wrong because the Dunmere example parallels the highway pattern rather than challenging it. Choice C is wrong because the forecasts mentioned concern bus ridership, not highway traffic. Choice D is wrong because the example strengthens Costa's argument rather than revealing a weakness in it.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Costaning fikricha, avtomagistrallarda kuzatiladigan qonuniyat — imkoniyat kengaytirilsa, foydalanuvchilar ko‘payadi — jamoat transportiga ham foyda keltirishi mumkin. Tagiga chizilgan jumlada avtobuslar tez-tez qatnay boshlagach, yo‘nalishdagi yo‘lovchilar soni rejalashtiruvchilar kutganidan ham ko‘proq, uch baravar oshgani tasvirlanadi. Oxirgi jumla esa shu misoldan xulosa chiqaradi. Demak, bu jumla Costaning fikrini qo‘llab-quvvatlovchi misol — to‘g‘ri javob A. B noto‘g‘ri: Dunmere misoli avtomagistral haqidagi kuzatuvga zid emas, aksincha, unga o‘xshash. C noto‘g‘ri: tilga olingan prognozlar avtomagistral harakati haqida emas, avtobus yo‘lovchilari haqida. D noto‘g‘ri: misol Costaning dalilini zaiflashtirmaydi, aksincha, kuchaytiradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is from a short story.\\n\\nMrs. Halloran had lived on Beech Street for thirty years, and in that time she had formed opinions about every house on it. The Pruitts' hedge was too tall; the Lanes left their porch light burning all night, which was wasteful. When a new family moved into number fourteen, she watched from her window for a full week before deciding that they were, on the whole, acceptable, though she reserved judgment on the dog. __It did not occur to her that the street might have been forming opinions of its own.__\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?\",\"option_a\":\"It reveals that Mrs. Halloran's neighbors strongly dislike her.\",\"option_b\":\"It adds a gently ironic perspective on Mrs. Halloran's habit of judging her neighbors.\",\"option_c\":\"It explains why Mrs. Halloran took a week to form an opinion of the new family.\",\"option_d\":\"It suggests that Mrs. Halloran has begun to regret her opinions about the street.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Most of the text shows Mrs. Halloran confidently judging her neighbors. The underlined sentence turns this around by pointing out something she never considers: her neighbors may be judging her in the same way. This creates mild irony at her expense, as choice B says. Choice A is too extreme: the sentence says only that the street might have opinions of its own, not that the neighbors dislike her. Choice C is wrong because the sentence does not explain her week of watching. Choice D is wrong because the sentence says the idea “did not occur to her,” so she cannot be regretting anything.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnning katta qismi Halloran xonimning qo‘shnilari haqida ishonch bilan hukm chiqarishini ko‘rsatadi. Tagiga chizilgan jumla vaziyatga teskari tomondan qaraydi: u hech o‘ylab ko‘rmagan narsa — qo‘shnilar ham u haqida xuddi shunday fikr yuritayotgan bo‘lishi mumkin. Bu uning ustidan yengil kinoya (ironiya) yaratadi — to‘g‘ri javob B. A haddan tashqari kuchli: jumlada ko‘cha ahlining ham o‘z fikri bo‘lishi mumkinligi aytiladi, qo‘shnilar uni yomon ko‘rishi emas. C noto‘g‘ri: jumla uning bir hafta kuzatganini tushuntirmaydi. D noto‘g‘ri: jumlada bu fikr uning “xayoliga ham kelmagani” aytiladi, demak u hech narsadan afsuslanmayapti.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Deserts are often pictured as places of constant, scorching heat. ______ in the Gobi Desert, which stretches across parts of Mongolia and China, winter temperatures can drop below −40°C, and snow sometimes dusts the dunes.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"Therefore,\",\"option_b\":\"However,\",\"option_c\":\"For example,\",\"option_d\":\"Similarly,\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence states a common image of deserts: places of constant heat. The second sentence describes a desert where winter temperatures fall below −40°C, which goes against that image. “However” signals this contrast, so choice B is correct.\\n\\n“Therefore” wrongly presents the cold winters as a result of the common image. “For example” would require the Gobi to illustrate constant heat, which it does not. “Similarly” signals a matching idea, but the two sentences conflict.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gap cho‘llar haqidagi keng tarqalgan tasavvurni beradi: doimiy issiq joylar. Ikkinchi gap esa qishda harorat −40°C dan ham pastga tushadigan cho‘lni tasvirlaydi — bu o‘sha tasavvurga zid. “However” aynan shu zidlikni bildiradi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\n“Therefore” sovuq qishni keng tarqalgan tasavvurning natijasi qilib ko‘rsatadi — bu mantiqsiz. “For example” Gobi doimiy issiqlikka misol bo‘lishini talab qiladi, lekin unday emas. “Similarly” o‘xshash fikrni bildiradi, ikki gap esa bir-biriga zid.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Uzbekistan is one of only two doubly landlocked countries in the world: it does not border an ocean, and none of its neighbors does either. ______ goods shipped to Uzbekistan by sea must cross at least two international borders over land before they arrive.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"As a result,\",\"option_b\":\"In contrast,\",\"option_c\":\"For instance,\",\"option_d\":\"Nevertheless,\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence explains that Uzbekistan is doubly landlocked: neither it nor any of its neighbors borders an ocean. The second sentence describes a consequence of that fact: goods arriving by sea must cross at least two borders by land. “As a result” signals cause and effect, so choice A is correct.\\n\\n“In contrast” and “Nevertheless” signal a conflict, but the second sentence follows directly from the first. “For instance” would present the second sentence as an example of being landlocked, but it actually describes an effect of it.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gap O‘zbekiston ikki karra dengizga chiqishi yo‘q davlat ekanini tushuntiradi: na o‘zi, na qo‘shnilari okeanga chegaradosh. Ikkinchi gap shu holatning oqibatini tasvirlaydi: dengiz orqali keladigan yuklar quruqlikda kamida ikki chegarani kesib o‘tishi kerak. “As a result” sabab-natija bog‘lanishini bildiradi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\n“In contrast” va “Nevertheless” zidlikni bildiradi, lekin ikkinchi gap birinchisidan bevosita kelib chiqadi. “For instance” ikkinchi gapni misol sifatida taqdim etadi, holbuki u misol emas, oqibat.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"English has borrowed many words from other languages, often through long chains of contact between cultures. ______ the word “kiosk” entered English from French, which had borrowed it from Turkish, and the word “shampoo” comes from Hindi.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"Instead,\",\"option_b\":\"However,\",\"option_c\":\"For example,\",\"option_d\":\"Consequently,\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence makes a general claim: English has borrowed many words from other languages, often through chains of contact. The second sentence gives specific cases of this—“kiosk” (from Turkish through French) and “shampoo” (from Hindi). “For example” introduces such illustrations, so choice C is correct.\\n\\n“Instead” and “However” signal a contrast or a replacement, but the second sentence supports the first. “Consequently” would make the borrowed words a result of the general claim, rather than examples of it.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gap umumiy fikrni bildiradi: ingliz tili boshqa tillardan ko‘plab so‘zlarni, ko‘pincha madaniyatlar orasidagi uzun aloqalar zanjiri orqali o‘zlashtirgan. Ikkinchi gap buning aniq misollarini keltiradi — “kiosk” (turk tilidan fransuz tili orqali) va “shampoo” (hind tilidan). “For example” aynan misol keltirishni bildiradi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\n“Instead” va “However” zidlik yoki almashtirishni bildiradi, ikkinchi gap esa birinchisini qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi. “Consequently” o‘zlashma so‘zlarni umumiy fikrning misoli emas, natijasi qilib ko‘rsatadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Builders looking for sustainable materials are increasingly turning to bamboo. The plant grows so quickly that a harvested grove can regrow in just a few years, unlike a forest of slow-growing hardwood trees. ______ bamboo is remarkably strong for its weight, so it can be used for scaffolding, floors, and even the frames of small houses.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"Instead,\",\"option_b\":\"Nevertheless,\",\"option_c\":\"Thus,\",\"option_d\":\"Additionally,\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text explains why builders are turning to bamboo. The second sentence gives one reason (it regrows quickly), and the third sentence gives a second, separate reason (it is strong for its weight). “Additionally” signals that another supporting point is being added, so choice D is correct.\\n\\n“Instead” suggests that the strength replaces the fast growth as a reason, which is not what the text says. “Nevertheless” signals a contrast, but both sentences favor bamboo. “Thus” presents the strength as a result of the fast growth, but the text does not claim that one causes the other.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn quruvchilar nima uchun bambukka murojaat qilayotganini tushuntiradi. Ikkinchi gap bitta sababni (u tez qayta o‘sadi), uchinchi gap esa ikkinchi, alohida sababni (og‘irligiga nisbatan juda mustahkam) keltiradi. “Additionally” yana bir dalil qo‘shilayotganini bildiradi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\n“Instead” mustahkamlik tez o‘sish o‘rnini egallaydigan sabab degan ma’noni beradi — matnda bunday deyilmagan. “Nevertheless” zidlikni bildiradi, lekin ikkala gap ham bambuk foydasiga. “Thus” mustahkamlikni tez o‘sishning natijasi qilib ko‘rsatadi, matn esa birini ikkinchisining sababi deb da’vo qilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"When the city's new public library was unveiled, several architecture critics dismissed its façade of irregular, patterned brickwork as distracting and out of place. ______ the building quickly became one of the most photographed landmarks in the city, and residents now print its image on postcards and souvenirs.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"For example,\",\"option_b\":\"Accordingly,\",\"option_c\":\"Even so,\",\"option_d\":\"Similarly,\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence reports a negative reaction: critics called the library's façade distracting and out of place. The second sentence describes a positive outcome that happened despite that criticism: the building became a beloved landmark. “Even so” signals that something is true in spite of what was just said, so choice C is correct.\\n\\n“For example” would make the building's popularity an example of the criticism. “Accordingly” would make the popularity a logical result of the criticism. “Similarly” signals that the second idea matches the first, but the two ideas point in opposite directions.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gap salbiy munosabatni bayon qiladi: tanqidchilar kutubxona fasadini chalg‘ituvchi va o‘rinsiz deb atashgan. Ikkinchi gap esa shu tanqidga qaramay yuz bergan ijobiy natijani tasvirlaydi: bino sevimli diqqatga sazovor joyga aylangan. “Even so” aytilgan narsaga qaramay boshqa bir narsa to‘g‘ri ekanini bildiradi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\n“For example” binoning mashhurligini tanqidning misoli qilib qo‘yadi. “Accordingly” mashhurlikni tanqidning mantiqiy natijasi qilib ko‘rsatadi. “Similarly” ikkinchi fikr birinchisiga o‘xshash ekanini bildiradi, lekin bu ikki fikr qarama-qarshi yo‘nalishda.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Producing silk thread by hand is a careful, step-by-step process. Workers first soak silkworm cocoons in hot water to soften the sticky protein that holds the fine fibers together. ______ they unwind the long filaments from several cocoons at once and twist them together into a single, stronger thread.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"In contrast,\",\"option_b\":\"For instance,\",\"option_c\":\"Nonetheless,\",\"option_d\":\"Next,\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text describes a process in order. The second sentence gives the first step (“Workers first soak silkworm cocoons in hot water…”), and the third sentence gives the step that follows it (unwinding and twisting the filaments). “Next” signals the following step in a sequence, so choice D is correct.\\n\\n“In contrast” and “Nonetheless” signal a conflict between the two steps, but there is none. “For instance” would present unwinding the filaments as an example of soaking the cocoons, which it is not.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn jarayonni ketma-ket tasvirlaydi. Ikkinchi gap birinchi bosqichni beradi (“Workers first soak silkworm cocoons in hot water…”), uchinchi gap esa undan keyingi bosqichni (iplarni yechib, eshish). “Next” ketma-ketlikdagi navbatdagi bosqichni bildiradi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\n“In contrast” va “Nonetheless” ikki bosqich orasida zidlik borligini bildiradi, lekin zidlik yo‘q. “For instance” iplarni yechishni pillani ivitishning misoli qilib ko‘rsatadi — bu noto‘g‘ri.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Astronomer Kamola Yusupova's computer models suggest that a distant planet's thick atmosphere traps enough heat to keep water on its surface in liquid form. ______ the models rely on estimates of the atmosphere's composition that have not yet been confirmed by direct observation, so Yusupova describes her conclusion as tentative.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"Thus,\",\"option_b\":\"Moreover,\",\"option_c\":\"That said,\",\"option_d\":\"For instance,\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence presents a conclusion suggested by Yusupova's models. The second sentence points out a limitation of those models—they depend on unconfirmed estimates—which is why she calls the conclusion tentative. “That said” introduces a qualification or caution about a preceding claim, so choice C is correct.\\n\\n“Thus” wrongly presents the models' limitation as a result of their conclusion. “Moreover” signals added support, but the second sentence weakens the claim rather than strengthening it. “For instance” signals an example, but the limitation is not an example of the planet trapping heat.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gap Yusupova modellari ko‘rsatgan xulosani keltiradi. Ikkinchi gap esa shu modellarning kamchiligini — ular tasdiqlanmagan taxminlarga tayanishini — ko‘rsatadi; shuning uchun olima xulosani dastlabki deb ataydi. “That said” oldingi fikrga cheklov yoki ehtiyot izohini kiritadi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\n“Thus” modellarning kamchiligini ularning xulosasi natijasi qilib ko‘rsatadi — bu mantiqsiz. “Moreover” qo‘shimcha dalil qo‘shilayotganini bildiradi, ikkinchi gap esa fikrni kuchaytirmaydi, balki zaiflashtiradi. “For instance” misol keltirishni bildiradi, lekin bu kamchilik sayyora issiqlikni ushlab qolishiga misol emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Researchers who monitored a river fed by mountain snowmelt found that its water quality changed sharply over the course of a single year. ______ the concentration of dissolved salts in late summer was nearly three times higher than it was in spring, when large amounts of fresh meltwater diluted the river.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"In contrast,\",\"option_b\":\"Specifically,\",\"option_c\":\"Regardless,\",\"option_d\":\"Similarly,\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence makes a general claim: the river's water quality changed sharply over the year. The second sentence gives the precise details of that change—salt levels in late summer were nearly three times higher than in spring. “Specifically” introduces a more exact statement of a preceding general claim, so choice B is correct.\\n\\n“In contrast” is tempting because the second sentence compares late summer with spring, but that comparison is the very change described in the first sentence, not something that contrasts with it. “Regardless” suggests that the second sentence holds true despite the first. “Similarly” suggests a separate but parallel observation rather than a detailed explanation of the same one.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gap umumiy fikrni bildiradi: daryo suvining sifati yil davomida keskin o‘zgargan. Ikkinchi gap shu o‘zgarishning aniq tafsilotlarini beradi — yozning oxirida tuz miqdori bahordagidan qariyb uch baravar yuqori bo‘lgan. “Specifically” oldingi umumiy fikrni aniqroq ifodalashni bildiradi, shuning uchun to‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\n“In contrast” jozibali, chunki ikkinchi gap yoz oxirini bahor bilan solishtiradi, lekin bu solishtirish birinchi gapda aytilgan o‘zgarishning o‘zi, unga zid narsa emas. “Regardless” ikkinchi gap birinchisiga qaramay to‘g‘ri ekanini bildiradi. “Similarly” esa bir xil kuzatuvning batafsil izohini emas, alohida, o‘xshash kuzatuvni bildiradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A biologist recorded the number of hours of direct sunlight per day, $x$, that each of 15 tomato plants received and the amount each plant grew, $y$, in centimeters, during one month. The line of best fit for the data is $y = 1.8x + 3.4$. According to the line of best fit, what is the predicted growth, in centimeters, of a plant that receives 6 hours of direct sunlight per day?\",\"option_a\":\"$10.8$\",\"option_b\":\"$14.2$\",\"option_c\":\"$22.2$\",\"option_d\":\"$31.2$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $x = 6$ into the equation: $y = 1.8(6) + 3.4 = 10.8 + 3.4 = 14.2$ centimeters. Choice A forgets to add 3.4, choice C swaps the roles of 1.8 and 3.4 ($3.4 \\\\times 6 + 1.8$), and choice D multiplies both numbers by 6.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tenglamaga $x = 6$ ni qo‘yamiz: $y = 1.8(6) + 3.4 = 10.8 + 3.4 = 14.2$ santimetr. A javobda 3.4 qo‘shilmagan, C javobda 1.8 va 3.4 ning o‘rni almashtirilgan ($3.4 \\\\times 6 + 1.8$), D javobda esa ikkala son ham 6 ga ko‘paytirilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"For 25 apartments in a city, a scatterplot shows each apartment's distance from the city center, $x$, in kilometers, and its monthly rent, $y$, in dollars. The line of best fit for the data is $y = -45x + 980$. Which of the following is the best interpretation of 980 in this context?\",\"option_a\":\"For each additional kilometer from the city center, the predicted monthly rent decreases by \\\\$980.\",\"option_b\":\"The greatest monthly rent among the 25 apartments is \\\\$980.\",\"option_c\":\"Every apartment located at the city center has a monthly rent of exactly \\\\$980.\",\"option_d\":\"The predicted monthly rent of an apartment located at the city center is \\\\$980.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"In $y = -45x + 980$, the constant 980 is the value of $y$ when $x = 0$. Here $x = 0$ means a distance of 0 kilometers from the city center, so 980 is the predicted monthly rent, in dollars, of an apartment at the city center. Choice A describes the slope, but the slope is $-45$, not 980. Choice C is too strong: a line of best fit gives **predicted** values, and actual rents vary around the line. Nothing in the equation identifies the greatest rent in the data (choice B).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y = -45x + 980$ tenglamada 980 — $x = 0$ bo‘lgandagi $y$ qiymati. $x = 0$ — shahar markazidan 0 kilometr masofa, demak 980 — shahar markazidagi kvartiraning bashorat qilingan oylik ijara haqi (dollarda). A javob qiyalikni ta’riflaydi, lekin qiyalik 980 emas, $-45$. C javob haddan tashqari qat’iy: eng mos chiziq **bashorat qilingan** qiymatlarni beradi, haqiqiy ijara haqlari esa chiziq atrofida tarqoq bo‘ladi. Tenglama ma’lumotlardagi eng katta ijara haqini ko‘rsatmaydi (B javob).\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A sports club recorded its number of members each year since 2010. The line of best fit for the data is $y = 12x + 40$, where $y$ is the predicted number of members and $x$ is the number of years since 2010. According to the line of best fit, what is the predicted number of members in 2025?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"220\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The year 2025 is $2025 - 2010 = 15$ years after 2010, so substitute $x = 15$: $y = 12(15) + 40 = 180 + 40 = 220$. Substituting $x = 2025$ is the trap: $x$ counts the years **since** 2010, not the calendar year.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"2025 yil — 2010 yildan $2025 - 2010 = 15$ yil keyin, shuning uchun $x = 15$ ni qo‘yamiz: $y = 12(15) + 40 = 180 + 40 = 220$. Tuzoq — $x = 2025$ ni qo‘yish: $x$ kalendar yilni emas, 2010 yildan **beri** o‘tgan yillar sonini bildiradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following equations best models the data?\",\"passage\":\"A biologist counted the bacteria in a sample at the start of an experiment and then once every hour. The results are shown in the table, where $t$ is the number of hours since the start of the experiment and $B$ is the number of bacteria.\\n\\n| $t$ (hours) | $B$ (bacteria) |\\n| ---: | ---: |\\n| 0 | 500 |\\n| 1 | 600 |\\n| 2 | 720 |\\n| 3 | 864 |\",\"option_a\":\"$B = 500 + 100t$\",\"option_b\":\"$B = 500(0.2)^t$\",\"option_c\":\"$B = 600(1.2)^t$\",\"option_d\":\"$B = 500(1.2)^t$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The differences between consecutive counts are 100, 120 and 144, so the data are not linear. The ratios are equal: $\\\\frac{600}{500} = \\\\frac{720}{600} = \\\\frac{864}{720} = 1.2$, so the count is multiplied by 1.2 each hour. This is an exponential model, $B = 500(1.2)^t$, where 500 is the count at $t = 0$. Choice A fits only the first hour (it predicts 700, not 720, at $t = 2$). Choice B uses the growth rate 0.2 as the base, which would make the count shrink. Choice C uses the count at $t = 1$ as the initial value, so it predicts 600 at $t = 0$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ketma-ket sonlar orasidagi farqlar 100, 120 va 144 — bir xil emas, demak ma’lumotlar chiziqli emas. Nisbatlar esa teng: $\\\\frac{600}{500} = \\\\frac{720}{600} = \\\\frac{864}{720} = 1.2$, ya’ni bakteriyalar soni har soatda 1.2 ga ko‘payadi. Bu eksponensial model: $B = 500(1.2)^t$, bunda 500 — $t = 0$ dagi son. A javob faqat birinchi soatga mos keladi ($t = 2$ da 720 emas, 700 ni beradi). B javob o‘sish sur’ati 0.2 ni asos qilib olgan — bunda son kamayib borardi. C javob boshlang‘ich qiymat sifatida $t = 1$ dagi sonni olgan, shuning uchun $t = 0$ da 600 ni beradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A scatterplot shows the age $x$, in weeks, and the height $y$, in centimeters, of 20 sunflower plants. The line of best fit for the data passes through the points $(4, 13.5)$ and $(12, 31.5)$. According to the line of best fit, by how many centimeters does the predicted height of a sunflower plant increase each week?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"2.25\",\"9/4\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The predicted increase per week is the slope of the line: $\\\\frac{31.5 - 13.5}{12 - 4} = \\\\frac{18}{8} = 2.25$ centimeters per week. A common error is to divide in the wrong order, $\\\\frac{8}{18} \\\\approx 0.44$, which would be weeks per centimeter. Enter 2.25 or 9/4.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Haftalik bashorat qilingan o‘sish — chiziqning qiyaligi: $\\\\frac{31.5 - 13.5}{12 - 4} = \\\\frac{18}{8} = 2.25$ santimetr/hafta. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — teskari bo‘lish: $\\\\frac{8}{18} \\\\approx 0.44$; bu bir santimetrga to‘g‘ri keladigan haftalar soni bo‘lardi. Javob maydoniga 2.25 yoki 9/4 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"On each of 30 days, a city's bike-share program recorded the high temperature $x$, in degrees Celsius, and the number of bike rentals $y$. The line of best fit for the data is $y = 42x + 150$. According to the line of best fit, at what high temperature, in degrees Celsius, would the predicted number of rentals be 1,200?\",\"option_a\":\"$25$\",\"option_b\":\"$28.6$\",\"option_c\":\"$32.1$\",\"option_d\":\"$50{,}550$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Set $y = 1{,}200$ and solve for $x$: $42x + 150 = 1{,}200$, so $42x = 1{,}050$ and $x = 25$. Choice B ignores the 150 and divides 1,200 by 42. Choice C adds 150 instead of subtracting it. Choice D substitutes 1,200 for $x$, but 1,200 is a number of rentals ($y$), not a temperature.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y = 1{,}200$ deb olib, $x$ ni topamiz: $42x + 150 = 1{,}200$, $42x = 1{,}050$ va $x = 25$. B javob 150 ni hisobga olmay, 1,200 ni 42 ga bo‘lgan. C javob 150 ni ayirish o‘rniga qo‘shgan. D javob 1,200 ni $x$ o‘rniga qo‘ygan, lekin 1,200 — harorat emas, ijaralar soni ($y$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A new social media account was tracked for 20 weeks. A scatterplot of the data shows $t$, the number of weeks since the account was created, and $f$, the number of followers. An exponential curve of best fit for the data is $f = 240(1.15)^t$. Which of the following is the best interpretation of 1.15 in this context?\",\"option_a\":\"The predicted number of followers increases by 1.15 each week.\",\"option_b\":\"The predicted number of followers increases by 115% each week.\",\"option_c\":\"The predicted number of followers increases by 15% each week.\",\"option_d\":\"The predicted number of followers increases by 15 each week.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"In an exponential model $f = a(b)^t$, each 1-unit increase in $t$ multiplies the predicted value by $b$. Multiplying by $1.15 = 1 + 0.15$ means the predicted number of followers grows by 15% of its current value each week. Choice B is tempting, but an increase of 115% would multiply the number of followers by 2.15, not 1.15. Choices A and D describe adding the same amount each week, which is linear growth, not exponential growth.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$f = a(b)^t$ ko‘rinishidagi eksponensial modelda $t$ ning har 1 birlikka oshishi bashorat qilingan qiymatni $b$ ga ko‘paytiradi. $1.15 = 1 + 0.15$ ga ko‘paytirish — kuzatuvchilar soni har hafta joriy qiymatning 15% iga oshishini bildiradi. B javob jozibali, lekin 115% ga oshish sonni 1.15 ga emas, 2.15 ga ko‘paytirishni anglatadi. A va D javoblar har hafta bir xil son qo‘shilishini ta’riflaydi — bu eksponensial emas, chiziqli o‘sish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"Two stores opened on the same day. For store A, the line of best fit for monthly sales is $y = 3.2x + 40$, and for store B, it is $y = 2.4x + 64$, where $y$ is the predicted monthly sales, in thousands of dollars, $x$ months after the stores opened. According to these lines of best fit, how many months after opening will the two stores have equal predicted monthly sales?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"30\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Set the two predictions equal: $3.2x + 40 = 2.4x + 64$. Subtracting gives $0.8x = 24$, so $x = 30$. Check: $3.2(30) + 40 = 136$ and $2.4(30) + 64 = 136$ thousand dollars. A common mistake is to enter 136, which is the predicted monthly sales at that time (in thousands of dollars), not the number of months.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikki bashoratni tenglaymiz: $3.2x + 40 = 2.4x + 64$. Bundan $0.8x = 24$ va $x = 30$. Tekshiruv: $3.2(30) + 40 = 136$ va $2.4(30) + 64 = 136$ ming dollar ✓. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — 136 deb yozish: bu oylar soni emas, o‘sha paytdagi bashorat qilingan oylik savdo (ming dollarda).\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"For generations, the village of Sorvon drew all of its water from a single stone well. So when engineer Kamila Usmonova proposed piping water down from a mountain spring, many residents were ______. They worried that the pipes would freeze in winter and leave the village with no water at all. Only after Usmonova showed them a buried pipeline that had worked through three cold winters in a neighboring valley did they agree to the plan.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"enthusiastic\",\"option_b\":\"skeptical\",\"option_c\":\"indifferent\",\"option_d\":\"grateful\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The residents “worried” that the pipes would fail and agreed to the plan only after seeing proof that a similar pipeline worked, so they doubted the plan: they were “skeptical.” “Enthusiastic” and “grateful” describe positive reactions, which contradict the residents' worries. “Indifferent” means not caring, but people who fear losing their water clearly care about the plan.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnga ko‘ra, aholi quvurlar qishda muzlab qolishidan “xavotirlangan” va qo‘shni vodiydagi shunday quvur ishlashini ko‘rgandan keyingina rejaga rozi bo‘lgan. Demak, ular rejaga shubha bilan qaragan — bu “skeptical” so‘zining ma’nosi. “Enthusiastic” (ishtiyoqli) va “grateful” (minnatdor) ijobiy munosabatni bildiradi va aholining xavotiriga zid. “Indifferent” (befarq) ham to‘g‘ri kelmaydi: suvsiz qolishdan qo‘rqqan odamlar bu rejaga befarq emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Before the bridge over the Zarin River was reopened, inspectors spent two weeks examining its steel beams, concrete supports and cables. They found only minor rust on a few railings and concluded that the structure was sound. The bridge reopened to traffic the following Monday.\",\"stem\":\"As used in the text, what does the word “sound” most nearly mean?\",\"option_a\":\"noisy\",\"option_b\":\"reasonable\",\"option_c\":\"deep\",\"option_d\":\"sturdy\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The inspectors examined the bridge's beams, supports and cables, found only minor problems and then reopened it, so “sound” describes a structure that is strong and in good condition: “sturdy.” “Noisy” relates to the noun “sound” (something heard), which does not fit an inspection of steel and concrete. “Reasonable” fits phrases such as “sound advice,” not a bridge. “Deep” fits “sound sleep,” not the condition of a structure.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Inspektorlar ko‘prikning to‘sinlari, tayanchlari va troslarini tekshirib, faqat kichik kamchiliklar topgan, so‘ng ko‘prik qayta ochilgan. Demak, bu yerda “sound” — mustahkam, yaxshi holatdagi degani, ya’ni “sturdy”. “Noisy” (shovqinli) “sound” otining (tovush) ma’nosiga bog‘liq va inshoot holatiga mos emas. “Reasonable” (oqilona) “sound advice” kabi birikmalarda ishlatiladi, ko‘prik haqida emas. “Deep” (chuqur) “sound sleep” (qattiq uyqu) iborasiga mos, inshootga emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Some ponds in dry regions hold water only during the rainy season. Biologist Farida Nasr studies a species of tiny shrimp that lives in these ponds. Its eggs can remain ______ in the dried mud for several years, showing no signs of development until rain refills the pond and triggers them to hatch.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"dormant\",\"option_b\":\"visible\",\"option_c\":\"fragile\",\"option_d\":\"abundant\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The eggs survive for years while “showing no signs of development” and hatch only when water returns, so they are alive but inactive: “dormant.” Nothing in the text says the eggs can be easily seen, so “visible” is unsupported. “Fragile” suggests the eggs are easily damaged, which contradicts their surviving for years in dry mud. “Abundant” describes quantity, but the sentence is about the eggs' inactive state, not how many there are.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tuxumlar yillar davomida “rivojlanish belgisini ko‘rsatmay” saqlanadi va faqat hovuz yana suvga to‘lganda yorilib chiqadi. Demak, ular tirik, lekin faol emas — bu “dormant” (nofaol, “uyqu” holatidagi) so‘zining ma’nosi. Matnda tuxumlarni ko‘rish oson ekani aytilmagan, shuning uchun “visible” (ko‘rinadigan) asossiz. “Fragile” (mo‘rt) tuxumlar oson shikastlanishini bildiradi, bu esa ularning quruq loyda yillab saqlanishiga zid. “Abundant” (mo‘l) miqdorni bildiradi, gap esa tuxumlarning soni haqida emas, holati haqida.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In his review of *The Salt Road*, a new opera by composer Hana Mirzo, critic Lionel Varga offered a qualified endorsement. He praised Mirzo's bold blending of folk melodies with orchestral music, calling several scenes unforgettable, but he questioned whether the opera's three-hour running time truly served its story and suggested that a shorter version might be more powerful.\",\"stem\":\"As used in the text, what does the word “qualified” most nearly mean?\",\"option_a\":\"certified\",\"option_b\":\"skilled\",\"option_c\":\"limited\",\"option_d\":\"eligible\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Varga praises parts of the opera but also doubts that its length serves the story, so his endorsement is not complete; it comes with reservations. In this context, “qualified” means “limited.” “Certified,” “skilled” and “eligible” reflect a different meaning of “qualified” (having the training or the right to do something), which describes people, as in “a qualified teacher,” not a critic's mixed opinion.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Varga operaning ba’zi jihatlarini maqtaydi, lekin uning davomiyligi syujetga xizmat qilishiga shubha bildiradi. Demak, uning ma’qullashi to‘liq emas, shartli — bu kontekstda “qualified” “limited” (cheklangan) degan ma’noni beradi. “Certified” (sertifikatlangan), “skilled” (malakali) va “eligible” (huquqi bor) “qualified” so‘zining boshqa ma’nosiga — biror ishga tayyorgarligi yoki huquqi borligiga bog‘liq. Bu ma’no odamlarga nisbatan ishlatiladi (masalan, “a qualified teacher”), tanqidchining aralash fikriga emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Earlier studies of the wild apple trees of the Tian Shan mountains relied on a few dozen trees sampled from easily reached valleys. Botanist Leyla Sharipova's survey was far more ______: over four summers, her team collected leaf samples from more than 1,200 trees across eleven mountain ranges, including slopes that could be reached only on foot.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"hasty\",\"option_b\":\"speculative\",\"option_c\":\"exhaustive\",\"option_d\":\"narrow\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text contrasts earlier studies, which used “a few dozen trees” from easy-to-reach valleys, with Sharipova's survey of more than 1,200 trees across eleven ranges over four summers. This contrast shows that her survey was far more thorough and complete: “exhaustive.” “Hasty” is contradicted by four summers of work. “Speculative” means based on guesses, but her survey rested on extensive sampling. “Narrow” is the opposite of what the text describes.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda avvalgi tadqiqotlar (oson boriladigan vodiylardan olingan bir necha o‘nta daraxt) Sharipovaning to‘rt yoz davomida o‘n bitta tog‘ tizmasidagi 1,200 dan ortiq daraxtni qamragan tadqiqoti bilan solishtiriladi. Bu qarama-qarshilik uning tadqiqoti ancha puxta va to‘liq bo‘lganini ko‘rsatadi — “exhaustive” (har tomonlama, to‘liq). “Hasty” (shoshma-shosharlik bilan qilingan) to‘rt yillik mehnatga zid. “Speculative” (taxminga asoslangan) ham to‘g‘ri emas: tadqiqot keng ko‘lamli namunalarga tayangan. “Narrow” (tor) esa matndagi tavsifning aksi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"When novelist Aurelia Banks published her first book, several reviewers dismissed it as ______, complaining that its plot simply borrowed familiar scenes from older adventure stories. Later critics, however, noticed that Banks rearranges those familiar scenes in deliberately surprising ways, turning readers' expectations against them.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"derivative\",\"option_b\":\"ambitious\",\"option_c\":\"obscure\",\"option_d\":\"sentimental\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The reviewers complained that the plot “simply borrowed familiar scenes from older adventure stories,” so they saw the book as unoriginal, copied from earlier works: “derivative.” “Ambitious” would be praise, not a reason to dismiss a book for borrowing. “Obscure” means hard to understand or little known, which conflicts with the scenes being “familiar.” “Sentimental” refers to excessive emotion, which the reviewers' complaint does not mention.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Taqrizchilar syujet eski sarguzasht hikoyalaridan “tanish sahnalarni shunchaki olgan”idan shikoyat qilgan. Demak, ular kitobni o‘ziga xos emas, avvalgi asarlardan ko‘chirilgan deb hisoblagan — bu “derivative” (taqlidiy, o‘zgalardan olingan). “Ambitious” (katta maqsadli) maqtov bo‘lardi, kitobni rad etish sababi emas. “Obscure” (tushunarsiz yoki kam ma’lum) sahnalarning “tanish” ekaniga zid. “Sentimental” (haddan tashqari hissiy) haqida esa taqrizchilarning shikoyatida hech narsa aytilmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Economist Dariga Seitova acknowledges that a new irrigation subsidy has raised wheat yields across the province. But she argues that enthusiasm for the program should be tempered by evidence that it has also encouraged farmers to plant water-hungry crops in districts where rivers are already shrinking. A policy that boosts harvests today, she warns, may leave those districts with less water for farming in the future.\",\"stem\":\"As used in the text, what does the word “tempered” most nearly mean?\",\"option_a\":\"hardened\",\"option_b\":\"moderated\",\"option_c\":\"concealed\",\"option_d\":\"replaced\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Seitova accepts that the subsidy has real benefits but points to a serious drawback, so she believes enthusiasm for the program should be reduced or balanced, not abandoned: “moderated.” “Hardened” reflects the sense of tempering metal, which makes it tougher; Seitova wants enthusiasm toned down, not strengthened. “Concealed” suggests hiding enthusiasm, which is not her point. “Replaced” is too extreme: she acknowledges the higher yields and does not call for enthusiasm to be swapped for something else entirely.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Seitova subsidiyaning haqiqiy foydasini tan oladi, lekin jiddiy kamchilikni ham ko‘rsatadi. Demak, uning fikricha, dasturga bo‘lgan ishtiyoqdan voz kechish emas, uni jilovlash, muvozanatga keltirish kerak — “moderated” (yumshatilgan, me’yorga keltirilgan). “Hardened” (toblangan, qattiqlashtirilgan) metallni toblash ma’nosiga bog‘liq — bu metallni mustahkamroq qiladi; Seitova esa ishtiyoqni kuchaytirishni emas, pasaytirishni istaydi. “Concealed” (yashirilgan) ham uning fikri emas. “Replaced” (almashtirilgan) esa haddan tashqari kuchli: u hosildorlik oshganini tan oladi va ishtiyoqni butunlay boshqa narsa bilan almashtirishni talab qilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Linguist Omar Petrosyan once believed that the whistled speech used by shepherds in the Vardan highlands was a simple code that could express only a few fixed messages, such as warnings and calls to gather the flocks. After recording hundreds of whistled conversations, however, he concluded that his earlier view had ______ the system: the shepherds use it to discuss prices, arrange visits and even tell jokes, expressing almost anything they could say in their spoken language.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"romanticized\",\"option_b\":\"corroborated\",\"option_c\":\"foreshadowed\",\"option_d\":\"underestimated\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Petrosyan first thought the whistled speech could express “only a few fixed messages,” but his recordings showed that it can express “almost anything.” His earlier view therefore judged the system to be far less capable than it is: it “underestimated” the system. “Romanticized” means presenting something in an idealized way, but his earlier view made the system seem simpler, not more appealing. “Corroborated” (confirmed) is the opposite of what happened, since the new evidence contradicted his view. “Foreshadowed” means hinted at something to come, which does not describe a mistaken belief.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Petrosyan avval hushtak tilida “faqat bir nechta tayyor xabar”ni ifodalash mumkin deb o‘ylagan, lekin yozuvlar unda “deyarli hamma narsani” aytish mumkinligini ko‘rsatgan. Demak, uning avvalgi qarashi bu tizimni haqiqatdagidan ancha zaif deb baholagan — ya’ni uni “underestimated” (yetarlicha baholamagan, kamsitib baholagan). “Romanticized” (ideallashtirilgan) to‘g‘ri emas: avvalgi qarash tizimni jozibali emas, oddiyroq qilib ko‘rsatgan. “Corroborated” (tasdiqlangan) yuz bergan voqeaning aksi, chunki yangi dalillar uning qarashini rad etgan. “Foreshadowed” (oldindan ishora qilgan) esa noto‘g‘ri fikrni tasvirlamaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v1\"]}]"
